First Steps - JDK,"Find Official JDK","Go to the official Oracle Java or OpenJDK website and find the download page for the latest LTS (Long-Term Support) version of the JDK."
First Steps - JDK,"Verify JDK Installation","Open a command prompt or terminal and run the command 'java -version'. Note down the version reported."
First Steps - JDK,"Verify Compiler Installation","In the same terminal, run 'javac -version'. If this command works, your compiler is correctly installed and in your system's PATH."
First Steps - JDK,"Locate JAVA_HOME","Find the directory where the JDK was installed on your computer. This path is your JAVA_HOME."
First Steps - JDK,"Understand The PATH","Explain in a comment what the system's PATH environment variable is and why the JDK's 'bin' directory needs to be in it."
First Steps - JDK,"JDK vs JRE","Write a short paragraph explaining the difference between the Java Development Kit (JDK) and the Java Runtime Environment (JRE)."
First Steps - JDK,"List Bin Contents","Navigate to the 'bin' directory inside your JDK installation and list its contents. Identify 'java.exe' and 'javac.exe' (or 'java' and 'javac')."
First Steps - First Program,Hello World,"Write a complete Java program in a file named `Hello.java` that prints the exact text ""Hello, World!"" to the console."
First Steps - First Program,Compile and Run,"Using the command line (like Terminal or Command Prompt), compile your `Hello.java` file using `javac` and run the resulting `.class` file using `java`."
First Steps - First Program,Print Your Name,"Modify your program to print your full name instead of ""Hello, World!""."
First Steps - Syntax,Anatomy of a Class,"Create a file `Anatomy.java` with an empty public class named `Anatomy`. Identify the class declaration line."
First Steps - Syntax,Anatomy of the `main` Method,"Add the `main` method to your `Anatomy` class. Write down its exact signature: `public static void main(String[] args)`."
First Steps - Syntax,Statements and Semicolons,"Inside the `main` method, write a statement to print a message. Identify the semicolon that terminates the statement."
First Steps - Syntax,Curly Braces,"In your program, identify the curly braces `{}` that define the body of the class and the body of the `main` method."
First Steps - Comments,Single-Line Comment,"Write a program and add a single-line comment (`//`) above the `main` method explaining the program's purpose."
First Steps - Comments,Multi-Line Comment,"Use a multi-line comment (`/* ... */`) to write a three-line story inside your Java code."
First Steps - Output,Using `System.out.println`,"Write a program that uses three separate `System.out.println()` statements to print three different facts about yourself."
First Steps - Output,Using `System.out.print`,"Use two `System.out.print()` statements to print ""Java"" and ""is fun"" on the same line, separated by a space."
First Steps - Variables,Declare an Integer (`int`),"Declare an integer variable named `numberOfStudents` and assign it a value of 30."
First Steps - Variables,Declare a Double,"Declare a variable named `priceOfCoffee` to hold a decimal value and assign it a value like 2.75."
First Steps - Variables,Declare a String,"Declare a String variable named `favoriteBook` and assign it the title of a book."
First Steps - Variables,Declare a Character (`char`),"Declare a character variable named `middleInitial` and assign it your middle initial."
First Steps - Variables,Declare a Boolean,"Declare a boolean variable named `isRaining` and assign it the value `false`."
First Steps - Variables,Printing Variables,"Write a program that declares an `int` variable, assigns it a value, and then prints the variable's value to the console."
First Steps - Variables,Concatenating a String and a Variable,"Print a sentence that combines a string literal with a variable, like `""My age is: "" + age`."
First Steps - Operators,Addition,"Create two `int` variables, add them together, and store the result in a third variable. Print the result."
First Steps - Operators,Subtraction,"Create two `double` variables, subtract one from the other, and print the result."
First Steps - Operators,Multiplication,"Calculate the area of a rectangle by multiplying its integer `length` and `width`. Print the result."
First Steps - Operators,Integer Division,"Divide the integer 17 by 5 and print the result. Observe that the decimal part is cut off."
First Steps - Operators,Floating-Point Division,"Divide 17.0 by 5.0 and print the result to see the correct decimal value."
First Steps - Operators,Modulo (Remainder),"Calculate the remainder of 20 divided by 3 using the `%` operator and print it."
First Steps - Variables,Variable Reassignment,"Declare an integer variable `x`, assign it the value 10, print it, then assign it the value 20, and print it again."
First Steps - Input,Creating a `Scanner`,"Write the code to create a `Scanner` object to read input from the keyboard (`System.in`)."
First Steps - Input,Reading an Integer,"Use your `Scanner` object to ask the user for their age and read it into an `int` variable."
First Steps - Input,Reading a String,"Use the `Scanner`'s `nextLine()` method to read the user's favorite color into a String variable."
First Steps - Input,Reading a Double,"Use the `Scanner`'s `nextDouble()` method to read the price of an item from the user."
First Steps - Type Casting,Explicit Casting (double to int),"Create a `double` variable with a value like 8.99. Cast it to an `int` and print the result to see truncation."
First Steps - Type Casting,Implicit Casting (int to double),"Assign an `int` variable to a `double` variable and print it. Notice that the conversion is automatic."
First Steps - Math Class,The `Math.PI` Constant,"Calculate the circumference of a circle (2 * pi * radius) using the `Math.PI` constant."
First Steps - Math Class,Square Root,"Use `Math.sqrt()` to find the square root of 144 and print it."
First Steps - Math Class,Absolute Value,"Use `Math.abs()` to find the absolute value of -15 and print it."
First Steps - Math Class,Rounding,"Use `Math.round()` to round the number 4.6 to the nearest whole number."
First Steps - Math.random,Basic Random Number,"Use `Math.random()` to generate and print a random decimal number between 0.0 and 1.0."
First Steps - Math.random,Simulate a Coin Flip,"Use `Math.random()` with an `if` statement to print ""Heads"" or ""Tails""."
First Steps - Control Flow,Simple `if` Statement,"Write a program that prints ""It's hot outside"" if a temperature variable is greater than 85."
First Steps - Control Flow,`if-else` Statement,"Write a program that checks if a grade is 60 or higher and prints ""Pass"" or ""Fail"" accordingly."
First Steps - Control Flow,`if-else if-else` Chain,"Check if a number is positive, negative, or zero, and print the correct message."
First Steps - Operators,Equality (`==`),"Use an `if` statement with the `==` operator to check if a variable is equal to 10."
First Steps - Operators,Inequality (`!=`),"Use an `if` statement with the `!=` operator to check if a variable is not equal to 0."
First Steps - Operators,Greater Than (`>`),"Check if an `age` variable is greater than 18."
First Steps - Operators,Less Than or Equal To (`<=`),"Check if a `quantity` variable is less than or equal to 100."
First Steps - Strings,String `length()`,"Find and print the number of characters in the string ""Java Programming""."
First Steps - Strings,String `toUpperCase()`,"Convert your name to all uppercase letters and print it."
First Steps - Strings,String `toLowerCase()`,"Convert the string ""HELLO"" to all lowercase letters and print it."
First Steps - Strings,String `charAt()`,"Print the character at index 1 of the string ""Computer""."
First Steps - First Project,Simple Calculator,"Create a program that asks the user for two numbers, then asks them to choose an operation (add, subtract). Perform the calculation and print the result."
First Steps - First Project,Greeting Generator,"Ask the user for their name and the current hour (0-23). Print ""Good Morning,"" ""Good Afternoon,"" or ""Good Evening"" with their name based on the hour."
First Steps - First Project,Tip Calculator,"Ask the user for a restaurant bill total. Calculate and print a 15% tip and the final total."
First Steps - First Project,Simple Story,"Ask the user for a name, a place, and an object. Use their answers to print a short, one-sentence story."
"Editors & First Program","WriteHelloWorld","Using a plain text editor (like Notepad, VS Code, Sublime Text), write a simple 'HelloWorld.java' program."
"Editors & First Program","CompileFromCLI","Open a terminal in the directory where you saved 'HelloWorld.java' and compile it using the command 'javac HelloWorld.java'."
"Editors & First Program","ObserveTheBytecode","After compiling, list the files in the directory. You should see a new 'HelloWorld.class' file. What is this file?"
"Editors & First Program","RunFromCLI","In the same terminal, run your compiled program using the command 'java HelloWorld'."
"Editors & First Program","ExplainMainMethod","In a comment in your code, explain the meaning of each part of 'public static void main(String[] args)'."
"Editors & First Program","javacVsjava","Write a short explanation of the difference between the 'javac' command and the 'java' command."
"Editors & First Program","IDEvsTextEditor","Discuss the advantages of using an IDE (like IntelliJ, Eclipse, VS Code with extensions) over a plain text editor for Java development."
"Editors & First Program","ChangeTheMessage","Modify your 'HelloWorld.java' file to print a different message. Recompile and run it to see the change."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","CreateCompileError","Intentionally remove the semicolon at the end of your 'System.out.println' statement. Try to compile and observe the error message."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","ReadTheCompileError","Read the error message from the previous exercise. Identify the file name, line number, and error description."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","FixAndRecompile","Fix the compile-time error and successfully recompile your program."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","CreateRuntimeError","Write a program that attempts to divide an integer by zero. Compile it (it should compile) and then run it."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","ReadTheStackTrace","Observe the 'ArithmeticException' and the stack trace from the previous exercise. Identify the exception type and the line number where it occurred."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","FixAndRerun","Fix the division-by-zero error, then recompile and rerun the program to ensure it works correctly."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","DebugWithPrint","Write a 'for' loop that counts from 0 to 5. Inside the loop, use 'System.out.println()' to print the value of the counter variable in each iteration."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","FindLogicalError","Write a program that should print numbers 1 through 10, but make a logical error so it only prints 1 through 9. Use print statements to debug."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","MentalWalkthrough","Before fixing the previous exercise, do a 'mental walkthrough' or 'desk check' of your loop to predict its behavior step-by-step."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","MultiFileCompile","Create two .java files, where one class uses the other. Compile both of them from the command line in a single 'javac' command."
"Code/Test/Debug Cycle","RunningWithDependencies","Run the main class from the previous exercise. Confirm that the Java runtime can find the necessary dependent '.class' file."
System.out.println,Print a Simple String,"Write a program that prints the sentence ""Java is fun!"" to the console."
System.out.println,Print a Number,"Use `println` to print an integer, like 42, to the console."
System.out.println,Print a Decimal,"Use `println` to print a floating-point number, like 3.14159."
System.out.println,Print a Boolean,"Write a program that prints the result of a boolean expression, such as `true` or `false`."
System.out.println,Print a Blank Line,"Call `System.out.println()` with no arguments to print a blank line."
System.out.println,Print Multiple Lines,"Use three separate `println` statements to print your name, city, and country on three different lines."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Addition,"Directly print the result of an addition operation, like `System.out.println(10 + 5);`."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Subtraction,"Directly print the result of a subtraction operation inside a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Multiplication,"Directly print the result of multiplying two numbers using a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Print the Result of Division,"Print the result of dividing two integers, like `15 / 4`, and observe the integer division result."
System.out.println,Print a String Variable,"Declare a String variable, assign it a value, and then print the variable."
System.out.println,Print an Integer Variable,"Declare an integer variable, assign it a value, and print the variable to the console."
System.out.println,Concatenate a String and a Number,"Combine a string literal with a number inside a `println` statement, like `""Age: "" + 25`."
System.out.println,Concatenate Two String Variables,"Declare two String variables (e.g. firstName, lastName) and print them together with a space in between."
System.out.println,Print with Parentheses for Order,"Print the result of a mixed arithmetic operation, using parentheses to control the order, e.g. `""Result: "" + (5 + 10)`."
System.out.println,Print a Character,"Declare a `char` variable and use `println` to print it to the console."
System.out.println,Print with Newline Escape Character,"Use a single `println` statement with the `\n` character to print two lines of text."
System.out.println,Print with Tab Escape Character,"Use `println` with the `\t` character to print two words separated by a tab."
System.out.println,Print a String with Quotes,"Write a `println` statement that displays a sentence containing double quotes."
System.out.println,Print the Value of a Boolean Expression,"Directly print the result of a comparison, such as `System.out.println(10 > 5);`."
System.out.println,Print a Method's Return Value,"Create a simple method that returns a String, and call this method inside a `println` statement."
System.out.println,Difference between `print` and `println`,"Use `System.out.print()` followed by `System.out.println()` to see how they combine on one line."
System.out.println,Print a Simple ASCII Art Box,"Use multiple `println` statements to draw a 3x3 box made of asterisks."
System.out.println,Print a User's Full Name,"Create three String variables for a first, middle, and last name. Print the full name on one line."
System.out.println,Print Calculation with Labels,"Print the result of a calculation with a descriptive label, e.g. `""Area: "" + (width * height)`."
System.out.println,Print Object Reference (Default `toString`),"Create a simple object (e.g. `new Object()`) and print it to see the default output."
System.out.println,Print System Property,"Use `println` to print a system property, like `System.getProperty(""java.version"")`."
System.out.println,Print a Formatted Address,"Use multiple `println` statements to print a mailing address, formatted correctly on separate lines."
System.out.println,Print a Null Value,"Declare a String variable and assign it `null`. Use `println` to print the variable's value."
System.out.println,Print a Long Expression,"Write a single `println` statement that concatenates five different strings together."
System.out.println,Print the Length of a String,"Directly print the length of a string literal, e.g. `System.out.println(""Hello"".length());`."
System.out.println,Print a Warning Message,"Use `println` to display a formatted warning message, such as `""WARNING: File not found.""`."
"Complex Scenarios","UsingCommandLineArgs","Modify your main method to print the first command-line argument ('args[0]')."
"Complex Scenarios","PassingCommandLineArgs","Run the previous program from the command line, passing your name as an argument (e.g. 'java MyProgram Alice')."
"Complex Scenarios","ArrayIndexOutOfBounds","Run the same program again, but this time, do not provide any command-line arguments. Observe and explain the 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
"Complex Scenarios","LoopThroughAllArgs","Write a program that loops through the 'args' array and prints every command-line argument that was passed to it."
"Complex Scenarios","CompilingWithPackages","Place your .java file in a subdirectory structure that matches a package name (e.g. 'com/mycompany/'). Compile it from the root directory."
"Complex Scenarios","RunningWithPackages","Run the compiled, packaged program from the root directory, using the fully qualified class name (e.g. 'java com.mycompany.MyClass')."
"Complex Scenarios","IntroToDebugger","Using an IDE like VS Code, set a breakpoint on the first line inside your 'main' method."
"Complex Scenarios","StartTheDebugger","Run your program in debug mode. The execution should pause at your breakpoint."
"Complex Scenarios","InspectVariables","While paused in the debugger, find the 'Variables' window and inspect the value of the 'args' array."
"Complex Scenarios","StepOver","With the debugger paused, use the 'Step Over' command to execute the current line and move to the next one."
"Complex Scenarios","StepInto","Create a second method in your class that is called by 'main'. Place a breakpoint on the method call and use 'Step Into' to move the debugger into that method."
"Complex Scenarios","CreateAJarFile","Use the 'jar' command-line tool to package your '.class' file(s) into an executable JAR file."
"Complex Scenarios","RunFromTheJar","Run your Java application directly from the JAR file you created using the 'java -jar' command."
"Complex Scenarios","ViewJarContents","Use the 'jar -tf' command to view the table of contents of your JAR file without extracting it."
Variables: Declaration,"DeclareAnInteger","Declare an integer variable named 'age' without initializing it."
Variables: Initialization,"InitializeAfterDeclaration","Declare an integer 'score', and on a separate line, initialize it to 100."
Variables: Combined,"DeclareAndInitialize","Declare and initialize a 'double' variable named 'price' to 19.99 in a single line."
Variables: Naming,"CamelCaseConvention","Declare a String variable to store a user's full name, following the camelCase naming convention."
Variables: Primitives,"AllPrimitiveTypes","Declare and initialize a separate variable for each of Java's 8 primitive types."
Variables: Reference Types,"DeclareAString","Declare and initialize a String variable named 'greeting' with the value ""Hello, World!"". "
Variables: Reassignment,"UpdateVariable","Declare an integer 'level', initialize it to 1, and then reassign its value to 2."
Variables: Constants,"DeclareFinal","Declare a 'final' double variable named 'PI' and initialize it to 3.14159."
Variables: Constants,"AttemptToChangeFinal","After declaring a final variable, attempt to reassign it to a new value and observe the compiler error."
Variables: Scope,"BlockScope","Declare a variable inside an 'if' block. Try to access it outside of the block and explain the scope error."
Variables: Scope,"MethodScope","Declare a variable inside a method. Try to access it from another method in the same class."
Variables: Scope,"VariableShadowing","Declare an instance variable 'x'. Inside a method, declare a local variable also named 'x'. Assign a value to the local 'x' and show how to access the instance 'x' using 'this.x'."
Variables: Type Casting,"ImplicitCasting","Assign an 'int' value to a 'double' variable and print the result to demonstrate widening conversion."
Variables: Type Casting,"ExplicitCasting","Assign a 'double' value to an 'int' variable using an explicit cast. Print the result to show truncation."
Variables: Default Values,"PrimitiveDefaultValues","Declare an instance variable for each primitive type but do not initialize them. Print their values from a method to see their defaults."
Variables: Default Values,"ReferenceDefaultValue","Declare an instance variable of type 'String' without initializing it. Print its value to see that it is 'null'."
Variables: Arithmetic,"SimpleExpression","Declare two integer variables, 'a' and 'b'. Create a third variable, 'sum', to store the result of their addition."
Variables: Concatenation,"StringAndInt","Declare a String 'label' and an int 'value'. Create a new String by concatenating them (e.g. ""Score: 100"")."
Variables: Swapping,"SwapTwoVariables","Declare two integers, 'x' and 'y'. Write the code to swap their values using a third temporary variable."
Variables: Reference vs Primitive,"PrimitiveAssignment","Assign an int 'a' to another int 'b'. Change 'a' and show that 'b' does not change."
Variables: Reference vs Primitive,"ReferenceAssignment","Assign a String object 's1' to another String 's2'. Explain why changing 's1' (e.g. s1 = ""New"") doesn't affect 's2' due to immutability and reference changes."
Variables: Reference vs Primitive,"MutableObjectReference","(Advanced) Create a 'StringBuilder' object 'sb1'. Assign it to 'sb2'. Append text using 'sb1' and print 'sb2' to show they both point to the same mutable object."
Variables: Type Inference,"SimpleVar","Use the 'var' keyword to declare and initialize a String. Print its class using '.getClass().getName()'."
Variables: Type Inference,"VarWithPrimitives","Use 'var' to declare a variable initialized with an integer literal. What is its inferred type?"
Variables: Type Inference,"VarLimitations","Try to declare a variable using 'var' without initializing it. Observe and explain the compiler error."
Variables: Type Inference,"VarAndNull","Try to initialize a 'var' variable with 'null'. Explain the resulting error."
Variables: Instance vs Static,"InstanceVariable","Create a class with an instance variable. Create two objects of the class, give the variable different values in each, and print them."
Variables: Instance vs Static,"StaticVariable","Add a 'static' variable to the same class. Change its value using one object and show that the value has changed when accessed via the second object."
Variables: Instance vs Static,"AccessingStatic","Show how to access the static variable from the previous exercise directly through the class name, without an object instance."
Variables: Lifecycle,"LocalVariableLifecycle","In a method, print a variable's value. Explain that the variable only exists while the method is executing."
Variables: Lifecycle,"InstanceVariableLifecycle","Explain that an instance variable's lifecycle is tied to the object it belongs to."
Variables: Uninitialized Local,"UninitializedLocalError","Declare a local variable inside a method but do not initialize it. Try to use it in a 'println' statement and observe the compile-time error."
Variables: Final Reference,"FinalReferencePitfall","Declare a 'final StringBuilder' variable. Show that while you can't reassign the variable, you can still modify the object it refers to (e.g. by appending text)."
Variables: char And int,"CharAsInt","Assign the character 'A' to an 'int' variable. Print the integer value."
Variables: int As char,"IntAsChar","Cast the integer 66 to a 'char' and print the resulting character."
Variables: Complex Declaration,"MultipleInOneLine","Declare three integer variables ('i', 'j', 'k') in a single statement."
Variables: Complex Initialization,"InitializeOneOfMany","In a single statement, declare three integers, but only initialize the second one."
Variables: Scope Challenge,"NestedBlockScope","Declare a variable 'x' in a method. Inside a 'for' loop in that method, declare another variable 'x'. Explain which 'x' is accessible where."
Variables: Widening And Narrowing,"DataLossExample","Cast a 'long' value that is larger than 'Integer.MAX_VALUE' to an 'int' and print the result to demonstrate data loss."
Variables: Var With Object,"VarAndObjectCreation","Use 'var' to declare a variable that holds a new instance of a custom class you create."
Variables: Final In Loop,"FinalInForEachLoop","Show that you can declare a 'final' variable in the declaration part of an enhanced for-each loop."
Variables: Underscore Literals,"NumericLiterals","Declare a 'long' variable for one million using underscores for readability (e.g. '1_000_000')."
"Arrays: Declaration","DeclareIntegerArray","Declare an array of integers named 'scores' that can hold 10 elements, but do not initialize it."
"Arrays: Initialization","InitializeWithNew","Initialize the 'scores' array from the previous exercise using the 'new' keyword."
"Arrays: Initialization","InitializeWithLiteral","Declare and initialize an array of Strings named 'weekdays' with the days of the week in a single line."
"Arrays: Accessing","GetFirstAndLast","From the 'weekdays' array, access and print the first element and the last element using its index."
"Arrays: Modifying","ChangeAnElement","Create an integer array with 5 numbers. Change the value of the element at index 2 to be 99."
"Arrays: Properties","ArrayLength","Create an array and print its size to the console using the '.length' property."
"Arrays: Iteration","LoopWithFor","Use a standard 'for' loop to iterate through an integer array and print each element."
"Arrays: Iteration","LoopWithForEach","Use an enhanced for-each loop to iterate through a String array and print each element."
"Arrays: Operations","CalculateSum","Write code to calculate the sum of all elements in an integer array."
"Arrays: Operations","CalculateAverage","Calculate the average of the elements in a double array. Ensure the result is a double."
"Arrays: Operations","FindMaximum","Write code to find the largest number in an integer array."
"Arrays: Operations","FindMinimum","Write code to find the smallest number in an integer array."
"Arrays: Searching","LinearSearch","Write a program to find if a specific number exists in an array. Print 'Found' or 'Not Found'."
"Arrays: Exceptions","OutOfBoundsError","Write code that intentionally tries to access an index outside the bounds of an array to trigger an 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException'."
"Arrays: Default Values","PrimitiveArrayDefaults","Declare an array of 5 integers without initializing its elements. Print the value at index 0 to see its default value."
"Arrays: Default Values","ObjectArrayDefaults","Declare an array of 5 Strings. Print the value at index 0 to see that its default is 'null'."
"Arrays: Utility Class","PrintAnArray","Use the 'Arrays.toString()' method to print the contents of an array in a readable format."
"Arrays: Utility Class","SortAnArray","Use the 'Arrays.sort()' method to sort an array of integers in ascending order."
"Arrays: Utility Class","FillAnArray","Use 'Arrays.fill()' to initialize all elements of an integer array to the value 7."
"Arrays: Copying","CopyArrayWithLoop","Copy all elements from one array to a new array of the same size using a 'for' loop."
"Arrays: Copying","CopyArrayWithSystem","Use 'System.arraycopy()' to copy a portion of one array into another."
"Arrays: Copying","CopyArrayWithArraysClass","Use 'Arrays.copyOf()' to create a new, larger array that contains all the elements of an original array."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","ReverseInPlace","Reverse the elements of an array in-place without creating a second array."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","FindDuplicates","Write code to find and print any duplicate values in a String array."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","ArrayOfObjects","Create a 'Student' class. Then, create an array that holds three instances of the 'Student' class."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","PassingArrayToMethod","Create a method that takes an integer array as a parameter and doubles the value of each element."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","ReturningArrayFromMethod","Create a method that takes an integer 'n' and returns a new array containing the first 'n' even numbers."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","CheckIfSorted","Write a method that returns 'true' if an integer array is sorted in ascending order and 'false' otherwise."
"Arrays: Complex Challenges","ShiftElementsLeft","Shift all elements of an array one position to the left, with the first element wrapping around to the end."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","Declare2DArray","Declare and initialize a 2x3 two-dimensional array (a grid) of integers."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","Access2DElement","From the 2D array, access and print the element in the first row, second column."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","Iterate2DArray","Use nested 'for' loops to iterate through all the elements of a 2D array and print them."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","SumAll2DElements","Write code to calculate the sum of all elements in a 2D integer array."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","SumARow","Write code to calculate the sum of elements in only the second row of a 2D array."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","FindIn2DArray","Search a 2D array for a specific value and print its row and column index if found."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","TicTacToe","Create a 3x3 char array to represent a Tic-Tac-Toe board, initializing it with empty spaces."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","RaggedArrayDeclare","Declare and initialize a 'ragged' or 'jagged' 2D array where each row has a different number of columns."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","IterateRaggedArray","Write the nested loops required to correctly iterate through all elements of a ragged array."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","LargestInEachRow","For a 2D array, find the largest element in each row and print it."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","MatrixAddition","Create two 2x2 matrices (2D arrays) and create a third matrix that is their sum."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","Declare3DArray","Declare and initialize a 3D array (a cube) of dimensions 2x2x2."
"Arrays: Multidimensional","Access3DElement","Access and print an element from the 'deepest' corner of the 3D array."
"Operators: Arithmetic","BasicAddition","Add two integer literals and store the result in a variable."
"Operators: Arithmetic","SubtractionAndNegation","Subtract one number from another. Separately, show the use of the unary minus operator to negate a number."
"Operators: Arithmetic","MultiplicationAndDivision","Multiply two doubles. Separately, perform integer division and double division on the same two numbers and compare."
"Operators: Arithmetic","ModuloForRemainder","Use the modulo operator (%) to find the remainder of 10 divided by 3."
"Operators: Arithmetic","EvenOrOdd","Use the modulo operator to determine if an integer is even or odd."
"Operators: Unary","PrefixIncrement","Declare an integer 'x'. In a separate statement, print the value of '++x' and then print 'x' again."
"Operators: Unary","PostfixIncrement","Declare an integer 'y'. In a separate statement, print the value of 'y++' and then print 'y' again."
"Operators: Unary","PrefixVsPostfixInExpression","Given 'int a = 5;', predict and explain the output of 'System.out.println(++a + a++);'."
"Operators: Unary","LogicalNOT","Declare a boolean 'isLoggedIn' as false. Print the value of '!isLoggedIn'."
"Operators: Assignment","SimpleAssignment","Declare and initialize a variable in one step using the '=' operator."
"Operators: Assignment","CompoundAddition","Use the '+=' operator to add 5 to an existing integer variable."
"Operators: Assignment","CompoundMultiplication","Use the '*=' operator to double the value of a variable."
"Operators: Assignment","ChainAssignment","Assign the same value to three different variables in a single line (e.g. 'a = b = c = 0;')."
"Operators: Relational","EqualTo","Use the '==' operator to compare two identical integer primitives. Then, compare two identical String literals."
"Operators: Relational","NotEqualTo","Use the '!=' operator to check if a variable's value is not 0."
"Operators: Relational","GreaterThan","Use the '>' operator to check if a variable 'score' is greater than 90."
"Operators: Relational","LessThanOrEqualTo","Use the '<=' operator to check if a variable 'itemsInCart' is less than or equal to the maximum allowed."
"Operators: Relational","ObjectComparison","Demonstrate why '==' returns false when comparing two different String objects created with 'new', even if they have the same content."
"Operators: Logical","LogicalAND","Write an 'if' statement that executes only if 'age >= 18 && hasLicense == true'."
"Operators: Logical","LogicalOR","Write an 'if' statement that executes if 'role.equals(""Admin"") || isOwner == true'."
"Operators: Logical","ShortCircuitingAND","Demonstrate short-circuiting by checking if a String object is not null AND its length is greater than 0."
"Operators: Logical","ShortCircuitingOR","Demonstrate short-circuiting by creating a condition where the left side of an '||' is true, preventing a method call on the right side."
"Operators: Bitwise","BitwiseAND","Perform a bitwise AND operation between the numbers 5 (0101) and 3 (0011) and print the result."
"Operators: Bitwise","BitwiseOR","Perform a bitwise OR operation between 5 (0101) and 3 (0011) and print the result."
"Operators: Bitwise","BitwiseXOR","Perform a bitwise XOR operation between 5 (0101) and 3 (0011). Use it to swap two numbers without a temporary variable."
"Operators: Bitwise","BitwiseNOT","Perform a bitwise NOT (complement) operation on the number 5 and explain the two's complement result."
"Operators: Bitwise","LeftShift","Use the left shift operator '<<' to multiply a number by 4."
"Operators: Bitwise","RightShift","Use the signed right shift operator '>>' to divide a negative number by 2."
"Operators: Bitwise","UnsignedRightShift","Use the unsigned right shift operator '>>>' on a negative number and compare the result with the signed right shift."
"Operators: Bitwise","CheckingABit","Use bitwise AND to check if the 3rd bit of an integer is set (is 1)."
"Operators: Bitwise","SettingABit","Use bitwise OR to set the 4th bit of an integer to 1."
"Operators: Ternary","SimpleTernary","Use the ternary operator to assign ""Even"" or ""Odd"" to a string variable based on an integer."
"Operators: Ternary","NestedTernary","Use a nested ternary operator to classify a number as ""Positive"", ""Negative"", or ""Zero""."
"Operators: Ternary","TernaryForReturnValue","Write a method that uses a single ternary expression in its return statement."
"Operators: instanceof","SimpleInstanceOf","Check if a variable of type 'Object' holding a 'String' is an instance of the 'String' class."
"Operators: instanceof","InstanceOfWithInheritance","Create a superclass 'Animal' and a subclass 'Dog'. Check if a 'Dog' object is an instance of both 'Dog' and 'Animal'."
"Operators: instanceof","InstanceOfNull","Check if a 'null' reference is an instance of any class and observe the result."
"Operators: Combined","ComplexArithmetic","Predict the result of '10 / 2 * (5 - 3) + 7 % 4'. Document the order of operations."
"Operators: Combined","ComplexLogical","Predict the result of '!(true && false) || (true && !false)'."
"Operators: Combined","ComplexBitwiseAndArithmetic","Predict the result of '5 + (7 & 3) << 1'."
"Operators: Combined","ArrowOperator","(Advanced) Create a simple Lambda expression using the arrow '->' operator."
"Operators: Combined","MethodReference","(Advanced) Show the use of the double colon '::' method reference operator."
"The String Class","DeclareAndInitialize","Create a String using a literal and another using the 'new' keyword. Print both."
"The String Class","StringConcatenation","Concatenate two strings using the '+' operator and print the result."
"The String Class","StringLength","Find and print the length of a given String using the '.length()' method."
"The String Class","AccessCharacter","Get and print the character at index 3 of a String using '.charAt()'."
"The String Class","CompareStringsEquals","Compare two strings for exact, case-sensitive equality using '.equals()'."
"The String Class","CompareStringsIgnoreCase","Compare two strings for equality, ignoring case, using '.equalsIgnoreCase()'."
"The String Class","CheckIfEmpty","Use '.isEmpty()' to check if a String is empty. Test with both an empty and a non-empty string."
"The String Class","FindSubstringIndex","Find the first occurrence of the substring ""Java"" in a sentence using '.indexOf()'."
"The String Class","FindLastSubstringIndex","Find the last occurrence of the character 'o' in a sentence using '.lastIndexOf()'."
"The String Class","CheckForSubstring","Use '.contains()' to check if a sentence contains the word ""awesome""."
"The String Class","StartsWith","Check if a String starts with the prefix ""https://"" using '.startsWith()'."
"The String Class","EndsWith","Check if a filename String ends with the suffix "".java"" using '.endsWith()'."
"The String Class","ExtractSubstring","Extract a substring from index 5 to 10 of a given String using '.substring()'."
"The String Class","ExtractToEnd","Extract a substring from index 8 to the end of the String using the one-argument version of '.substring()'."
"The String Class","ToUpperCase","Convert an entire String to uppercase using '.toUpperCase()'."
"The String Class","ToLowerCase","Convert an entire String to lowercase using '.toLowerCase()'."
"The String Class","TrimWhitespace","Remove leading and trailing whitespace from a String using '.trim()'."
"The String Class","ReplaceCharacter","Replace all occurrences of the character 'a' with '@' in a String using '.replace()'."
"The String Class","ReplaceSubstring","Replace the first occurrence of the word ""error"" with ""success"" using '.replaceFirst()'."
"The String Class","SplitBySpace","Split a sentence into an array of words using the space character as a delimiter with '.split()'."
"The String Class","SplitByComma","Split a CSV string (e.g. ""one,two,three"") into an array of values."
"The String Class","ImmutabilityDemo1","Create a String, call '.toUpperCase()' on it, and print the original string to show it hasn't changed."
"The String Class","ImmutabilityDemo2","Explain in a comment why String is immutable and what happens in memory when you ""modify"" a String."
"The String Class","StringPool","Create two strings with the same literal value. Compare them using '==' and '.equals()' and explain the results."
"The String Class","NewVsLiteral","Create one string with a literal and another with 'new String(""..."")'. Compare them with '==' and explain the difference."
"The String Class","IntToString","Convert an integer to a String using 'String.valueOf()'."
"The String Class","StringToCharArray","Convert a String to a character array using '.toCharArray()' and loop through it."
"The String Class","JoinStringArray","Join an array of strings into a single string with a hyphen delimiter using 'String.join()'."
"The String Class","FormatString","Use 'String.format()' to create a string like ""Hello, [Name]! You have [Number] messages."" with variables."
"The String Class","CompareToLexicographically","Use '.compareTo()' to determine if one string comes before or after another alphabetically."
"The String Class","MethodChaining","On a single line, trim a string, convert it to lowercase, and check if it starts with ""hello""."
"The String Class","StringBuilderIntro","Create a simple loop that concatenates numbers to a string. Re-write it using 'StringBuilder' for better performance."
"The String Class","StringBuilderAppend","Use 'StringBuilder.append()' to build a string piece by piece."
"The String Class","StringBuilderReverse","Use 'StringBuilder.reverse()' to reverse a string."
"The String Class","PalindromeCheck","Write code to check if a string is a palindrome (reads the same forwards and backwards)."
"The String Class","CountVowels","Write a program that counts the number of vowels in a given string."
"The String Class","ExtractFileName","Given a full file path (e.g. ""/users/home/document.txt""), extract just the filename ""document.txt""."
"The String Class","GetFileExtension","From the file path in the previous exercise, extract just the extension ""txt""."
"The String Class","RegularExpressionMatch","Use the '.matches()' method to check if a string is a valid 5-digit zip code (e.g. matches the regex ""\\d{5}"")."
"The String Class","ReplaceAllWithRegex","Use '.replaceAll()' to replace all digits in a string with the '#' character."
"The String Class","InternMethod","Create a string with 'new' and another with a literal. Call '.intern()' on the 'new' string and compare with '==' again."
"The String Class","CodePointAt","Use '.codePointAt()' to get the Unicode value of a character, including one outside the Basic Multilingual Plane (e.g. an emoji)."
"String Constants","LiteralVsNewObject","Create two strings: one with a literal ""Java"" and one with 'new String(""Java"")'. Compare them with '=='."
"String Constants","TwoLiterals","Create two string variables, both assigned the literal ""Hello"". Compare them using '==' and explain the result."
"String Constants","TheStringPool","In a comment, define what the String Constant Pool is and its purpose in Java."
"String Constants","InternMethodSimple","Create a string with 'new'. Call the '.intern()' method on it and assign the result to a new variable. Compare this new variable with a literal string using '=='."
"String Constants","InternOnLiteral","What happens when you call '.intern()' on a string that was already created as a literal? Demonstrate with code."
"String Constants","ConcatenatedLiterals","Create a string 'String s = ""He"" + ""llo"";'. Compare it with the literal ""Hello"" using '=='. Explain the compile-time concatenation."
"String Constants","ConcatenatedVariables","Create two string variables. Concatenate them and compare the result with a literal using '=='. Explain why the result is false."
"String Constants","FinalVariableConcatenation","Declare two 'final' string variables. Concatenate them and compare the result with a literal using '=='. Explain the difference from the previous exercise."
"String Constants","LiteralAndVariableConcat","Concatenate a string literal with a string variable. Compare the result to a new literal using '==' and explain."
"String Constants","GarbageCollection","If you create a string with 'new String(""...")') that is not interned, is it eligible for garbage collection like other objects? Explain."
"String Constants","SubstringAndPool","Create a string literal. Call '.substring()' on it to get an identical string. Compare the result with the original using '=='."
"String Constants","ReplaceAndPool","Call '.replace()' on a string literal in a way that results in an identical string. Compare the new string with the original using '=='."
"String Constants","ToUpperCaseAndPool","Call '.toUpperCase()' on a lowercase string literal. Compare the result with a new uppercase literal using '=='."
"String Constants","StringBuilderAndPool","Create a string using 'StringBuilder'. Convert it to a String and compare it with a literal of the same value using '=='."
"String Constants","SwitchStatementStrings","Use string literals in a 'switch' statement. Explain how the String Pool makes this efficient."
"String Constants","AnnotationsAndLiterals","Explain why string values used in annotations must be compile-time constants."
"String Constants","MemoryUsage","In a comment, discuss the memory implications of creating thousands of strings using 'new' versus using literals."
"String Constants","PerformanceOfIntern","Discuss a scenario where calling '.intern()' might be useful, and a scenario where it might hurt performance."
"String Constants","StringFromCharArray","Create a string from a character array. Compare it with a literal of the same value using '=='."
"String Constants","StringValueOf","Convert an integer to a string using 'String.valueOf()'. Compare the result with a literal using '=='."
"String Constants","NewStringFromLiteral","Predict the result of 'new String(""abc"") == new String(""abc"")'."
"String Constants","LiteralFromConcatenatedFinals","Given 'final String a = ""a""; final String b = ""b"";', predict '""ab"" == a + b'."
"String Constants","LiteralFromConcatenatedNonFinals","Given 'String a = ""a""; String b = ""b"";', predict '""ab"" == a + b'."
"String Constants","InterningAConcatenatedString","Take the concatenated string from the previous exercise, call '.intern()' on it, and then compare it to the literal '""ab""'."
"String Constants","ClassConstants","Declare a 'public static final String' constant in a class. Explain where this string is stored."
"String Constants","LoadingClasses","If two different classes both use the literal ""OK"", how many ""OK"" objects are in the String Pool?"
"String Constants","SystemIdentityHashCode","Use 'System.identityHashCode()' to print the hash codes of two identical literals and one 'new' string."
"String Constants","SplitAndPool","Split a string literal. Compare the first element of the resulting array with another literal using '=='."
"String Constants","TrimAndPool","Call '.trim()' on a literal that has spaces (' "" hello "" '). Compare the result with the literal '""hello""' using '=='."
"String Constants","DynamicVsCompileTime","Explain the difference between a compile-time constant string and a string whose value is determined at runtime."
"String Constants","InternAndGarbageCollection","What happens to a string in the String Pool if it is interned but no other references to it exist? Can it be garbage collected?"
"String Constants","StringJoinerAndPool","Use 'StringJoiner' to build a string. Compare the final string with a literal using '=='."
"String Constants","FormatAndPool","Use 'String.format()' to create a string. Compare it with a literal of the same value using '=='."
"String Constants","ToCharArrayAndBack","Convert a literal to a char array and then create a new string from that array. Compare the new string to the original literal with '=='."
"String Constants","StringBuilderCapacity","Does the initial capacity of a 'StringBuilder' have any relationship to the String Pool?"
"String Constants","StringFromBytes","Create a string from a byte array. Compare it to a literal using '=='."
"String Constants","ReflectionAndLiterals","Can you use reflection to modify the value of a string literal in the pool? (Discuss why this is a bad idea)."
"String Constants","StringDeduplicationG1","(Advanced) Research and explain in a comment the G1 garbage collector's String Deduplication feature and how it relates to the String Pool."
"String Constants","RecordClassAndStrings","Create a Java Record with a String field. Instantiate it with a literal and discuss how the String Pool is involved."
"String Constants","TextBlockAndPool","Create a string using a Text Block (Java 15+). Compare it to an equivalent single-line literal using '=='."
"String Constants","PredictTheOutput1","Predict: 'String s1 = ""test""; String s2 = new String(s1); System.out.println(s1 == s2.intern());'"
"String Constants","PredictTheOutput2","Predict: 'String s1 = ""Ja""; String s2 = ""va""; String s3 = s1 + s2; System.out.println(s3 == ""Java"");'"
"The Scanner Class","ReadFullName","Create a Scanner and ask the user for their first name and last name. Read them using 'next()' and print a welcome message."
"The Scanner Class","ReadAnInteger","Prompt the user to enter their age and read it using 'nextInt()'. Print back their age."
"The Scanner Class","ReadADouble","Prompt the user to enter the price of an item and read it using 'nextDouble()'."
"The Scanner Class","TheNextLineTrap","Ask for the user's age ('nextInt()'), then ask for their favorite quote ('nextLine()'). Observe the problem and then fix it."
"The Scanner Class","FixTheNextLineTrap","Explain in a comment two ways to fix the 'nextLine trap' demonstrated in the previous exercise."
"The Scanner Class","SumTwoNumbers","Read two integers from the user and print their sum."
"The Scanner Class","SimpleCalculator","Read two doubles and a character ('+', '-', '*', '/') from the user. Perform the corresponding calculation."
"The Scanner Class","HasNextIntValidation","Use a 'while' loop and 'hasNextInt()' to ensure the user enters a valid integer before you try to read it."
"The Scanner Class","HasNextDoubleValidation","Use an 'if' statement with 'hasNextDouble()' to check if the next input is a double before reading it."
"The Scanner Class","ClosingTheScanner","Create a Scanner, use it, and then properly close it using the '.close()' method. Explain why this is important."
"The Scanner Class","TryWithResources","Rewrite the previous exercise using a try-with-resources block to automatically close the Scanner."
"The Scanner Class","InputMismatchException","Write code that prompts for an integer but enter a string. Catch the 'InputMismatchException' and print a friendly error message."
"The Scanner Class","LoopUntilValidInput","Combine a 'while' loop, a try-catch block, and 'hasNextInt()' to repeatedly prompt a user until they enter a valid integer."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingBooleans","Prompt the user with a yes/no question and read their answer ('true' or 'false') using 'nextBoolean()'."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingSingleCharacter","Ask the user to enter a single character and read it. (Hint: use 'next().charAt(0)')."
"The Scanner Class","ChangingTheDelimiter","Use the 'useDelimiter()' method to change the Scanner's delimiter to a comma. Read a comma-separated list of numbers."
"The Scanner Class","ResettingTheDelimiter","After changing the delimiter, show how to reset it back to the default whitespace."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingAnEntireLine","Ask the user to type a full sentence and read the entire line, including spaces, using 'nextLine()'."
"The Scanner Class","TokenizingAString","Create a Scanner that reads from a String object instead of 'System.in'. Iterate through its tokens."
"The Scanner Class","CountingWordsInString","Use a Scanner on a String and a 'while' loop with 'hasNext()' to count the number of words."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingFromFile","Create a text file with some data. Use a Scanner with a 'File' object to read and print the contents of the file."
"The Scanner Class","FileNotFoundException","Wrap the file-reading exercise in a try-catch block to handle the 'FileNotFoundException'."
"The Scanner Class","SumNumbersFromFile","Create a file containing one integer per line. Use a Scanner to read the file and calculate the sum of the numbers."
"The Scanner Class","ParsingCSV","Create a String of comma-separated values (e.g. ""apple,banana,cherry""). Use a Scanner with a changed delimiter to print each value."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingMixedDataTypes","Read a line of input that contains a name, age, and GPA (e.g. ""John 25 3.8"") in a single line using multiple 'next...' calls."
"The Scanner Class","LoopForMultipleRecords","Write a program that uses a loop to ask for and read the name and age for three different people."
"The Scanner Class","SentinelControlledLoop","Use a 'while' loop with a Scanner to read numbers from the user until they enter a specific value (e.g. -1) to quit."
"The Scanner Class","FindMinAndMax","Read a series of integers from the user (ending with a non-integer) and find the minimum and maximum values entered."
"The Scanner Class","ScannerAndLocale","Create a Scanner and use 'useLocale()' to set it to a locale (e.g. 'Locale.GERMANY') where the decimal separator is a comma."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingWithRadix","Use 'useRadix(16)' to make the Scanner interpret the next integer as a hexadecimal number."
"The Scanner Class","ScannerFindInLine","Use the 'findInLine()' method to find and extract a specific pattern (e.g. a four-digit number) from a line of text."
"The Scanner Class","ScannerSkipPattern","Use the 'skip()' method to ignore a certain pattern in the input stream."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingFromURL","(Advanced) Create a Scanner that reads the HTML source code from a URL object."
"The Scanner Class","MultipleScanners","Create one Scanner for 'System.in' and another for a String. Use both and explain why closing the System.in scanner is problematic in some apps."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingUntilEOF","When reading from a file, use a 'while(scanner.hasNextLine())' loop to read every line until the end of the file."
"The Scanner Class","BufferingIssue","Discuss in a comment what the internal buffer of the Scanner is and how it relates to the 'nextLine()' trap."
"The Scanner Class","ClearingTheBuffer","Show how 'scanner.nextLine()' can be used by itself to clear the input buffer after a 'nextInt()' call."
"The Scanner Class","PasswordEntry","Read a password from the user. Discuss why Scanner is not the ideal class for this and mention 'System.console()'."
"The Scanner Class","BuildingAnArray","Ask the user how many numbers they want to enter. Create an array of that size, then use a loop and a Scanner to fill the array."
"The Scanner Class","ReadingMultilineInput","Tell the user to enter a short story and type 'END' on a new line to finish. Read the input line by line until 'END' is detected."
"The Scanner Class","ParsingKeyValuePairs","Read a string like ""name=John age=30"". Use a Scanner with multiple delimiters ('=' and ' ') to parse the keys and values."
"The Scanner Class","InteractiveStory","Create a simple 'mad libs' style game where you ask the user for nouns, verbs, etc., and build a story with their input."
"Operator Precedence","MultiplicationBeforeAddition","Predict the output of 'int result = 5 + 3 * 2;'. Explain why multiplication is performed first."
"Operator Precedence","DivisionBeforeSubtraction","Predict the output of 'int result = 20 - 10 / 2;'. Explain the order of operations."
"Operator Precedence","ParenthesesOverride","Predict the output of 'int result = (5 + 3) * 2;'. Explain how parentheses change the evaluation order."
"Operator Precedence","ModuloAndAddition","Predict the output of 'int result = 10 % 3 + 4;'. Which operator has higher precedence?"
"Operator Precedence","LeftToRightAssociativity","Predict the output of 'int result = 10 - 5 - 3;'. Explain the role of left-to-right associativity for subtraction."
"Operator Precedence","MultiplicativeAssociativity","Predict the output of 'int result = 24 / 4 / 2;'. Explain how associativity applies here."
"Operator Precedence","UnaryMinus","Predict the output of 'int result = 10 + -3 * 2;'. Explain the precedence of the unary minus operator."
"Operator Precedence","PrefixIncrement","Given 'int x = 5;', predict the final values of x and y in 'int y = ++x;'. "
"Operator Precedence","PostfixIncrement","Given 'int x = 5;', predict the final values of x and y in 'int y = x++;'."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexIncrement","Given 'int x = 3;', predict the output of 'System.out.println(x++ * ++x);'."
"Operator Precedence","LogicalNOT","Predict the output of 'boolean result = !(true && false);'. Explain the precedence of the NOT operator."
"Operator Precedence","RelationalBeforeEquality","Predict the output of 'boolean result = 5 > 3 == 6 < 4;'. Explain the evaluation order."
"Operator Precedence","ArithmeticBeforeRelational","Predict the output of 'boolean result = 5 + 2 > 6;'. Which is evaluated first, '+' or '>'?"
"Operator Precedence","LogicalANDBeforeOR","Predict the output of 'boolean result = true || false && false;'. Explain the precedence of '&&' vs '||'."
"Operator Precedence","ParenthesesInLogicalExpr","Predict the output of 'boolean result = (true || false) && false;'. How do parentheses affect the outcome?"
"Operator Precedence","RightToLeftAssignment","Predict the final values of a, b, and c after 'int a, b, c; a = b = c = 10;'."
"Operator Precedence","CompoundAssignment","Given 'int x = 5;', predict the final value of x after 'x += 3 * 2;'."
"Operator Precedence","ShiftAndAddition","Predict the output of 'int result = 5 + 4 << 1;'. Explain the precedence of additive vs. shift operators."
"Operator Precedence","BitwiseANDAndEquality","Predict the output of 'boolean result = 5 == 3 & 7 == 7;'. Note the use of single '&'."
"Operator Precedence","BitwiseORAndEquality","Predict the output of 'boolean result = 5 > 3 | 2 < 1;'. Note the use of single '|'."
"Operator Precedence","BitwiseVsLogicalPrecedence","Predict the output of 'boolean result = true || true && false | false;'. Explain the full order."
"Operator Precedence","TernaryOperatorSimple","Predict the output of 'int result = 5 > 3 ? 10 : 20;'."
"Operator Precedence","TernaryAndArithmetic","Predict the output of 'int result = 10 + (5 > 3 ? 10 : 20);'. What happens without parentheses?"
"Operator Precedence","TernaryLowPrecedence","Predict the output of 'int result = 5 > 3 ? 10 : 20 + 5;'. Explain why the addition is not applied to both outcomes."
"Operator Precedence","InstanceOfPrecedence","Given 'String s = ""hello"";', predict the output of 'boolean result = s instanceof String == true;'."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexExpression1","Predict the output of 'int result = 10 * 2 / 5 + 3 - 1;'. Document each step of the evaluation."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexExpression2","Given 'int a=5, b=6, c=7;', predict the output of 'boolean result = a + b * c > 50 && c - a > b;'."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexExpression3","Given 'int x=2;', predict the final value of x after 'x *= 5 + 3;'."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexExpression4","Predict the output of 'int result = 12 / 3 * 2 + 5 % 3;'."
"Operator Precedence","ComplexExpression5","Predict the output of 'boolean result = !(5 * 2 > 10) || 5 + 1 == 6;'."
"Operator Precedence","IntegerAndDouble","Predict the output of 'double result = 5 / 2 * 2.0;'. Explain the role of integer division."
"Operator Precedence","IntegerAndDoubleReordered","Predict the output of 'double result = 5 * 2.0 / 2;'. Compare the result to the previous exercise."
"Operator Precedence","BitwiseXORPrecedence","Predict the output of 'int result = 5 + 2 ^ 3 + 1;'. Where does XOR fall in the order of operations?"
"Operator Precedence","ShiftWithParentheses","Predict the output of 'int result = (5 + 3) << 1;'. Compare with the earlier shift exercise."
"Operator Precedence","UnaryAndMultiplicative","Given 'int x = 5;', predict the output of 'int result = -x++;'. Explain the interaction of unary minus and postfix."
"Operator Precedence","PrefixInExpression","Given 'int a = 2, b = 3;', predict the output of 'int result = ++a * b - a;'."
"Operator Precedence","PostfixInExpression","Given 'int a = 2, b = 3;', predict the output of 'int result = a++ * b - a;'."
"Operator Precedence","BitwiseNOT","Predict the output of 'int result = ~10 + 3;'. Explain the precedence of bitwise NOT."
"Operator Precedence","LogicalVsBitwiseShortCircuit","Explain why 'x != 0 && 10/x > 1' is safe, but 'x != 0 & 10/x > 1' is not, when x is 0."
"Operator Precedence","TernaryAndAssignment","Predict the final value of x: 'int x = 10; x = x > 5 ? 1 : -1;'."
"Operator Precedence","VeryComplexExpression1","Predict 'int result = 100 / 10 * 2 + (10 % 3) - --x;' where x starts at 5."
"Operator Precedence","VeryComplexExpression2","Predict 'boolean result = x++ > 5 && y-- < 10 || z * 2 == 20;' given x=5, y=10, z=10."
"Logical Operators: AND","SimpleAND","Use the '&&' operator in an 'if' statement to check if an integer is both greater than 10 AND less than 20."
"Logical Operators: AND","LoginLogic","Write a condition that checks if a 'username' String is not empty AND a 'password' String has more than 8 characters."
"Logical Operators: AND","LeapYearComponent","Write a condition to check if a year is divisible by 4 AND not divisible by 100."
"Logical Operators: AND","ShortCircuitDemonstration","Create a condition 'x != 0 && 10 / x > 1'. Test it with x=0 to demonstrate short-circuiting (no error is thrown)."
"Logical Operators: AND","MultipleConditions","Check if a person is eligible for a senior discount: age >= 65 AND isCitizen == true."
"Logical Operators: AND","NullCheckAndMethodCall","Check if a String variable is not null AND its length is greater than 0, demonstrating safe method access."
"Logical Operators: AND","PointInRectangle","Check if a point (x, y) is inside a rectangle defined by (x1, y1) and (x2, y2). The condition would be 'x > x1 && x < x2 && y > y1 && y < y2'."
"Logical Operators: AND","AlphanumericCheck","Use Character methods to check if a char is a letter AND it is lowercase."
"Logical Operators: OR","SimpleOR","Use the '||' operator to check if a character is a vowel ('a' || 'e' || 'i' || 'o' || 'u')."
"Logical Operators: OR","WeekendCheck","Write a condition that checks if a 'dayOfWeek' String is equal to 'Saturday' OR 'Sunday'."
"Logical Operators: OR","AdminOrOwner","Use the '||' operator to grant access if a user's role is 'ADMIN' OR their username matches the 'owner' username."
"Logical Operators: OR","ShortCircuitDemonstrationOR","Create a condition 'isLoggedIn || attemptLogin()'. If 'isLoggedIn' is true, the 'attemptLogin()' method should not be called."
"Logical Operators: OR","OutsideARange","Write a condition to check if a temperature is dangerous, i.e., less than 0 OR greater than 100."
"Logical Operators: OR","InvalidInputOR","Check if an input string is invalid if it's null OR it's empty."
"Logical Operators: OR","ShippingDestination","Allow shipping if the destination is 'USA' OR 'Canada' OR 'Mexico'."
"Logical Operators: NOT","SimpleNOT","Use the '!' operator to check if a boolean 'isGameOver' is false."
"Logical Operators: NOT","NegateAnExpression","Use the '!' operator with parentheses to negate a complex expression, e.g. '!(age > 18 && hasLicense)'."
"Logical Operators: NOT","CheckForNonEmptyString","Use '!myString.isEmpty()' as a condition in an 'if' statement to proceed only if a string has content."
"Logical Operators: NOT","ToggleBoolean","Toggle the value of a boolean flag using the statement 'myFlag = !myFlag;'."
"Logical Operators: NOT","NotEqualTo","Explain the difference between using '!=' for primitives and using '!.equals()' for objects like Strings."
"Logical Operators: NOT","FlippingAFlag","In a loop, if a condition is met, flip a boolean 'found' from false to true using 'found = !found;'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","AND and OR Precedence","Write a condition 'a || b && c'. Explain which operator is evaluated first and how parentheses can change the meaning."
"Logical Operators: Combined","ComplexRangeCheck","Check if a number is within the range 10-20 OR the range 50-60 using both '&&' and '||'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","TicketEligibility","A person can buy a ticket if they have enough money AND (they are an adult OR they are accompanied by a guardian)."
"Logical Operators: Combined","DeMorgansLaw","Demonstrate De Morgan's Law: show that '!(A && B)' is equivalent to '!A || !B' using boolean variables."
"Logical Operators: Combined","LoopContinuation","Use a 'while' loop that continues as long as 'triesLeft > 0 && !isCorrectGuess'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","ValidInputCheck","Write a condition that checks if user input is NOT null AND is NOT empty."
"Logical Operators: Combined","ThreePartCheck","Check if an order can be shipped: 'inStock && !isInternationalShipping || hasSpecialPermit'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","ExclusiveOR(XOR)","Simulate an XOR operation using other logical operators: '(a && !b) || (!a && b)'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","FileAccessLogic","Check if a file can be read: 'fileExists && !isLocked && hasReadPermission'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","PasswordValidation","Write a condition to check if a password is valid: length > 8 AND contains a number AND contains an uppercase letter."
"Logical Operators: Combined","SimplifyNestedIf","Rewrite a nested 'if' statement into a single 'if' statement using the '&&' operator."
"Logical Operators: Combined","TernaryWithLogic","Use the ternary operator with a logical expression, e.g. 'String message = (userIsAdmin && isProduction) ? "" : ""'."
"Logical Operators: Combined","ReturnBooleanExpression","Write a method that directly returns the result of a logical expression, e.g. 'return age >= 18 && hasID;'."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","BitwiseVsLogicalAND","Use both '&' and '&&' in a condition. Explain the difference in their behavior, especially regarding short-circuiting."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","BitwiseVsLogicalOR","Use both '|' and '||' in a condition. Explain the difference, showing how the bitwise version does not short-circuit."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","BitwiseXOR","Use the bitwise XOR operator '^' to check if exactly one of two boolean conditions is true."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","DeMorgansLawPart2","Demonstrate the other part of De Morgan's Law: show that '!(A || B)' is equivalent to '!A && !B'."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","RedundantCondition","Analyze the expression '(age > 18 || age > 21)' and explain why part of it is redundant."
"Logical Operators: Advanced","ContradictoryCondition","Analyze the expression '(x < 10 && x > 20)' and explain why it will always evaluate to false."
"Conditionals: if","CheckForPositiveNumber","Write a program with an 'if' statement that prints 'The number is positive.' if an integer variable is greater than 0."
"Conditionals: if","IsEvenCheck","Use an 'if' statement and the modulo operator (%) to print 'The number is even.' if an integer is even."
"Conditionals: if","PasswordLengthCheck","Write an 'if' statement that checks if a String's length is greater than 8 and prints a confirmation message."
"Conditionals: if","CheckForEmptyString","Use an 'if' statement to check if a String is empty using the '.isEmpty()' method."
"Conditionals: if","TemperatureWarning","If a 'double' variable for temperature is above 30.0, use an 'if' statement to print a heat warning."
"Conditionals: if-else","OddOrEven","Use an 'if-else' statement to print whether a given integer is 'Odd' or 'Even'."
"Conditionals: if-else","PassOrFail","Given a score, use an 'if-else' statement to print 'Pass' if the score is 50 or above, and 'Fail' otherwise."
"Conditionals: if-else","LoginSuccess","Simulate a login. If a boolean 'isLoggedIn' is true, print 'Welcome!', else print 'Please log in.'."
"Conditionals: if-else","AdultOrMinor","Use an 'if-else' statement to determine if a person is an 'Adult' (18 or older) or a 'Minor'."
"Conditionals: if-else","InStockOrOutOfStock","Based on an integer 'stockCount', use 'if-else' to print 'In Stock' if the count is positive, otherwise 'Out of Stock'."
"Conditionals: if-else-if","GradeClassifier","Use an 'if-else-if-else' ladder to classify a score into grades: A (>90), B (80-89), C (70-79), D (60-69), F (<60)."
"Conditionals: if-else-if","NumberSignClassifier","Use 'if-else-if-else' to determine if a number is 'Positive', 'Negative', or 'Zero'."
"Conditionals: if-else-if","SeasonDetector","Given a month number (1-12), use an 'if-else-if' ladder to determine the season (e.g. Winter for 12, 1, 2)."
"Conditionals: if-else-if","InternetSpeed","Classify internet speed: <10 Mbps is 'Slow', 10-100 is 'Average', >100 is 'Fast'."
"Conditionals: if-else-if","TriangleType","Given three side lengths, use 'if-else-if' to determine if a triangle is 'Equilateral', 'Isosceles', or 'Scalene'."
"Conditionals: switch","DayOfTheWeek","Use a 'switch' statement with an integer (1-7) to print the corresponding day of the week."
"Conditionals: switch","VowelOrConsonant","Use a 'switch' statement with a 'char' to determine if it's a vowel (a, e, i, o, u) or a consonant."
"Conditionals: switch","SwitchWithDefault","Re-create the DayOfTheWeek exercise, but add a 'default' case to handle invalid numbers."
"Conditionals: switch","TrafficLight","Use a 'switch' statement on a String ('RED', 'YELLOW', 'GREEN') to print the appropriate action ('Stop', 'Caution', 'Go')."
"Conditionals: switch","FallThroughBehavior","Create a 'switch' statement for a month number. Group cases for the same season together using fall-through (no 'break')."
"Conditionals: switch","Java14SwitchExpressions","(Advanced) If using Java 14+, rewrite the DayOfTheWeek exercise using the new arrow syntax for switch expressions."
"Conditionals: switch","MenuSelection","Use a 'switch' statement to handle user input for a simple text menu (e.g. 1 for 'New Game', 2 for 'Load Game')."
"Conditionals: nested if","NestedAgeAndLicense","Use a nested 'if' to check if a person is 18 or older, and if so, check a boolean to see if they have a driver's license."
"Conditionals: nested if","NestedPermissions","Check if a user is an 'Admin'. If they are, use a nested 'if' to check if they are trying to access a 'secure' area."
"Conditionals: nested if","LeapYearLogic","Use nested 'if' statements to determine if a year is a leap year. (Divisible by 4, but not by 100 unless also divisible by 400)."
"Conditionals: logical operators","LogicalAND","Use 'if' with the '&&' operator to check if a number is both greater than 10 AND less than 100."
"Conditionals: logical operators","LogicalOR","Use 'if' with the '||' operator to check if a character is an uppercase letter OR a lowercase letter."
"Conditionals: logical operators","LogicalNOT","Use 'if' with the '!' operator to check if a boolean variable 'isGameOver' is false."
"Conditionals: logical operators","WeekendCheck","Use the '||' operator to check if a day of the week string is equal to 'Saturday' or 'Sunday'."
"Conditionals: logical operators","ValidRange","Combine '&&' and '||' to check if a number is within the range 1-10 OR the range 90-100."
"Conditionals: ternary operator","TernaryOddOrEven","Use the ternary operator to assign the string 'Even' or 'Odd' to a variable based on an integer's value."
"Conditionals: ternary operator","TernaryPassOrFail","Use the ternary operator to set a 'result' string to 'Pass' or 'Fail' based on a score."
"Conditionals: ternary operator","TernaryAbsoluteValue","Use the ternary operator to calculate the absolute value of a number."
"Conditionals: ternary operator","TernaryDiscount","A customer gets a 10% discount if they are a member. Use the ternary operator to calculate the final price."
"Conditionals: ternary operator","TernaryInPrintStatement","Use the ternary operator directly inside a 'System.out.println()' statement to print one of two messages."
"Conditionals: combined","ComplexValidation","Write a condition that checks if an age is >= 18 AND a boolean 'hasLicense' is true, OR if an age is >= 16 AND a boolean 'hasPermit' is true."
"Conditionals: combined","ShippingCost","Calculate shipping cost. If price > $50, cost is 0. Else, if 'isExpressShipping' is true, cost is $10, otherwise it's $5."
"Conditionals: combined","ComparingStrings","Use '.equals()' inside an 'if' statement to compare two strings for equality, not the '==' operator."
"Conditionals: combined","NullCheck","Before calling a method on a String object, use an 'if' statement to check that the object reference is not 'null'."
"Conditionals: combined","CharacterTypeCheck","Use 'if-else-if' with methods from the 'Character' class to check if a char is a digit, a letter, or whitespace."
"Autoboxing","PrimitiveToWrapper","Assign an 'int' primitive directly to an 'Integer' reference variable to demonstrate basic autoboxing."
"Autoboxing","WrapperToPrimitive","Assign an 'Integer' object directly to an 'int' primitive variable to demonstrate basic unboxing."
"Autoboxing","AutoboxingInArrayList","Create an 'ArrayList<Integer>' and add several 'int' primitives to it. Explain how autoboxing makes this possible."
"Autoboxing","UnboxingFromArrayList","Retrieve an element from the 'ArrayList<Integer>' from the previous exercise and assign it to an 'int' primitive."
"Autoboxing","UnboxingInArithmetic","Declare an 'Integer' object and a 'Double' object. Add them together and store the result in a 'double' primitive, relying on unboxing."
"Autoboxing","NullPointerExceptionRisk","Create an 'Integer' reference and set it to 'null'. Attempt to assign it to an 'int' primitive to trigger and explain the 'NullPointerException'."
"Autoboxing","MethodParameterBoxing","Create a method that accepts an 'Integer' parameter. Call this method by passing an 'int' primitive to it."
"Autoboxing","MethodReturnUnboxing","Create a method that returns an 'Integer' object. Call this method and assign the result directly to an 'int' primitive."
"Autoboxing","BooleanAutoboxing","Assign a primitive 'boolean' value directly to a 'Boolean' reference variable."
"Autoboxing","CharacterAutoboxing","Add a primitive 'char' to an 'ArrayList<Character>' to show autoboxing with the 'char' type."
"Autoboxing","EqualityVsIdentity","Create two 'Integer' objects by autoboxing the value 100. Compare them using both '==' and '.equals()' and explain the result."
"Autoboxing","EqualityVsIdentityCached","Repeat the previous exercise, but use the value 200. Explain why the result of the '==' comparison might be different."
"Autoboxing","IntegerCacheExplained","In a comment, explain the range of values that Java caches for 'Integer' objects and how it affects the '==' operator."
"Autoboxing","PerformanceConsideration","Create a loop that runs a million times, adding 'long' primitives to an 'ArrayList<Long>'. Discuss the performance overhead of autoboxing in this scenario."
"Autoboxing","UnboxingForSwitch","Use a 'Character' wrapper object in a 'switch' statement, demonstrating the implicit unboxing that occurs."
"Autoboxing","IncrementingAWrapper","Declare an 'Integer' variable initialized to 0. Use the increment operator (++) on it inside a loop and explain what happens behind the scenes."
"Autoboxing","MixedTypeUnboxing","Add an 'Integer' and a 'short' primitive. Explain how both unboxing and numeric promotion work together."
"Autoboxing","AutoboxingInTernary","Use the ternary operator to assign either an 'int' literal or another 'int' literal to a 'Double' reference. Explain the conversions."
"Autoboxing","RemoveFromList","Create an 'ArrayList<Integer>' with numbers 1-10. Try to remove the number 5 by passing the 'int' primitive 5 to the 'remove()' method. Explain the behavior."
"Autoboxing","FixingRemoveFromList","Fix the previous exercise by passing an 'Integer' object to the 'remove()' method instead of a primitive."
"Autoboxing","AutoboxingAndOverloading","Create a class with two overloaded methods, one taking an 'int' and one an 'Integer'. Call the method with an 'int' and predict which version will be called."
"Autoboxing","UnboxingAndCasting","Assign a 'Double' object to an 'int' primitive. Explain why this requires both an explicit cast and unboxing."
"Autoboxing","AutoboxingInMaps","Create a 'HashMap<String, Integer>' and use 'put()' to add entries using 'int' primitives for the values."
"Autoboxing","WhenToAvoid","Write a short paragraph describing a scenario where you should prefer using primitive types over their wrapper classes to avoid performance issues."
"Primitive Type Conversion","WideningIntToLong","Declare an 'int' variable and assign it to a 'long' variable. Print both to show the implicit conversion."
"Primitive Type Conversion","WideningIntToDouble","Declare an 'int' variable and assign it to a 'double' variable. Print the double to see the added decimal part."
"Primitive Type Conversion","WideningFloatToDouble","Declare a 'float' and assign its value to a 'double'. Explain why this is a widening conversion."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NarrowingDoubleToInt","Declare a 'double' with a decimal value (e.g. 123.45). Explicitly cast it to an 'int' and print the result to observe the truncation."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NarrowingLongToInt","Declare a 'long' with a value that fits in an 'int'. Cast it to an 'int' and print. Then, try with a 'long' that is too large and observe the data loss."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NarrowingIntToByte","Declare an 'int' with the value 130. Cast it to a 'byte' and print the result to see how the value wraps around."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NarrowingDoubleToFloat","Declare a 'double' variable. Explicitly cast it to a 'float' and discuss the potential loss of precision."
"Primitive Type Conversion","CharToIntConversion","Declare a 'char' variable with the value 'A'. Assign it to an 'int' variable and print the integer to see its ASCII value."
"Primitive Type Conversion","IntToCharConversion","Declare an 'int' with the value 97. Cast it to a 'char' and print the result to see the corresponding character."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NumericPromotionByte","Add two 'byte' variables together and try to store the result in a 'byte' variable. Fix the compiler error by storing the result in an 'int'."
"Primitive Type Conversion","NumericPromotionShort","Multiply two 'short' variables. Explain why the result is promoted to an 'int' by the Java compiler."
"Primitive Type Conversion","MixedTypeIntAndDouble","Add an 'int' and a 'double'. Store the result in a variable of the appropriate type and print it."
"Primitive Type Conversion","MixedTypeLongAndFloat","Multiply a 'long' and a 'float'. Determine the resulting data type and store the product accordingly."
"Primitive Type Conversion","ComplexExpressionType","Write a complex expression involving at least three different primitive types (e.g. (byte + short) * int / double). Determine the final data type of the result."
"Primitive Type Conversion","StringToInteger","Use 'Integer.parseInt()' to convert a string containing a number (e.g. ""250"") into an 'int' primitive."
"Primitive Type Conversion","StringToDouble","Use 'Double.parseDouble()' to convert a string containing a decimal number (e.g. ""99.5"") into a 'double' primitive."
"Primitive Type Conversion","StringToBoolean","Use 'Boolean.parseBoolean()' to convert the string ""true"" into a 'boolean' primitive."
"Primitive Type Conversion","HandleNumberFormatException","Wrap a call to 'Integer.parseInt()' in a try-catch block to handle the 'NumberFormatException' that occurs when parsing a non-numeric string."
"Primitive Type Conversion","IntToStringConcat","Convert an 'int' to a 'String' by concatenating it with an empty string (e.g. '' + 100)."
"Primitive Type Conversion","DoubleToStringValueOf","Convert a 'double' to a 'String' using the 'String.valueOf()' method."
"Primitive Type Conversion","BooleanToString","Convert a 'boolean' variable to a 'String' and print its value."
"Primitive Type Conversion","IllegalCast","Try to cast a 'boolean' to an 'int'. Observe and explain the compiler error."
"Primitive Type Conversion","IllegalObjectCast","Try to cast a 'String' object to an 'int' using '(int)'. Explain why this is a compile-time error and different from parsing."
"Primitive Type Conversion","TernaryOperatorTypes","Use the ternary operator with an 'int' and a 'double' as the possible results (e.g. 'true ? 10 : 20.0'). Determine the data type of the result."
"Primitive Types: byte","DeclareByte","Declare a 'byte' variable to store the number of planets in our solar system and print it."
"Primitive Types: byte","ByteMinMax","Print the minimum and maximum values a 'byte' can hold using the 'Byte.MIN_VALUE' and 'Byte.MAX_VALUE' constants."
"Primitive Types: byte","ByteOverflow","Assign 'Byte.MAX_VALUE' to a byte variable. Add 1 to it, store the result in another byte variable, and print it to observe the overflow."
"Primitive Types: byte","ByteUnderflow","Assign 'Byte.MIN_VALUE' to a byte variable. Subtract 1 from it and print the result to observe the underflow."
"Primitive Types: short","DeclareShort","Declare a 'short' variable to store the number of days in a year and print it."
"Primitive Types: short","ShortArithmetic","Create two 'short' variables. Add them together and try to store the result in a 'short' variable. Observe the compiler error and fix it by casting."
"Primitive Types: int","DeclareInt","Declare an 'int' variable to store the height of Mount Everest in meters (8848) and print it."
"Primitive Types: int","IntegerDivision","Divide 10 by 3 using integer variables and print the result to see how the decimal part is truncated."
"Primitive Types: int","IntegerWrapperMethods","Use the 'Integer.parseInt()' method to convert the string ""123"" into an 'int' primitive."
"Primitive Types: long","DeclareLong","Declare a 'long' variable to store the approximate age of the Earth in years (4,543,000,000). Remember to use the 'L' suffix."
"Primitive Types: long","LongForTimestamps","Use 'System.currentTimeMillis()' to get the current time as a 'long' and print it."
"Primitive Types: long","PreventingOverflow","Multiply two large integers that would overflow an 'int', but store the result in a 'long' to get the correct value (e.g. 100000 * 100000)."
"Primitive Types: float","DeclareFloat","Declare a 'float' variable to store the value of Pi. Remember to use the 'f' suffix."
"Primitive Types: float","FloatPrecisionIssue","Add 0.1f to itself 10 times in a loop. Print the result and observe the small precision error."
"Primitive Types: float","FloatVsDouble","Declare the same fractional number (e.g. 1/3) as both a 'float' and a 'double'. Print both to compare their precision."
"Primitive Types: double","DeclareDouble","Declare a 'double' variable to store a person's precise height in meters (e.g. 1.82)."
"Primitive Types: double","DoubleForCalculations","Calculate the area of a circle with a radius of 7.5 units. Use 'double' variables for the radius, Pi, and the resulting area."
"Primitive Types: double","SpecialDoubleValues","Divide a positive double by 0.0 and a negative double by 0.0 to produce and print 'Infinity' and '-Infinity'."
"Primitive Types: char","DeclareCharLiteral","Declare a 'char' variable to store your first initial using single quotes."
"Primitive Types: char","DeclareCharUnicode","Declare a 'char' variable to store the Greek letter omega using its Unicode escape sequence '\\u03A9'."
"Primitive Types: char","CharAsInteger","Assign the integer 65 to a 'char' variable and print the result. Then, cast the character 'a' to an 'int' and print its value."
"Primitive Types: char","CharacterWrapperMethods","Use the 'Character.isDigit()' and 'Character.isLetter()' methods to check if a 'char' variable holds a number or a letter."
"Primitive Types: boolean","DeclareBoolean","Declare a 'boolean' variable named 'isJavaStaticallyTyped' and initialize it to 'true'."
"Primitive Types: boolean","BooleanExpression","Write a boolean expression that checks if an 'int' variable 'age' is greater than or equal to 18. Store the result in a 'boolean' variable."
"Primitive Types: boolean","BooleanOperators","Declare two boolean variables. Use the AND (&&) and OR (||) operators to combine them and print the results."
"Primitive Types: boolean","ToggleAFlag","Declare a boolean variable 'isLightOn' set to true. Use the NOT (!) operator to toggle its value to false."
"For Loop","CountToOneHundred","Use a standard for loop to print the numbers from 1 to 100, each on a new line."
"For Loop","EvenNumbers","Use a for loop and an if statement to print all the even numbers between 1 and 50."
"For Loop","CountdownFromTen","Write a for loop that counts down from 10 to 1 and prints 'Liftoff!' at the end."
"For Loop","SumOfFirstN","Use a for loop to calculate the sum of the first 100 positive integers and print the result."
"For Loop","MultiplicationTable","Use nested for loops to print a 10x10 multiplication table."
"For Loop","IterateStringChars","Use a for loop to iterate through the characters of a String and print each character on a new line."
"While Loop","GuessTheNumber","Create a 'guess the number' game that uses a while loop to continue until the user guesses the correct number."
"While Loop","InputValidation","Use a while loop to repeatedly prompt a user for their age until they enter a value between 0 and 120."
"While Loop","SentinelControlledSum","Write a program that uses a while loop to read numbers from the user until they enter -1, then prints the sum of all numbers entered."
"While Loop","PowerOfTwo","Use a while loop to find the first power of 2 that is greater than 1000."
"While Loop","ReverseAnInteger","Use a while loop to reverse the digits of an integer (e.g. 12345 becomes 54321)."
"While Loop","SimpleMenuLoop","Create a text-based menu that loops with a while loop, asking for user input until they select the 'exit' option."
"Do-While Loop","RunOnceGuarantee","Create a do-while loop where the condition is initially false. Print a message inside the loop to demonstrate that it always executes at least once."
"Do-While Loop","MenuWithDoWhile","Re-implement the menu from the while loop section, this time using a do-while loop, which is often a more natural fit for menus."
"Do-While Loop","PasswordPrompt","Use a do-while loop to prompt a user for a password. The loop should continue until they enter the correct password."
"Do-While Loop","ConfirmExit","Run a simple task and then use a do-while loop to ask the user 'Do you want to run it again? [y/n]'. The loop continues as long as they type 'y'."
"Do-While Loop","DiceRollUntilSix","Simulate rolling a six-sided die using a do-while loop. The loop should continue until a 6 is rolled, and you should print each roll."
"Do-While Loop","ReadUntilPositive","Use a do-while loop to read an integer from the user, guaranteeing the loop runs at least once, and continue looping while the number is not positive."
"For-Each Loop","IterateStringArray","Create an array of your favorite book titles (as Strings). Use a for-each loop to print each title."
"For-Each Loop","SumIntegerArray","Use a for-each loop to calculate and print the sum of all the elements in an integer array."
"For-Each Loop","FindMaximumValue","Use a for-each loop to find the largest number in an array of integers."
"For-Each Loop","PrintArrayList","Create an ArrayList of Doubles and add some values. Use a for-each loop to print every element in the list."
"For-Each Loop","ConcatenateStrings","Given an array of words, use a for-each loop to build a single sentence String from them."
"For-Each Loop","ReadOnlyLimitation","In a comment, explain why a for-each loop is considered 'read-only' and cannot be used to modify the elements of the collection it is iterating over."
"Getters and Setters","BasicEncapsulation","Create a 'Person' class with a private 'name' field and public 'getName()' and 'setName()' methods."
"Getters and Setters","ReadOnlyProperty","Create a 'Student' class with a private final 'studentId' field, initialized in the constructor, and provide only a getter for it."
"Getters and Setters","ValidationInSetter","In a 'Product' class, create a 'setPrice()' method for a private 'price' field that only allows positive values to be set."
"Getters and Setters","BooleanGetterConvention","Create an 'Item' class with a private boolean 'isAvailable' field. Implement the getter using the 'isAvailable()' naming convention."
"Getters and Setters","CalculatedProperty","Create a 'Rectangle' class with private 'width' and 'height' fields. Create a 'getArea()' method that calculates and returns the area without a corresponding 'area' field."
"Getters and Setters","RefactorPublicFields","Given a class with public fields, rewrite it to use private fields and the proper getter and setter methods."
"Getters and Setters","WhyEncapsulate","Write a short paragraph explaining why using private fields with public getters/setters is better than using public fields."
"Getters and Setters","UsingThisKeyword","In a setter method, name the parameter the same as the field and use the 'this' keyword to distinguish between them."
"Getters and Setters","ImmutableClass","Create an immutable 'Color' class with private final fields for red, green, and blue values. Provide only getters."
"Getters and Setters","SetterWithLogic","Create a 'Temperature' class where 'setCelsius()' not only sets the Celsius value but also calculates and updates a private 'fahrenheit' field."
"Getters and Setters","NullCheckInSetter","Create a 'Book' class with a private 'title' field. The 'setTitle()' method should not allow a null value to be assigned."
"Getters and Setters","DefensiveCopyingGetter","Create a class that holds a private 'ArrayList<String>'. The getter should return a new copy of the list, not the original reference."
"Getters and Setters","DefensiveCopyingSetter","For the class in the previous exercise, the setter should create a new 'ArrayList' from the incoming list to store internally."
"Getters and Setters","FluentInterface","Modify the setter methods in your 'Person' class to return 'this' (the current object instance) to allow for method chaining."
"Getters and Setters","UsingGettersInternally","Create a method inside your 'Person' class called 'printDetails()' that uses its own 'getName()' method to print the person's details."
"Getters and Setters","WriteOnlyProperty","Create a 'Password' class with a private 'hashedPassword' field. Provide a 'setPassword()' method that takes a plain string, hashes it, and stores it, but provide no getter."
"Getters and Setters","IDEGeneration","Use your IDE's built-in functionality to automatically generate getters and setters for a class with several private fields."
"Getters and Setters","ToStringWithGetters","Implement the 'toString()' method for one of your classes, using the getter methods to build the descriptive string."
"Getters and Setters","LazyInitialization","Create a class with a private, complex object field. In the getter, check if the field is null, and if it is, create and initialize the object before returning it."
"Getters and Setters","GettersAndInheritance","Create a 'Manager' subclass of 'Employee'. Show that the 'Manager' class can use the public getters/setters from 'Employee' but cannot directly access its private fields."
"Getters and Setters","SetterForEnum","Create a class with a private enum field for 'Status' (e.g. PENDING, ACTIVE, INACTIVE). The setter should only accept valid 'Status' enum constants."
"Getters and Setters","GetterForArray","Create a class with a private String array. The getter should return a copy of the array using 'clone()'."
"Getters and Setters","SetterForArray","Create a setter for the class in the previous exercise. It should also store a clone of the incoming array."
"Getters and Setters","TradeOffsDiscussion","In a comment, discuss a potential downside of automatically providing a public getter and setter for every private field in a class."
"Polymorphism","BasicMethodOverriding","Create a 'Vehicle' superclass with a 'drive()' method. Create a 'Car' subclass that overrides 'drive()' to print 'Driving a car.'."
"Polymorphism","SuperclassReference","Create an object of the 'Car' class from the previous exercise, but store it in a 'Vehicle' reference variable. Call the 'drive()' method."
"Polymorphism","PolymorphicArray","Create an array of 'Vehicle' type that holds both 'Vehicle' and 'Car' objects. Iterate through the array and call the 'drive()' method on each element."
"Polymorphism","AbstractShapeClass","Create an abstract class 'Shape' with an abstract method 'calculateArea()'. Create 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' subclasses that implement this method."
"Polymorphism","InterfacePolymorphism","Create an interface 'Drawable' with a 'draw()' method. Have 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' classes implement this interface. Create a 'Drawable' reference to a 'Circle' object."
"Polymorphism","MethodOverloadingBasics","Create a class 'Calculator' with two 'add' methods: one that takes two integers and another that takes two doubles."
"Polymorphism","OverloadingWithDifferentTypes","In the 'Calculator' class, add another 'add' method that takes three integers."
"Polymorphism","InstanceOfOperator","In your polymorphic 'Vehicle' array, use the 'instanceof' operator to check if an object is a 'Car' before calling a 'Car'-specific method (e.g. 'openTrunk()')."
"Polymorphism","DowncastingExample","From the previous exercise, if an object is an instance of 'Car', downcast the 'Vehicle' reference to a 'Car' reference to call the 'openTrunk()' method."
"Polymorphism","AbstractClassConstructor","Add a constructor to your abstract 'Shape' class that takes a color. Call this constructor from the 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' subclasses using 'super()'."
"Polymorphism","ZooAnimalHierarchy","Create a superclass 'Animal' with a 'makeSound()' method. Create subclasses like 'Dog', 'Cat', and 'Cow' that override this method to make their specific sounds."
"Polymorphism","PolymorphismWithInterfaces","Create an interface 'Playable' with a 'play()' method. Create classes 'Guitar' and 'Piano' that implement it. Create a method that accepts any 'Playable' object."
"Polymorphism","FinalMethodRestriction","Add a 'final' method to the 'Vehicle' class. Attempt to override this method in the 'Car' subclass and observe the compiler error."
"Polymorphism","OverridingToString","Override the 'toString()' method in your 'Car' class to return a descriptive string about the car (e.g. its make and model)."
"Polymorphism","PolymorphismInCollections","Create an ArrayList of 'Shape' and add 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' objects to it. Loop through the list and print the area of each shape."
"Polymorphism","DynamicMethodDispatch","Create a 'Person' class and a 'Student' subclass that overrides a 'greet()' method. Demonstrate that the method called depends on the object's actual type at runtime, not the reference type."
"Polymorphism","InterfaceDefaultMethods","Add a default method to your 'Drawable' interface. Show that 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' objects can call this method without implementing it."
"Polymorphism","StaticVsDynamicBinding","Create a class with a static method and a non-static method. Create a subclass that attempts to 'override' both. Demonstrate the difference in how they are called."
"Polymorphism","AbstractVsInterface","Create an abstract class 'Appliance' with state (e.g. 'isOn') and an abstract method. Create an interface 'Switchable'. Discuss when you would use one over the other."
"Polymorphism","PolymorphicParameters","Create a method 'printShapeDetails' that accepts a 'Shape' object as a parameter. Call this method with both 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' objects."
"Polymorphism","ConstructorOverloading","Create a 'Book' class with multiple constructors: one default, one that takes a title, and one that takes a title and author."
"Polymorphism","AvoidingClassCastException","Write code that attempts to downcast a 'Vehicle' object to a 'Car' object without first checking with 'instanceof', and wrap it in a try-catch block to handle the 'ClassCastException'."
"Polymorphism","BenefitsOfPolymorphism","Write a short paragraph explaining how using a superclass reference for subclass objects (polymorphism) simplifies code, for example, when adding a new 'Motorcycle' subclass."
"Polymorphism","CovariantReturnTypes","In your 'Vehicle' class, have a method that returns a 'Vehicle' object. In the 'Car' subclass, override this method to return a 'Car' object."
"Introduction Java Programming",Hello World,"Write a program that prints 'Hello World!'to the console."
"Introduction Java Programming",Hello World Variation,"Write a program that prints 'Hello, [Your Name]!' to the console, where [Your Name] is a variable holding your name."
"Introduction Java Programming",Simple Calculator,"Create a program that takes two numbers as input and performs basic arithmetic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division)."
"Introduction Java Programming",Area of a Rectangle,"Calculate and display the area of a rectangle. The length and width should be stored in variables."
"Introduction Java Programming",Temperature Converter,"Convert a temperature from Celsius to Fahrenheit. The formula is F = (C * 9/5) + 32."
"Introduction Java Programming",Age in Days,"Write a program that takes a user's age in years and calculates their approximate age in days."
"Introduction Java Programming",Simple Interest Calculator,"Calculate simple interest given principal, rate, and time. The formula is SI = (P * R * T) / 100."
"Introduction Java Programming",Quotient and Remainder,"Find the quotient and remainder of two integers."
"Introduction Java Programming",Swap Two Numbers,"Write a program to swap the values of two variables without using a temporary variable."
"Introduction Java Programming",Even or Odd,"Check if a given number is even or odd and print the result."
"Introduction Java Programming",Vowel or Consonant,"Check if a given character is a vowel or a consonant."
"Introduction Java Programming",Largest of Three Numbers,"Find the largest among three numbers using conditional statements."
"Introduction Java Programming",Leap Year Checker,"Determine if a given year is a leap year. A year is a leap year if it is divisible by 4, except for end-of-century years, which must be divisible by 400."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Keyword Identifier,"Write a program that declares variables using at least five different Java keywords. Add comments to explain the purpose of each variable."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Identifier Naming Conventions,"Create a program with variables that demonstrate both good and bad identifier naming conventions. Use comments to explain why certain names are good or bad."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Literal Showcase,"Declare variables of different data types and initialize them with various literals (integer, floating-point, character, string, boolean)."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Comment Types,"Write a program that includes single-line, multi-line, and documentation comments to explain different parts of the code."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Circle Calculations,"Create a program to calculate the circumference and area of a circle. Use identifiers for the radius and pi, and a literal for the value of pi."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Book Information,"Declare variables to store information about a book: title (String), author (String), publication year (int), and price (double). Use meaningful identifiers."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Student Grades,"Create a program that stores a student's name and their grades in three subjects. Use appropriate identifiers and literals."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Escape Sequence Practice,"Write a program that uses various escape sequences in a string literal to format the output (e.g. newline, tab, backslash)."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Final Keyword Example,"Declare a constant using the 'final' keyword and attempt to reassign it to demonstrate that it's a compile-time error. Use comments to explain."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Boolean Logic,"Declare boolean variables and initialize them with boolean literals. Perform logical operations and print the results."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Character Literals,"Declare character variables and initialize them with different character literals, including Unicode escape sequences."
"Keywords identifiers literals comments",Null Literal,"Declare an object reference variable and initialize it to the null literal. Add a comment explaining what a null reference means."
"Data Types",Data Type Ranges,"Write a program that prints the minimum and maximum values for each primitive data type (byte, short, int, long, float, double)."
"Data Types",Type Conversion,"Declare a variable of each primitive data type and try to assign it to every other primitive data type to observe which conversions are implicit and which require explicit casting."
"Data Types",Character to Integer,"Declare a character variable and assign it a letter. Then, assign the character variable to an integer variable and print the integer value to see its ASCII representation."
"Data Types",Floating-Point Precision,"Declare float and double variables with the same fractional value. Perform a calculation and observe the difference in precision."
"Data Types",Boolean Flags,"Create a program that uses boolean variables as flags to control the flow of execution in an if-else statement."
"Data Types",Scientific Notation,"Declare a double variable and initialize it using scientific notation (e.g. 1.23e4). Print the value to the console."
"Data Types",Long for Large Numbers,"Use a long data type to store and calculate the factorial of a number like 20, which would overflow an int."
"Data Types",Short for Memory Saving,"Imagine a scenario where memory is limited. Declare an array of 'short' to store a large number of values that fit within its range, and comment on the memory savings compared to 'int'."
"Data Types",Byte for File I/O,"Simulate reading a byte from a file by declaring a byte variable and assigning it a value between -128 and 127."
"Data Types",Primitive vs. Wrapper,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer wrapper class object. Demonstrate autoboxing and unboxing by assigning between them."
"Data Types",Default Values,"Declare instance variables of each primitive data type in a class but do not initialize them. Create an object of the class and print the default values of these variables."
"Data Types",Data Type Mismatch Error,"Write a program that intentionally tries to assign a value of a larger data type to a smaller data type without casting and observe the compiler error. Comment on the reason for the error."
"Variables",Variable Scope,"Create a class with a global variable, a local variable inside a method, and a block-level variable inside a loop. Print the values of these variables to understand their scope."
"Variables",Variable Initialization,"Declare variables of different data types and initialize them at the time of declaration. Print their values."
"Variables",Variable Assignment,"Declare variables and then assign values to them in separate statements. Print their values."
"Variables",Variable Reassignment,"Declare a variable, assign it a value, print it, then reassign it a new value and print it again to show that variables can hold different values over time."
"Variables",Variable Lifetime,"Write a method that declares a local variable. Call this method multiple times and observe that the local variable is created and destroyed with each method call."
"Variables",Uninitialized Variable Error,"Declare a local variable but do not initialize it. Try to use it in an expression and observe the compiler error. Comment on why this happens."
"Variables",Static Variable Counter,"Create a class with a static variable that acts as a counter. Increment this counter every time a new object of the class is created. Print the counter's value to see how many objects have been created."
"Variables",Instance vs. Static Variables,"Create a class with both an instance variable and a static variable. Create multiple objects of the class, change the instance variable for one object, and change the static variable. Print the variables for all objects to see the difference."
"Variables",Final Variable,"Declare a final variable and initialize it. Try to reassign it a new value and observe the compiler error. Explain the concept of a constant."
"Variables",Naming Convention Practice,"Declare variables for a user's first name, last name, age, and isStudent status, following Java's naming conventions for variables."
"Variables",Type Inference with 'var',"If using Java 10 or later, declare a few local variables using the 'var' keyword and let the compiler infer the type. Print the class of each variable to confirm its type."
"Variables",Variable Shadowing,"Create a class with an instance variable named 'x'. In a method within that class, declare a local variable also named 'x'. Demonstrate how the local variable 'shadows' the instance variable."
"Primitive Types",Primitive Operations,"Write a program that declares variables of each primitive data type (byte, short, int, long, float, double, boolean, char) and performs a basic operation on each (e.g. addition for numbers, negation for boolean)."
"Primitive Types",Integer Division and Remainder,"Declare two int variables and perform division and modulus operations. Print the results to understand how integer division works."
"Primitive Types",Floating-Point Arithmetic,"Declare two double variables and perform addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division. Observe the results with decimal points."
"Primitive Types",Character Arithmetic,"Declare a char variable with a letter, then add an integer to it. Print the resulting character to see how character arithmetic works based on ASCII values."
"Primitive Types",Boolean Logic,"Declare two boolean variables and use them in expressions with logical AND (&&), OR (||), and NOT (!). Print the results."
"Primitive Types",Byte Overflow,"Declare a byte variable and assign it the maximum byte value. Then, add 1 to it and print the result to see the overflow behavior."
"Primitive Types",Long for Time,"Use a long variable to store the current time in milliseconds (using System.currentTimeMillis()) and print it."
"Primitive Types",Short Array,"Declare an array of type short to store the daily high temperatures for a week. Initialize and print the values."
"Primitive Types",Casting Primitives,"Declare an int and a double. Explicitly cast the double to an int and the int to a double. Print the results to see the effect of casting."
"Primitive Types",Char as a Number,"Declare a char variable with a digit (e.g. '5'). Subtract the char '0' from it to get the integer value of the digit."
"Primitive Types",Float vs. Double,"Declare a float and a double, both initialized to the same value. Compare them for equality and discuss potential precision issues with floats."
"Primitive Types",Default Primitive Values,"Create a class with instance variables of each primitive type. Do not initialize them. Create an object and print their default values."
"Wrapper Classes",Autoboxing and Unboxing,"Declare a primitive int and an Integer object. Demonstrate autoboxing by assigning the primitive to the object and unboxing by assigning the object to the primitive."
"Wrapper Classes",Wrapper Class Methods,"Use the Integer wrapper class to convert a string to an int (parseInt), an int to a string (toString), and to find the min/max of two numbers (min, max)."
"Wrapper Classes",ArrayList of Integers,"Create an ArrayList that can hold integers. Add some integers to it (demonstrating autoboxing) and then retrieve and print them (demonstrating unboxing)."
"Wrapper Classes",Null Wrapper Reference,"Declare a wrapper class variable (e.g. Double) and assign it the value null. Try to unbox it to a primitive double and observe the NullPointerException."
"Wrapper Classes",Character Wrapper Methods,"Use the Character wrapper class to check if a character is a digit (isDigit), a letter (isLetter), or whitespace (isWhitespace)."
"Wrapper Classes",Boolean Wrapper,"Use the Boolean wrapper class to parse a string ('true' or 'false') into a boolean value."
"Wrapper Classes",Comparing Wrapper Objects,"Create two Integer objects with the same value. Compare them using '==' and the '.equals()' method. Explain the difference in the output."
"Wrapper Classes",Wrapper Constants,"Print the values of constants like Integer.MAX_VALUE, Integer.MIN_VALUE, Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY, and Double.NaN."
"Wrapper Classes",Binary, Octal, Hex String,"Use the Integer wrapper class methods to convert an integer into its binary, octal, and hexadecimal string representations."
"Wrapper Classes",Parsing with a Radix,"Use the Integer.parseInt(String s, int radix) method to parse a binary string and a hexadecimal string into an integer."
"Wrapper Classes",Number Superclass,"Create a method that accepts a Number object (the superclass of all numeric wrapper classes). Pass in an Integer, a Double, and a Float to demonstrate polymorphism."
"Wrapper Classes",Custom Wrapper Method,"Create a utility class with a static method that takes an int array and returns an Integer array. This will require manual boxing in a loop."
"Expressions",Arithmetic Expression,"Write a program that evaluates a complex arithmetic expression involving addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, and modulus, using parentheses to control the order of operations."
"Expressions",Relational Expression,"Create expressions that use all the relational operators (==, !=, >, <, >=, <=) to compare two numbers. The result of each expression should be a boolean."
"Expressions",Logical Expression,"Write a program that uses logical operators (&&, ||, !) to combine multiple boolean expressions. For example, check if a number is between 1 and 100."
"Expressions",Bitwise Expression,"Use bitwise operators (&, |, ^, ~) on two integer variables and print the results in binary to understand their effect."
"Expressions",Assignment Expression,"Use compound assignment operators (+=, -=, *=, /=, %=) to modify the value of a variable."
"Expressions",Ternary Operator,"Use the ternary operator to find the minimum of two numbers and assign it to a variable in a single line."
"Expressions",Operator Precedence,"Write an expression without parentheses that relies on operator precedence (e.g. mixing * and +). Predict the result and then run the program to verify."
"Expressions",Type Casting in Expressions,"Create an expression that involves different numeric data types (e.g. int and double). Observe the implicit type promotion. Then, use explicit casting to change the result."
"Expressions",String Concatenation,"Write an expression that concatenates a string with a number. Observe how the number is automatically converted to a string."
"Expressions",Increment and Decrement,"Demonstrate the difference between pre-increment (++x) and post-increment (x++) operators in an expression."
"Expressions",Short-Circuiting Logical Operators,"Create a logical expression using && where the first operand is false. Use a method call as the second operand and show that the method is never called."
"Expressions",Instanceof Expression,"Create a simple class hierarchy and use the 'instanceof' operator to check if an object is an instance of a particular class or interface."
"Classes",Simple Class,"Define a 'Dog' class with attributes for name (String) and age (int), and a method 'bark()' that prints 'Woof!'."
"Classes",Class with Constructor,"Create a 'Person' class with attributes for name and age. Include a constructor to initialize these attributes when a new Person object is created."
"Classes",Class with Methods,"Define a 'Rectangle' class with attributes for length and width. Add methods to calculate the area and perimeter."
"Classes",Multiple Objects,"Create a 'Car' class. In your main method, create three different 'Car' objects, each with unique attributes (e.g. make, model, year)."
"Classes",Getters and Setters,"Design a 'Student' class with private attributes for student ID and GPA. Provide public getter and setter methods to access and modify these attributes."
"Classes",Static vs. Instance Members,"Create a 'Counter' class with a static variable to count the number of objects created and an instance variable to give each object a unique ID."
"Classes",Method Overloading,"In a 'Calculator' class, create multiple 'add' methods that can add two integers, two doubles, or three integers."
"Classes",The 'this' Keyword,"In a 'Book' class, use the 'this' keyword in the constructor to distinguish between instance variables and constructor parameters with the same name."
"Classes",Class with a Class Member,"Create an 'Author' class and a 'Book' class. The 'Book' class should have an 'Author' object as one of its attributes."
"Classes",toString Method,"In a 'Product' class with attributes for name and price, override the 'toString()' method to return a string representation of the product's details."
"Classes",Encapsulation Example,"Create a 'BankAccount' class with a private 'balance' attribute. Provide public methods for 'deposit' and 'withdraw' that include validation (e.g. cannot withdraw more than the balance)."
"Classes",Simple Circle Class,"Define a 'Circle' class with a 'radius' attribute. Include methods to calculate the diameter, circumference, and area."
"Objects",Object Creation,"Define a 'Lamp' class with a boolean attribute 'isOn'. In the main method, create two 'Lamp' objects, one representing a desk lamp and one a ceiling lamp."
"Objects",Accessing Attributes,"Create a 'Movie' class with public attributes for 'title' and 'director'. Create a 'Movie' object, set its attributes, and then print them."
"Objects",Calling Methods,"Create a 'TrafficLight' class with a method 'changeColor()'. Create a 'TrafficLight' object and call its 'changeColor()' method multiple times."
"Objects",Object as a Parameter,"Write a method that takes a 'Person' object as a parameter and prints that person's details."
"Objects",Object as a Return Type,"Create a method that creates and returns a new 'Car' object with default values."
"Objects",Array of Objects,"Create an array of 'Student' objects. Initialize each element of the array with a new 'Student' object and then loop through the array to print each student's name."
"Objects",Comparing Objects,"Create two 'Point' objects with x and y coordinates. Compare them using '==' and the '.equals()' method (you'll need to override .equals() for a meaningful comparison). Explain the difference."
"Objects",Null Reference,"Declare a 'Book' object reference but initialize it to 'null'. Try to call a method on this object and handle the resulting NullPointerException."
"Objects",Object State,"Create a 'Microwave' class with methods like 'start()', 'stop()', and 'setTime()'. Create a 'Microwave' object and call these methods to change its internal state."
"Objects",Garbage Collection,"Create a method where you instantiate a large number of objects inside a loop. After the method finishes, explain that these objects are now eligible for garbage collection."
"Objects",Anonymous Objects,"Call a method that requires an object as a parameter by creating an anonymous object directly in the method call, e.g. 'printDetails(new Person("John", 30));'."
"Objects",Object Cloning,"Implement the 'Cloneable' interface and override the 'clone()' method in a 'Course' class to create a copy of a 'Course' object."
"Classes and Objects",Library System,"Create 'Book' and 'Library' classes. The 'Library' class should have an array of 'Book' objects. Implement methods to add a book and display all books."
"Classes and Objects",Bank Account Management,"Create a 'BankAccount' class. In your main method, create an account, deposit money, withdraw money, and print the final balance."
"Classes and Objects",Student Roster,"Create a 'Student' class. Use an ArrayList to store multiple 'Student' objects. Write code to add a new student, find a student by ID, and remove a student."
"Classes and Objects",E-commerce Cart,"Design 'Product' and 'ShoppingCart' classes. The 'ShoppingCart' should be able to add 'Product' objects and calculate the total price."
"Classes and Objects",Dice Rolling Simulator,"Create a 'Die' class with a method to 'roll()' that returns a random number between 1 and 6. In your main method, create two 'Die' objects and roll them to simulate a dice game."
"Classes and Objects",Contact List,"Create a 'Contact' class with name and phone number. Create a program that acts as a contact list, allowing you to add and display 'Contact' objects."
"Classes and Objects",Simple Pet Simulator,"Create a 'Pet' class with attributes like hunger and happiness, and methods like 'feed()' and 'play()'. Create a 'Pet' object and interact with it."
"Classes and Objects",Car Factory,"Create a 'Car' class. Write a program that simulates a car factory by creating multiple 'Car' objects in a loop."
"Classes and Objects",Playlist Manager,"Design 'Song' and 'Playlist' classes. The 'Playlist' class should allow you to add 'Song' objects and display the list of songs."
"Classes and Objects",Rectangle Area Comparison,"Create a 'Rectangle' class. In your main method, create two 'Rectangle' objects and write code to determine which one has the larger area."
"Classes and Objects",Employee Payroll,"Create an 'Employee' class with attributes like name and hourly wage. Write a program to calculate the weekly pay for an employee object, given the hours worked."
"Classes and Objects",Point Distance Calculator,"Create a 'Point' class with x and y coordinates. Write a method that takes two 'Point' objects and calculates the distance between them."
"Writing Classes",Class Blueprint,"Write a 'House' class with attributes for number of bedrooms, number of bathrooms, and square footage. Include a default constructor and a parameterized constructor."
"Writing Classes",Data Hiding,"Create a 'Person' class with private attributes for name and social security number. Provide a public method to get the name but no public method to get the social security number, demonstrating data hiding."
"Writing Classes",Static Utility Class,"Create a 'MathUtils' class that is not meant to be instantiated (give it a private constructor). Add static methods for operations like finding the factorial of a number or checking if a number is prime."
"Writing Classes",Immutable Class,"Write an immutable 'Color' class with final attributes for red, green, and blue values. The values should be set only through the constructor."
"Writing Classes",Overriding equals() and hashCode() ,"In a 'Student' class, override the 'equals()' and 'hashCode()' methods to base equality on the student's ID number, not on the object reference."
"Writing Classes",Class with an Enum,"Create an 'enum' for 'DayOfWeek'. Then, create a 'Meeting' class that has a 'DayOfWeek' attribute to specify on which day the meeting occurs."
"Writing Classes",Constructor Overloading,"Create a 'Pizza' class with multiple constructors: a default constructor for a plain cheese pizza, one that takes toppings, and one that takes toppings and size."
"Writing Classes",Copy Constructor,"In a 'Point' class, create a copy constructor that takes another 'Point' object and initializes the new object's attributes with the values from the existing object."
"Writing Classes",Singleton Pattern,"Implement the Singleton pattern for a 'DatabaseConnection' class to ensure that only one instance of the class can ever be created."
"Writing Classes",Inner Class,"Create an 'Outer' class with a private method. Then, create an 'Inner' class inside the 'Outer' class that can access the private method of the 'Outer' class."
"Writing Classes",Class with a 'finalize' method,"Create a class and override the 'finalize()' method to print a message when the object is about to be garbage collected (Note: Explain that this is not a reliable mechanism for resource cleanup)."
"Writing Classes",Fluent Interface,"Design a 'PersonBuilder' class with a fluent interface. For example, 'new PersonBuilder().withName("John").withAge(30).build();'."
"Operators",Basic Arithmetic,"Write a program that takes two integers from the user and prints their sum, difference, product, quotient, and remainder."
"Operators",Relational Operators,"Write a program that compares two numbers and prints whether the first number is greater than, less than, or equal to the second number."
"Operators",Logical Operators,"Create a program that checks if a user is eligible to vote (age >= 18) and is a citizen. Use logical AND."
"Operators",Bitwise AND, OR, XOR,"Take two integers and perform bitwise AND, OR, and XOR operations on them. Print the results in decimal and binary."
"Operators",Bitwise Shift Operators,"Take an integer and perform left shift (<<), right shift (>>), and unsigned right shift (>>>) operations. Explain the difference in the output."
"Operators",Compound Assignment,"Declare a variable and use all the compound assignment operators (+=, -=, *=, /=, %=, &=, |=, ^=, <<=, >>=) on it, printing the result after each operation."
"Operators",Ternary Operator for Max,"Use the ternary operator to find the maximum of three numbers."
"Operators",Increment/Decrement Puzzle,"Write a code snippet with a mix of pre- and post-increment/decrement operators and predict the final values of the variables involved."
"Operators",Operator Precedence Challenge,"Evaluate the expression 'int result = 5 + 10 * 3 - 8 / 4 % 2;' without running it. Then, verify your answer with a program."
"Operators",String Concatenation Operator,"Concatenate a string with an integer and a double using the '+' operator and print the result."
"Operators",instanceof Operator,"Create a parent class and a child class. Create an object of the child class and use the 'instanceof' operator to check if it's an instance of the child class and the parent class."
"Operators",Bitwise NOT (Complement),"Take an integer, apply the bitwise complement operator (~), and print the result. Explain why the result is what it is."
"Type casting",Implicit Casting (Widening),"Declare a 'byte', 'short', and 'int'. Assign the 'byte' to the 'short', and the 'short' to the 'int'. Print the values to show implicit casting."
"Type casting",Explicit Casting (Narrowing),"Declare a 'double' and an 'int'. Explicitly cast the 'double' to an 'int' and print the result to see the truncation of the decimal part."
"Type casting",Casting in Expressions,"Write an expression to calculate the average of three integers. Cast one of the integers to a 'double' before the division to get a floating-point result instead of an integer result."
"Type casting",Potential Data Loss,"Explicitly cast a 'long' value that is larger than the maximum 'int' value to an 'int'. Print the result to demonstrate data loss."
"Type casting",Casting Characters to Integers,"Declare a 'char' variable. Cast it to an 'int' to get its ASCII/Unicode value."
"Type casting",Casting Integers to Characters,"Declare an 'int' variable with a value corresponding to an ASCII character (e.g. 65 for 'A'). Cast it to a 'char' and print the result."
"Type casting",Casting with Objects (Upcasting),"Create a 'Dog' class that inherits from an 'Animal' class. Create a 'Dog' object and assign it to an 'Animal' reference variable (upcasting)."
"Type casting",Casting with Objects (Downcasting),"Using the 'Animal' reference from the previous exercise that holds a 'Dog' object, explicitly cast it back to a 'Dog' reference variable (downcasting). Use 'instanceof' to check before casting."
"Type casting",ClassCastException,"Create an 'Animal' reference holding a 'Cat' object. Try to downcast it to a 'Dog' reference to see the 'ClassCastException' at runtime."
"Type casting",Casting Primitives to Wrappers,"Demonstrate how casting works with wrapper classes, for example, casting an 'Integer' to a 'Double' is not possible directly, but you can get the 'intValue()' and then cast the primitive."
"Type casting",Casting in Method Calls,"Create an overloaded method, one that takes an 'int' and one that takes a 'double'. Call the method with an 'int' variable, and then call it by casting the 'int' variable to a 'double'."
"Type casting",Rounding with Casting,"Show how to round a 'double' to the nearest 'int' by adding 0.5 and then casting to 'int'."
"if and switch",Grade Calculator,"Write a program that takes a numerical score (0-100) and prints the corresponding letter grade (A, B, C, D, F) using an if-else if-else ladder."
"if and switch",Simple Login,"Create a program that checks if a user-entered username and password match predefined values using an if-else statement."
"if and switch",Positive, Negative, or Zero,"Write a program that checks if a given number is positive, negative, or zero using an if-else if-else statement."
"if and switch",Day of the Week,"Use a switch statement to print the name of the day of the week, given a number from 1 to 7."
"if and switch",Vowel or Consonant with Switch,"Use a switch statement to determine if a given character is a vowel or a consonant. Handle both uppercase and lowercase vowels."
"if and switch",Triangle Type,"Write a program that takes the lengths of three sides of a triangle and determines if it is equilateral, isosceles, or scalene."
"if and switch",ATM Machine,"Simulate a simple ATM. Ask the user for an action (check balance, deposit, withdraw) and use a switch statement to perform the corresponding action."
"if and switch",Rock, Paper, Scissors,"Write a simple rock-paper-scissors game against the computer. Use if-else statements to determine the winner."
"if and switch",Season Detector,"Given a month (as a number 1-12), use a switch statement to determine the season (Winter, Spring, Summer, Fall)."
"if and switch",Discount Calculator,"A shop gives a 10% discount if the cost of purchased quantity is more than 1000. Ask the user for the quantity and price per item. Calculate and print the total cost."
"if and switch",Nested If,"Write a program to find the largest of three numbers using nested if statements."
"if and switch",Traffic Light,"Simulate a traffic light. Given the current color of the light ('Red', 'Yellow', 'Green'), print the action a driver should take."
"Loop Break Continue",Print Numbers 1 to 10,"Write a simple for loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10."
"Loop Break Continue",Sum of First N Natural Numbers,"Use a while loop to calculate the sum of the first N natural numbers, where N is input by the user."
"Loop Break Continue",Multiplication Table,"Print the multiplication table for a given number using a for loop."
"Loop Break Continue",Factorial Calculation,"Calculate the factorial of a number using a do-while loop."
"Loop Break Continue",Iterate Through an Array,"Create an integer array and use an enhanced for loop (for-each) to print all its elements."
"Loop Break Continue",Find a Number in an Array,"Use a for loop and the 'break' statement to search for a specific number in an array. Stop the loop as soon as the number is found."
"Loop Break Continue",Print Even Numbers,"Use a for loop and the 'continue' statement to print only the even numbers between 1 and 20."
"Loop Break Continue",Password Entry,"Write a program that repeatedly prompts a user to enter a password until they enter the correct one. Use a do-while loop."
"Loop Break Continue",Reverse a String,"Use a for loop to iterate backward through a string and print its reverse."
"Loop Break Continue",Fibonacci Series,"Generate and print the first N terms of the Fibonacci series using a loop."
"Loop Break Continue",Prime Number Check,"Write a program that checks if a given number is prime using a for loop and a break statement."
"Loop Break Continue",Nested Loop for Pattern,"Use nested for loops to print a right-angled triangle pattern of asterisks."
"Defining a Class",Simple Car Class,"Define a 'Car' class with attributes for 'make', 'model', and 'year'. Include a method 'displayInfo()' that prints these details."
"Defining a Class",Student Class,"Define a 'Student' class with fields for 'name', 'studentId', and an array of grades. Add a method 'calculateAverage()' that returns the average grade."
"Defining a Class",Rectangle Class,"Define a 'Rectangle' class with 'length' and 'width' as attributes. Include methods 'getArea()' and 'getPerimeter()'."
"Defining a Class",BankAccount Class,"Define a 'BankAccount' class with attributes 'accountNumber' and 'balance'. Add methods 'deposit(double amount)' and 'withdraw(double amount)'."
"Defining a Class",Dog Class,"Define a 'Dog' class with attributes 'name' and 'breed'. Include a method 'bark()' that prints 'Ruff! Ruff!'."
"Defining a Class",Book Class,"Define a 'Book' class with fields for 'title', 'author', and 'numberOfPages'. Add a method 'isLongRead()' that returns true if the book has more than 500 pages."
"Defining a Class",Circle Class,"Define a 'Circle' class with a 'radius' attribute. Include methods 'getCircumference()' and 'getArea()'."
"Defining a Class",LightBulb Class,"Define a 'LightBulb' class with a boolean attribute 'isOn'. Add methods 'turnOn()' and 'turnOff()' to change its state."
"Defining a Class",Point Class,"Define a 'Point' class with 'x' and 'y' integer coordinates. Add a method 'distanceFromOrigin()' that calculates its distance from (0,0)."
"Defining a Class",Person Class,"Define a 'Person' class with 'name' and 'age' attributes. Include a method 'introduce()' that prints a message like 'Hi, my name is [name] and I am [age] years old'."
"Defining a Class",Product Class,"Define a 'Product' class with 'name' and 'price' attributes. Add a method 'applyDiscount(double percentage)' that reduces the price."
"Defining a Class",Temperature Class,"Define a 'Temperature' class that stores a temperature in Celsius. Include methods 'toFahrenheit()' and 'toKelvin()' for conversion."
"Creating Objects",Instantiate a Car,"Using the 'Car' class from a previous exercise, create two different 'Car' objects in your main method and call their 'displayInfo()' method."
"Creating Objects",Instantiate a Student,"Create a 'Student' object, set its name and ID, add some grades, and then call the 'calculateAverage()' method."
"Creating Objects",Array of Rectangles,"Create an array that can hold 5 'Rectangle' objects. Instantiate each element of the array with a new 'Rectangle' object with different dimensions."
"Creating Objects",Bank Simulation,"Create two 'BankAccount' objects for two different people. Perform a series of deposits and withdrawals on both accounts."
"Creating Objects",Dog Pack,"Instantiate three 'Dog' objects with different names and breeds. Make each dog bark."
"Creating Objects",Library Shelf,"Create five different 'Book' objects and store them in an ArrayList. Iterate through the list and print the title of each book."
"Creating Objects",Circle Comparison,"Create two 'Circle' objects. Write code to determine which circle has a larger area."
"Creating Objects",Room Lighting,"Create a 'LightBulb' object. Call its 'turnOn()' method, check its state, then call its 'turnOff()' method and check its state again."
"Creating Objects",Geometric Shape,"Instantiate a 'Point' object and print its distance from the origin."
"Creating Objects",Family Members,"Create 'Person' objects representing members of a family. Have each person introduce themselves."
"Creating Objects",Shopping Cart,"Create several 'Product' objects. Simulate adding them to a shopping cart and calculate the total price."
"Creating Objects",Weather Report,"Create a 'Temperature' object for the current temperature in Celsius. Then, print the equivalent temperature in Fahrenheit and Kelvin."
"Constructors",Person with Constructors,"Create a 'Person' class with a default constructor that initializes name to 'Unknown' and age to 0, and a parameterized constructor that accepts a name and age."
"Constructors",Book with Overloaded Constructors,"Create a 'Book' class with three constructors: one default, one that takes only the title, and one that takes title, author, and year."
"Constructors",Rectangle Constructor,"In a 'Rectangle' class, create a constructor that takes length and width as arguments to initialize the object."
"Constructors",No-Arg and Parameterized Car,"Create a 'Car' class with a no-arg constructor that sets default values and a parameterized constructor to set make, model, and year."
"Constructors",Circle from Radius,"Create a 'Circle' class where the only way to create an object is by providing the radius through a parameterized constructor."
"Constructors",Copy Constructor,"Create a 'Point' class with a constructor that takes x and y, and a copy constructor that takes another 'Point' object to create a duplicate."
"Constructors",Student Constructor,"Create a 'Student' class with a constructor that requires a name and student ID for instantiation."
"Constructors",Pizza Order,"Design a 'Pizza' class with overloaded constructors: one for a small cheese pizza, one that lets you specify the size, and one that lets you specify size and toppings."
"Constructors",Default Constructor in Action,"Create a class without any constructor defined. Instantiate it to show that Java provides a default constructor automatically."
"Constructors",Chaining Constructors,"In a class, create an overloaded constructor that calls another constructor in the same class using 'this()'."
"Constructors",Private Constructor,"Create a utility class with only static methods and make its constructor private to prevent instantiation."
"Constructors",Constructor with Validation,"In a 'BankAccount' constructor, add validation to ensure the initial balance is not negative."
"this Keyword",Distinguish Instance Variables,"In a constructor for a 'Person' class, use 'this' to assign parameter values (e.g. 'name', 'age') to instance variables with the same names (this.name = name)."
"this Keyword",Call Another Constructor,"Create a class with two constructors. Have one constructor call the other using 'this()' to reduce code duplication."
"this Keyword",Pass as an Argument,"Create a method that takes an object of the current class as an argument. From another method in the same class, call the first method, passing 'this' as the argument."
"this Keyword",Return the Current Instance,"Create a method with a fluent interface style that returns 'this' (the current object) to allow for method chaining (e.g. object.setX(10).setY(20);)."
"this Keyword",In a Setter Method,"In a setter method, like 'setName(String name)', use 'this.name = name' to assign the new value to the instance variable."
"this Keyword",Avoiding Name Conflicts,"Create a method that has a local variable with the same name as an instance variable. Use 'this' to explicitly refer to the instance variable."
"this Keyword",Anonymous Inner Class,"Use 'this' inside an anonymous inner class to refer to the inner class instance, and 'ClassName.this' to refer to the outer class instance."
"this Keyword",In a Constructor for a Helper Method,"Call a private helper method from within a constructor, passing 'this' to the helper method so it can operate on the newly created object."
"this Keyword",Explicitly Calling a Method,"Although not necessary, show how 'this.myMethod()' is equivalent to just 'myMethod()' when calling another method of the same object."
"this Keyword",In equals() Method,"When overriding the 'equals(Object obj)' method, use 'this == obj' as the first check for reference equality."
"this Keyword",In toString() Method,"When overriding the 'toString()' method, use 'this' implicitly or explicitly to access the instance variables to build the string representation."
"this Keyword",Static Context Error,"Try to use the 'this' keyword inside a static method and observe the compiler error. Explain why 'this' cannot be used in a static context."
"Access Modifiers",Public Access,"Create a class with a public method. Create an object of this class in another class (in a different package) and call the public method."
"Access Modifiers",Private Access,"Create a class with a private variable. Try to access this variable directly from another class and observe the compiler error. Then, add a public getter to access it."
"Access Modifiers",Protected Access,"Create a class 'A' with a protected method in package P1. Create a subclass 'B' of 'A' in package P2. Show that 'B' can access the protected method."
"Access Modifiers",Default (Package-Private) Access,"Create a class with a default-access method in package P1. Show that another class in P1 can access it, but a class in package P2 cannot."
"Access Modifiers",Encapsulation with private,"Create a 'BankAccount' class with a private 'balance'. All modifications to the balance must go through public 'deposit' and 'withdraw' methods."
"Access Modifiers",Public Class,"Demonstrate that a public class can be accessed from any other class."
"Access Modifiers",Private Constructor,"Create a class with a private constructor to prevent it from being instantiated from outside the class (useful for utility classes or Singletons)."
"Access Modifiers",Protected Fields in Inheritance,"Create a superclass with a protected field. In a subclass, access and modify this field directly."
"Access Modifiers",Public Constants,"Create an interface with a 'public static final' constant and access it from another class."
"Access Modifiers",Mixing Modifiers,"Create a class with public, protected, default, and private members. Create another class and show which members are accessible from where (same class, same package, subclass, different package)."
"Access Modifiers",Getters and Setters,"Reinforce the concept of using private fields and public getters/setters to control access to an object's state."
"Access Modifiers",Access Modifier Error,"Write code that deliberately tries to violate an access modifier rule (e.g. accessing a private member from another class) and comment on the resulting error."
"Public Interface",Calculator Interface,"Define the public interface for a 'Calculator' class. This should include public methods like 'add()', 'subtract()', 'multiply()', and 'divide()'."
"Public Interface",BankAccount Interface,"Design the public interface for a 'BankAccount' class. Include methods like 'getBalance()', 'deposit(amount)', and 'withdraw(amount)'."
"Public Interface",API for a 'Person' Class,"Define the public methods for a 'Person' class. This could include a constructor, getters for name and age, and a setter for age."
"Public Interface",Thermostat Public Methods,"Design the public interface for a 'Thermostat' class. It should have methods like 'getCurrentTemperature()', 'setTargetTemperature(temp)', and 'isHeatingOn()'."
"Public Interface",Public Constants,"In a utility class, define public static final constants that are part of its public interface, e.g. 'public static final double PI = 3.14159;'."
"Public Interface",Car's Public Interface,"Define the public methods a driver would use for a 'Car' class: 'startEngine()', 'stopEngine()', 'accelerate(amount)', 'brake(amount)'."
"Public Interface",Hiding Implementation,"Create a class with a public method that performs a complex calculation. The calculation itself should be broken down into several private helper methods, which are not part of the public interface."
"Public Interface",Interface vs. Implementation,"Create a 'List' interface (like java.util.List) and then provide two different implementing classes, 'ArrayList' and 'LinkedList'. The public interface is the same, but the implementation differs."
"Public Interface to a-Class",Stable Interface,"Design a public interface for a class. Then, change the private implementation details without changing the public method signatures, demonstrating that client code is not affected."
"Public Interface",Method Signatures,"Focus on the method signatures (access modifier, return type, name, parameters) as the contract of the public interface."
"Public Interface",Documentation with Javadoc,"Write a simple class with a public interface and use Javadoc comments to document what each public method does, what its parameters are, and what it returns."
"Public Interface",User of a Class,"Write a 'User' class that interacts with a 'DataService' class only through its public interface, without any knowledge of its internal workings."
"Private Interface",Helper Methods,"Create a class with a public method 'calculateArea()'. This method should call several private helper methods like 'validateInput()', 'performCalculation()', and 'logResult()'."
"Private Interface",Internal State Management,"In a 'BankAccount' class, the 'balance' field should be private. All changes to the balance are managed internally by public methods like 'deposit' and 'withdraw'."
"Private Interface",Refactoring to Private Methods,"Take a class with one very long public method and refactor it by extracting logical parts into smaller, private helper methods."
"Private Interface",Hiding Complexity,"Create a class that connects to a database. The public method might be 'getUser(id)', but the private interface would consist of methods like 'openConnection()', 'buildQuery()', 'executeQuery()', and 'closeConnection()'."
"Private Interface",Private Fields,"Emphasize that all instance variables should generally be private, making them part of the private interface, accessible only within the class itself."
"Private Interface",Private Constructor,"Create a class with a private constructor and a public static factory method 'createInstance()'. This hides the construction logic."
"Private Interface",Internal Constants,"Define a 'private static final' constant that is used in calculations within the class but is not exposed to the outside world."
"Private Interface",State Validation,"A public 'setAge(int age)' method might call a private 'isValidAge(int age)' method to validate the input before changing the object's state."
"Private Interface",Implementation Detail,"Create a class that internally uses an array to store data. All the array manipulation logic should be in private methods. The public interface might just be 'add(item)' and 'get(index)'."
"Private Interface",Security,"In a 'User' class, the 'password' field should be private and never exposed directly. A public 'changePassword' method would handle the logic, possibly calling private encryption methods."
"Private Interface",Code Organization,"Demonstrate how using private methods helps in organizing the code within a class and makes the public methods easier to read and understand."
"Private Interface",Testing Private Methods,"Discuss the concept that you typically test a class's public interface, and by doing so, you are indirectly testing the private methods it calls. (Direct testing of private methods is possible but often discouraged)."
"Static Methods",Utility Method,"Create a 'MathUtils' class with a static method 'max(int a, int b)' that returns the larger of two integers, without needing to create an instance of 'MathUtils'."
"Static Methods",Factory Method,"Create a 'Person' class with a private constructor and a public static factory method 'createPerson(String name)' that returns a new 'Person' object."
"Static Methods",Main Method,"Explain that the 'public static void main(String[] args)' method is static so that the JVM can call it without creating an object of the class."
"Static Methods",Static Counter,"Create a 'Car' class with a private static int 'carCount'. Increment this counter in the constructor and provide a public static method 'getCarCount()' to retrieve the total number of cars created."
"Static Methods",Static Initializer Block,"Use a static initializer block to initialize a complex static variable, for example, a 'Map' that needs to be populated with some default values when the class is loaded."
"Static Methods",Static Import,"Use a static import to import all static members of the 'java.lang.Math' class, so you can call methods like 'sqrt()' and 'pow()' directly without the 'Math.' prefix."
"Static Methods",Static vs. Instance,"Create a class with both a static method and an instance method. From the main method, call the static method using the class name and the instance method using an object of the class."
"Static Methods",Accessing Static Members,"Show that a static method can access other static members (fields and methods) of the class directly."
"Static Methods",Cannot Access Instance Members,"Demonstrate that a static method cannot directly access instance members (fields and methods) of the class, and explain why (no 'this' reference)."
"Static Methods",Helper Function,"Create a class that performs some data processing. The main instance method can call a private static helper method to perform a pure, reusable calculation."
"Static Methods",Singleton Pattern with Static Method,"Implement the Singleton pattern, where a private static instance of the class is accessed through a public static 'getInstance()' method."
"Static Methods",Constants Class,"Create a class 'Constants' that only contains 'public static final' fields. This class is not meant to be instantiated and its members are accessed statically (e.g. Constants.MAX_USERS)."
"Static Class Members",Static Variable (Class Variable),"Create a 'Student' class with a static variable 'schoolName'. All 'Student' objects will share this same school name."
"Static Class Members",Static Counter,"Create a class 'Thing' with a private static int 'counter'. Increment it in the constructor. Create several 'Thing' objects and print the final value of the counter."
"Static Class Members",Static Constant,"Define a 'public static final double PI' in a 'Circle' class. Use it in calculations for area and circumference."
"Static Class Members",Static Initializer,"Use a static block to initialize a static 'ArrayList' with some default values when the class is first loaded."
"Static Class Members",Static Method,"Create a utility class 'StringUtils' with a static method 'reverse(String s)' that returns the reversed string."
"Static Class Members",Accessing Static Members from Instance Method,"Show that an instance method can access static members of the class."
"Static Class Members",Accessing Static Members from Static Method,"Show that a static method can only access other static members of the class."
"Static Class Members",Changing a Static Variable,"Create two objects of a class with a static variable. Change the static variable's value using one object reference and show that the change is reflected when accessing it through the other object reference."
"Static Class Members",Static vs. Instance Memory,"Explain the difference in memory allocation: static members belong to the class and there's only one copy, while instance members belong to each object."
"Static Class Members",Static Nested Class,"Create a static nested class. Instantiate it without needing an instance of the outer class."
"Static Class Members",When to Use Static,"Create two scenarios: one where an instance variable is appropriate (e.g. a car's color) and one where a static variable is appropriate (e.g. the number of wheels on a car, which is always 4)."
"Static Class Members",Static Import,"Use a static import to bring a static constant into the local namespace and use it without the class name prefix."
"Getters and Setters",Basic Getters and Setters,"Create a 'Person' class with private fields 'name' and 'age'. Provide public 'getName()', 'setName()', 'getAge()', and 'setAge()' methods."
"Getters and Setters",Read-Only Field,"Create a 'Student' class with a private 'studentId' field. Provide a public 'getStudentId()' method but no 'setStudentId()' method, making the field read-only after object creation."
"Getters and Setters",Write-Only Field,"Create a 'PasswordManager' class with a private 'newPassword' field. Provide a 'setNewPassword()' method but no 'getNewPassword()' method for security reasons."
"Getters and Setters",Validation in Setter,"In the 'setAge(int age)' method of a 'Person' class, add validation to ensure the age is not negative."
"Getters and Setters",Calculation in Getter,"In a 'Rectangle' class with private 'width' and 'height', create a 'getArea()' method that calculates and returns the area, rather than storing it in a separate field."
"Getters and Setters",Boolean Getter Convention,"For a private boolean field like 'isEngineOn', name the getter 'isEngineOn()' instead of 'getIsEngineOn()'."
"Getters and Setters",Defensive Copying in Getter,"If a class has a private field that is a mutable object (like a 'Date' or an 'ArrayList'), the getter should return a copy of the object to protect the internal state."
"Getters and Setters",Defensive Copying in Setter,"Similarly, if a setter takes a mutable object as a parameter, it should store a copy of it, not the reference to the original object."
"Getters and Setters",Fluent Setters,"Modify the setter methods to return 'this' (the current object) to allow for method chaining, e.g. 'person.setName("John").setAge(30);'."
"Getters and Setters",Getter/Setter for an Array,"In a class with a private array field, the getter could return a copy of the array. Discuss the design choices for a setter (e.g. set the whole array, or provide 'add'/'remove' methods instead)."
"Getters and Setters",Lazy Initialization in Getter,"In a getter for a complex object, check if the field is null. If it is, create the object on the first call to the getter. This is lazy initialization."
"Getters and Setters",IDE Generation,"Explain how modern IDEs can automatically generate getters and setters for class fields."
"Inheritance",Simple Inheritance,"Create a base class 'Animal' with a method 'eat()'. Create a derived class 'Dog' that inherits from 'Animal'. Create a 'Dog' object and call the 'eat()' method."
"Inheritance",Method Overriding,"In the 'Dog' class from the previous exercise, override the 'eat()' method to print 'Dog is eating'. Also, create a 'Cat' class that overrides 'eat()' to print 'Cat is eating'."
"Inheritance",The 'super' Keyword,"In the 'Dog' class, create a constructor that calls the constructor of the 'Animal' superclass using 'super()'. Also, in an overridden method, call the superclass's version of the method using 'super.methodName()'."
"Inheritance",The 'final' Keyword,"Create a 'final' class and try to extend it to see the compiler error. Create a method with the 'final' keyword and try to override it in a subclass."
"Inheritance",Multi-level Inheritance,"Create a class 'A', have class 'B' inherit from 'A', and class 'C' inherit from 'B'. Show that an object of class 'C' has access to members of both 'A' and 'B'."
"Inheritance",Hierarchical Inheritance,"Create a base class 'Vehicle'. Create two subclasses, 'Car' and 'Bicycle', that both inherit from 'Vehicle'."
"Inheritance",Protected Members,"Create a superclass with a 'protected' member. Show that a subclass can access this member directly."
"Inheritance",The 'instanceof' Operator,"Create objects of 'Animal', 'Dog', and 'Cat'. Use the 'instanceof' operator to check their types."
"Inheritance",Upcasting,"Create a 'Dog' object and assign it to an 'Animal' reference variable. Call a method that is defined in the 'Animal' class."
"Inheritance",Downcasting,"Take the 'Animal' reference from the previous exercise, check if it's an 'instanceof Dog', and then cast it back to a 'Dog' reference to call a method specific to the 'Dog' class."
"Inheritance",Abstract Class,"Create an abstract class 'Shape' with an abstract method 'draw()'. Create concrete subclasses 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' that provide an implementation for the 'draw()' method."
"Inheritance",Constructor Chaining,"Create a class hierarchy and place print statements in each constructor. Create an object of the most derived class to see the order in which constructors are called."
"Extends Keyword",Vehicle Hierarchy,"Create a 'Vehicle' class. Then, create a 'Car' class that 'extends Vehicle' to inherit its properties and methods."
"Extends Keyword",Employee and Manager,"Create an 'Employee' class with properties like 'name' and 'salary'. Create a 'Manager' class that 'extends Employee' and adds a 'department' property."
"Extends Keyword",Animal Kingdom,"Create an 'Animal' class with an 'eat()' method. Create a 'Lion' class that 'extends Animal' and overrides the 'eat()' method."
"Extends Keyword",Shape and Circle,"Create a 'Shape' class. Then, create a 'Circle' class that 'extends Shape' and adds a 'radius' property."
"Extends Keyword",Calling Superclass Method,"In the 'Lion' class, create a method that calls the 'eat()' method from the 'Animal' class using 'super.eat()'."
"Extends Keyword",Single Inheritance,"Demonstrate single inheritance by having a 'Dog' class extend an 'Animal' class."
"Extends Keyword",Multi-level Inheritance,"Demonstrate multi-level inheritance: 'GermanShepherd' extends 'Dog', which extends 'Animal'."
"Extends Keyword",Constructor Chaining with extends,"In the 'Car' constructor, use 'super()' to call the constructor of the 'Vehicle' class."
"Extends Keyword",Final Class,"Create a 'final class String' (or a similar example) and try to create a new class that 'extends' it to show the compiler error."
"Extends Keyword",Extending Object,"Create a simple 'Person' class. Explain that if no 'extends' keyword is used, the class implicitly 'extends java.lang.Object'."
"Extends Keyword",Accessing Protected Members,"Create a 'Parent' class with a 'protected' field. Create a 'Child' class that 'extends Parent' and accesses that protected field."
"Extends Keyword",IS-A Relationship,"Explain the 'IS-A' relationship that the 'extends' keyword represents (e.g. a 'Car' IS-A 'Vehicle')."
"Super Keyword",Calling Superclass Constructor,"In a 'Manager' class that extends 'Employee', use 'super(name, salary)' in the 'Manager' constructor to call the 'Employee' constructor."
"Super Keyword",Calling Superclass Method,"In a 'Dog' class that overrides the 'makeSound()' method from the 'Animal' class, use 'super.makeSound()' inside the overridden method to call the parent's version first."
"Super Keyword",Accessing Superclass Field,"If a subclass has a field with the same name as a field in the superclass (shadowing), use 'super.fieldName' to access the superclass's field."
"Super Keyword",Constructor Chaining,"Create a three-level inheritance hierarchy. In the constructor of the lowest class, call 'super()' and trace the chain of constructor calls up to the top."
"Super Keyword",Super in a Method,"Create a 'printDetails()' method in a subclass that first calls 'super.printDetails()' to print the parent's details, and then prints its own specific details."
"Super Keyword",Implicit super() Call,"Create a superclass with a no-arg constructor and a subclass with a constructor. Show that 'super()' is called implicitly if not written explicitly."
"Super Keyword",Explicit super() Call Requirement,"Create a superclass that only has a parameterized constructor (no default constructor). In the subclass, show that you get a compiler error until you explicitly call 'super(...)' with the required arguments."
"Super Keyword",Super vs. This,"Create a class and use both 'super()' and 'this()' (in different constructors) to demonstrate their different purposes (calling superclass vs. same-class constructors)."
"Super Keyword",Cannot Use in Static Context,"Try to use the 'super' keyword inside a static method and observe the compiler error. Explain why."
"Super Keyword",Super with Multiple Levels,"In a class 'C' that extends 'B' which extends 'A', show that 'super' in 'C' refers to 'B', not 'A'."
"Super Keyword",First Statement in Constructor,"Demonstrate that the call to 'super()' or 'this()' must be the very first statement in a constructor."
"Super Keyword",Real World Scenario,"Model a 'Laptop' class extending a 'Computer' class. The 'Laptop' constructor would call 'super()' to initialize common computer properties and then initialize its own properties like 'batteryLife'."
"Method Overriding",Animal Sounds,"Create a base class 'Animal' with a 'makeSound()' method. Create subclasses 'Dog', 'Cat', and 'Cow' that each override 'makeSound()' to print their specific sound."
"Method Overriding",Shape Area,"Create a 'Shape' class with a method 'getArea()' that returns 0. Create 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' subclasses that override 'getArea()' to calculate their area correctly."
"Method Overriding",Vehicle Movement,"Create a 'Vehicle' class with a 'move()' method. Create 'Car' and 'Boat' subclasses that override 'move()' to describe how they move (e.g. 'driving on road', 'sailing on water')."
"Method Overriding",Using @Override Annotation,"Repeat one of the previous exercises, but add the '@Override' annotation above the overridden methods. Then, make a mistake in the method signature to show how the annotation helps catch errors at compile time."
"Method Overriding",Calling the Overridden Method,"In a 'Manager' class that overrides the 'getSalary()' method from the 'Employee' class, the overridden method should call 'super.getSalary()' and then add a bonus."
"Method Overriding",Access Modifiers in Overriding,"Show that an overridden method can have a less restrictive access modifier (e.g. protected in superclass, public in subclass), but not a more restrictive one."
"Method Overriding",Final Methods,"Create a class with a 'final' method. Try to override this method in a subclass and observe the compiler error."
"Method Overriding",Static Methods Cannot Be Overridden,"Create a class with a static method. Create a subclass with a static method of the same signature. Show that this is method hiding, not overriding, by calling the method on references of both the superclass and subclass types."
"Method Overriding",Covariant Return Types,"Create a superclass with a method that returns an 'Object'. In the subclass, override the method to return a more specific type, like a 'String'."
"Method Overriding",Overriding toString() ,"Create a 'Person' class and override the 'toString()' method from the 'Object' class to return a custom string representation of the person's details."
"Method Overriding",Overriding equals() ,"Create a 'Student' class and override the 'equals()' method from the 'Object' class to compare students based on their student ID."
"Method Overriding",Dynamic Method Dispatch,"Create a superclass reference variable that points to a subclass object. Call an overridden method on this reference and show that the subclass's version of the method is executed at runtime."
"Final Keyword",Final Variable (Constant),"Declare a 'final' variable for PI and use it to calculate the area of a circle. Try to reassign it and observe the compiler error."
"Final Keyword",Final Method,"Create a 'Parent' class with a 'final' method. Create a 'Child' class that extends 'Parent' and try to override the 'final' method."
"Final Keyword",Final Class,"Create a 'final' class 'ImmutablePoint'. Try to create another class that extends 'ImmutablePoint'."
"Final Keyword",Blank Final Variable,"Declare a 'final' instance variable without initializing it. Initialize it in the constructor. Show that it cannot be changed after the object is constructed."
"Final Keyword",Static Final Variable,"Create a 'public static final' variable in a class to define a global constant."
"Final Keyword",Final Method Parameter,"Create a method that takes a 'final' parameter. Show that the parameter's value cannot be changed inside the method."
"Final Keyword",Final Local Variable,"Declare a 'final' local variable inside a method. Try to change its value later in the method."
"Final Keyword",Final with Anonymous Classes,"Use a 'final' local variable inside an anonymous inner class to show that it's accessible."
"Final Keyword",Final with Loops,"Show how a 'final' variable can be used in an enhanced for loop ('for (final String item : list)')."
"Final Keyword",Final for Immutability,"Create an immutable 'Student' class where all fields are 'private final' and set only by the constructor."
"Final Keyword",Final vs. Finally vs. Finalize,"Write a short program or comments explaining the difference between the 'final' keyword, the 'finally' block in exception handling, and the 'finalize()' method."
"Final Keyword",Final Reference Variable,"Declare a 'final' reference to an 'ArrayList'. Show that you cannot reassign the reference to a new 'ArrayList', but you can still add or remove elements from the original list."
"Polymorphism",Drawing Shapes,"Create a 'Shape' superclass and 'Circle', 'Rectangle', 'Triangle' subclasses. Create an array of 'Shape' objects, populate it with different shapes, and loop through it, calling a 'draw()' method on each. This demonstrates polymorphism."
"Polymorphism",Animal Noises,"Create an 'Animal' superclass and 'Dog', 'Cat' subclasses. Create a method that accepts an 'Animal' object and calls its 'makeSound()' method. Pass both a 'Dog' and a 'Cat' object to this method."
"Polymorphism",Employee Payroll,"Create an 'Employee' base class and subclasses like 'SalariedEmployee' and 'HourlyEmployee'. Each has a 'calculatePay()' method. Process a list of 'Employee' objects and calculate the total payroll."
"Polymorphism",Dynamic Method Dispatch,"Create a superclass reference pointing to a subclass object. Call an overridden method to show that the subclass's version is executed at runtime."
"Polymorphism",Polymorphism with Interfaces,"Create an interface 'Playable' with a 'play()' method. Have 'Guitar' and 'Piano' classes implement this interface. Write a method that takes a 'Playable' object and calls 'play()'."
"Polymorphism",Upcasting and Downcasting,"Demonstrate polymorphism by upcasting a 'Manager' object to an 'Employee' reference. Then, safely downcast it back to a 'Manager' to access manager-specific methods."
"Polymorphism",The 'instanceof' operator,"In a polymorphic array of 'Animal' objects, use 'instanceof' to check if an object is a 'Dog' before trying to call a dog-specific method like 'fetch()'."
"Polymorphism",Abstract Classes and Polymorphism,"Use an abstract 'Vehicle' class with an abstract 'startEngine()' method. Create concrete subclasses and treat them polymorphically in a list."
"Polymorphism",Polymorphism in Method Parameters,"Create a 'Printer' class with a method 'print(Object obj)'. Pass it a 'String', an 'Integer', and a custom 'Person' object to show it can handle any object polymorphically (by calling their 'toString()' method)."
"Polymorphism",Polymorphism in Return Types,"Create a factory method that has a return type of a superclass ('Vehicle') but can return an instance of any of its subclasses ('Car', 'Truck') based on some input."
"Polymorphism",Compile-time vs. Run-time Polymorphism,"Create an example of method overloading (compile-time polymorphism) and method overriding (run-time polymorphism) and explain the difference."
"Polymorphism",Benefits of Polymorphism,"Write a small program that would be much more complex without polymorphism (e.g. using a long if-else-if chain with 'instanceof' checks) and compare it to the cleaner polymorphic version."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Shape,"Create an abstract class 'Shape' with an abstract method 'calculateArea()' and a concrete method 'printShapeName()'. Create 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' subclasses that implement the abstract method."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Animal,"Create an abstract class 'Animal' with an abstract method 'makeSound()' and a concrete method 'sleep()'. Create 'Dog' and 'Cat' subclasses."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract BankAccount,"Design an abstract 'BankAccount' class with fields for balance and account number, an abstract method 'calculateInterest()', and concrete methods for 'deposit' and 'withdraw'."
"Abstract Classes",Cannot Instantiate Abstract Class,"Try to create an instance of your abstract 'Shape' class and observe the compiler error. Explain why this is not allowed."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Class with Constructor,"Give your abstract 'Animal' class a constructor that initializes a 'name' field. Show how subclasses must call this constructor using 'super()'."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract vs. Concrete Methods,"Create an abstract class that has a mix of abstract and concrete methods to demonstrate that it's not an all-or-nothing concept."
"Abstract Classes",Polymorphism with Abstract Classes,"Create an array of 'Shape' references and populate it with 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' objects. Loop through the array and call the 'calculateArea()' method on each."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Class without Abstract Methods,"Create an abstract class that has no abstract methods. Explain a potential reason for doing this (e.g. to prevent instantiation of a base class)."
"Abstract Classes",Partial Implementation,"Create a multi-level hierarchy where 'A' is abstract, 'B' is an abstract class that extends 'A' and implements some of its methods, and 'C' is a concrete class that extends 'B'."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Class vs. Interface,"Create a scenario where an abstract class is a better choice than an interface (e.g. when you want to provide some common implemented functionality or have instance variables)."
"Abstract Classes",Template Method Pattern,"Implement the Template Method design pattern using an abstract class. The abstract class defines the skeleton of an algorithm in a method, and subclasses override specific steps."
"Abstract Classes",Abstract Class as a Base,"Use an abstract class as a base for a set of related classes to enforce a common contract and provide shared code."
"Abstract Methods",Shape's Abstract Method,"In an abstract 'Shape' class, declare an abstract method: 'public abstract double getArea();'."
"Abstract Methods",Vehicle's Abstract Method,"In an abstract 'Vehicle' class, declare an abstract method 'startEngine()' that subClasses must implement."
"Abstract Methods",Implementing an Abstract Method,"Create a 'Circle' class that extends 'Shape' and provides a concrete implementation for the 'getArea()' method."
"Abstract Methods",Compiler Error for Unimplemented Method,"Create a concrete class that extends an abstract class but fails to implement one of its abstract methods. Observe the compiler error."
"Abstract Methods",Multiple Abstract Methods,"Create an abstract class 'DataSource' with multiple abstract methods like 'connect()', 'getData()', and 'disconnect()'."
"Abstract Methods",Abstract Method in a Hierarchy,"Create an abstract class 'A' with an abstract method 'foo()'. Create an abstract class 'B' that extends 'A'. Show that 'B' does not have to implement 'foo()', but any concrete subclass of 'B' must."
"Abstract Methods",Abstract Method Signature,"Explain that an abstract method has no body (no curly braces), just a signature followed by a semicolon."
"Abstract Methods",Cannot be private,"Try to declare an abstract method as 'private' and observe the compiler error. Explain why this is not allowed."
"Abstract Methods",Cannot be final,"Try to declare an abstract method as 'final' and observe the compiler error. Explain why."
"Abstract Methods",Cannot be static,"Try to declare an abstract method as 'static' and observe the compiler error. Explain why."
"Abstract Methods",Abstract Method and Polymorphism,"Call the abstract method through a superclass reference pointing to a subclass object to see polymorphism in action."
"Abstract Methods",Forcing a Contract,"Explain how abstract methods are used to force subClasses to provide a specific piece of functionality."
"Interfaces",Drawable Interface,"Create an interface 'Drawable' with a single method 'draw()'. Have 'Circle', 'Rectangle', and 'Image' classes implement this interface."
"Interfaces",Comparable Interface,"Create a 'Student' class and implement the 'Comparable' interface to define a natural ordering for students (e.g. by student ID or name)."
"Interfaces",Multiple Interfaces,"Create a 'SuperHero' class that implements both 'Flyable' and 'Fightable' interfaces."
"Interfaces",Interface vs. Abstract Class,"Create a situation where an interface is a better choice than an abstract class (e.g. for providing a capability to unrelated classes)."
"Interfaces",Default Methods,"Create an interface with a 'default' method. Provide a class that implements the interface but does not override the default method, showing it inherits the implementation."
"Interfaces",Static Methods in Interfaces,"Add a 'static' helper method to an interface. Call this method using the interface name."
"Interfaces",Interface Constants,"Declare a constant (which is implicitly public, static, and final) in an interface and access it from an implementing class."
"Interfaces",Polymorphism with Interfaces,"Create a list of 'Drawable' objects, add 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' instances to it, and loop through, calling the 'draw()' method on each."
"Interfaces",Marker Interface,"Create a marker interface (an interface with no methods, like 'Serializable'). Create a class that implements it and explain its purpose."
"Interfaces",Functional Interface,"Create a functional interface (an interface with a single abstract method) and use a lambda expression to provide its implementation."
"Interfaces",Extending Interfaces,"Create an interface 'A' and another interface 'B' that extends 'A'. A class implementing 'B' must provide implementations for methods from both 'A' and 'B'."
"Interfaces",Private Methods in Interfaces,"(Java 9+) Create an interface with a default method that calls a private method within the same interface to share code between default methods."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Inheritance vs. Implementation,"Create a 'Dog' class that 'extends' an abstract 'Animal' class and 'implements' a 'Pet' interface."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Single vs. Multiple Inheritance,"Create a class that extends one abstract class and implements two different interfaces to demonstrate the difference in inheritance capabilities."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Constructors,"Show that an abstract class can have a constructor (which is called by subclasses via 'super()'), while an interface cannot."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Instance Variables,"Demonstrate that an abstract class can have instance variables (state), while an interface can only have public static final constants."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Access Modifiers,"Show that abstract class methods can have various access modifiers (public, protected), while interface methods before Java 9 were implicitly public."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",IS-A vs. HAS-A (or CAN-DO),"Model a scenario where an abstract class represents an 'IS-A' relationship (a 'Car' is a 'Vehicle') and an interface represents a 'CAN-DO' capability (a 'Car' can be 'Drivable')."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Shared Code,"Create an abstract class to provide common, implemented methods to a group of related subclasses."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Unrelated Classes Contract,"Use an interface to define a contract for a group of unrelated classes (e.g. 'Comparable' for 'Student', 'Book', 'Product')."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Default Methods,"Show how 'default' methods in interfaces bring them closer to abstract classes, but explain the remaining differences (state, constructors)."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",When to Use Which,"Provide two problem descriptions: one that is better solved with an abstract class and one that is better solved with an interface. Implement both."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Evolution (Java 8+),"Discuss how interfaces have evolved with default and static methods, blurring some of the traditional lines between them and abstract classes."
"Abstract Classes-Interfaces",Code Example,"Provide a clear, side-by-side code example of a simple abstract class and a simple interface, each being used by a concrete class."
"Recursion",Factorial,"Write a recursive function to calculate the factorial of a non-negative integer."
"Recursion",Fibonacci Sequence,"Write a recursive function to find the nth term of the Fibonacci sequence."
"Recursion",Sum of Digits,"Write a recursive function to calculate the sum of the digits of a number."
"Recursion",String Reversal,"Write a recursive function that takes a string and returns its reverse."
"Recursion",Binary Search,"Implement the binary search algorithm using recursion to find an element in a sorted array."
"Recursion",Tower of Hanoi,"Solve the classic Tower of Hanoi puzzle using a recursive function."
"Recursion",Base Case,"In the factorial function, clearly identify and comment on the base case (when n is 0 or 1) that stops the recursion."
"Recursion",Recursive Step,"In the factorial function, clearly identify and comment on the recursive step (n * factorial(n-1)) that calls the function again with a smaller problem."
"Recursion",Stack Overflow,"Write a recursive function without a proper base case to demonstrate a StackOverflowError."
"Recursion",Palindrome Checker,"Write a recursive function to check if a string is a palindrome."
"Recursion",Power Function,"Write a recursive function to calculate the power of a number (x^n)."
"Recursion",Recursion vs. Iteration,"Solve a problem (like factorial or Fibonacci) using both recursion and an iterative loop. Compare the two approaches."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Array Declaration and Initialization,"Declare an integer array of size 5. Initialize it with values {10, 20, 30, 40, 50} and print all its elements using a for loop."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Find the Sum and Average,"Create a double array and write code to calculate the sum and average of its elements."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Find the Maximum and Minimum,"Find the largest and smallest element in an integer array."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Search for an Element,"Create an array of strings. Write a program that checks if a given string exists in the array."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Reverse an Array,"Write a program to reverse the elements of an array in place."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Copy an Array,"Create an array and copy its elements to a new array."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Enhanced For Loop,"Use the enhanced for loop (for-each) to iterate through and print the elements of an array."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Array as a Method Parameter,"Write a method that takes an array as a parameter and prints its elements."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Array as a Return Value,"Write a method that creates and returns an array of integers."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Sort an Array,"Use the 'Arrays.sort()' method to sort an array of integers in ascending order."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Count Occurrences,"Count the number of times a specific element appears in an array."
"One-Dimensional Arrays",Merge Two Arrays,"Write a program to merge two sorted arrays into a single sorted array."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",2D Array Initialization,"Declare and initialize a 2x3 2D array (a matrix) of integers. Print all its elements using nested for loops."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Matrix Addition,"Create two 3x3 matrices (2D arrays) and write a program to find their sum."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Accessing Elements,"Create a 2D array and print the element at a specific row and column (e.g. row 1, column 2)."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Sum of All Elements,"Calculate the sum of all elements in a 2D array."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Find Max in 2D Array,"Find the largest element in a 2D array."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Jagged Array,"Create and initialize a jagged array (an array of arrays where each sub-array has a different length). Print its elements."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Tic-Tac-Toe Board,"Represent a Tic-Tac-Toe board using a 3x3 2D char array. Write a method to display the board."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",3D Array,"Declare and initialize a 2x2x2 3D array. Access and print a specific element."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Iterating with For-Each,"Use nested for-each loops to iterate through and print all elements of a 2D array."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Row and Column Sums,"For a given 2D array, calculate and print the sum of each row and the sum of each column."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Matrix Transpose,"Write a program to find the transpose of a square matrix."
"Multi-Dimensional Arrays",Passing 2D Array to Method,"Create a method that takes a 2D array as a parameter and prints it in a matrix format."
"Array Literals",Integer Array Literal,"Declare and initialize an integer array in a single line using an array literal: 'int[] numbers = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};'."
"Array Literals",String Array Literal,"Create a string array of weekday names using an array literal."
"Array Literals",Anonymous Array,"Pass an anonymous array literal directly to a method, e.g. 'printArray(new int[]{9, 8, 7});'."
"Array Literals",Empty Array Literal,"Initialize an array to be empty using an array literal: 'String[] empty = {};'."
"Array Literals",Array of Objects,"Create a 'Student' class and then initialize an array of 'Student' objects using an array literal and the 'new' keyword for each object."
"Array Literals",Double Array Literal,"Create an array of double values representing prices using an array literal."
"Array Literals",Character Array Literal,"Create a character array of vowels using an array literal."
"Array Literals",Boolean Array Literal,"Create a boolean array representing a series of true/false flags using an array literal."
"Array Literals",2D Array Literal,"Initialize a 2D array (matrix) using nested array literals."
"Array Literals",Jagged Array Literal,"Initialize a jagged array using nested array literals of different lengths."
"Array Literals",Using with For-Each Loop,"Create an array using a literal and immediately iterate over it with a for-each loop."
"Array Literals",Limitations,"Explain that array literals can only be used during declaration or in an anonymous array creation."
"String Class",String Length and Concatenation,"Create two strings, find their lengths, and concatenate them to form a new string."
"String Class",Character Access,"Get and print the character at a specific index in a string using 'charAt()'."
"String Class",Substring,"Extract and print a substring from a given string using the 'substring()' method."
"String Class",String Comparison,"Compare two strings for equality using both '==' and the '.equals()' method. Explain the difference."
"String Class",Case Conversion,"Convert a string to all uppercase and all lowercase using 'toUpperCase()' and 'toLowerCase()'."
"String Class",Searching in a String,"Use 'indexOf()' and 'startsWith()' to find the position of a character or substring and to check if a string begins with a certain prefix."
"String Class",Replacing Characters,"Use the 'replace()' method to replace all occurrences of a character or substring within a string."
"String Class",Trimming Whitespace,"Use the 'trim()' method to remove leading and trailing whitespace from a string."
"String Class",Splitting a String,"Split a comma-separated string into an array of strings using the 'split()' method."
"String Class",Immutability,"Demonstrate the immutability of strings by showing that methods like 'concat()' or 'toUpperCase()' return a new string rather than modifying the original."
"String Class",String Formatting,"Use the 'String.format()' method to create a formatted string with placeholders for variables."
"String Class",Checking for Empty or Blank,"(Java 11+) Use 'isEmpty()' and 'isBlank()' to check if a string is empty or contains only whitespace."
"Exception Handling",Try-Catch Block,"Write a program that divides two numbers. Use a try-catch block to handle the 'ArithmeticException' that occurs if the user tries to divide by zero."
"Exception Handling",Multiple Catch Blocks,"Write a program that accesses an array element. Use multiple catch blocks to handle both 'ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException' and 'InputMismatchException' (if reading from user)."
"Exception Handling",The 'finally' Block,"Create a program that reads from a simulated file. Use a try-catch-finally block to ensure that a 'file is closed' message is printed, regardless of whether an exception occurred."
"Exception Handling",The 'throws' Keyword,"Write a method that could potentially throw a checked exception (like 'IOException'). Use the 'throws' keyword in the method signature to declare it."
"Exception Handling",Throwing an Exception,"Write a 'withdraw' method for a bank account. If the withdrawal amount is greater than the balance, 'throw' a new 'IllegalArgumentException'."
"Exception Handling",Custom Exception,"Create your own custom checked exception class (e.g. 'InsufficientFundsException'). Modify the previous exercise to throw this custom exception instead."
"Exception Handling",Checked vs. Unchecked,"Provide an example of code that causes a checked exception (and must be handled) and code that causes an unchecked exception (runtime exception)."
"Exception Handling",Try-with-Resources,"(Java 7+) Rewrite the 'finally' block exercise using a try-with-resources statement to automatically close a resource."
"Exception Handling",Exception Hierarchy,"Catch a more general exception type, like 'Exception' or 'RuntimeException', to show how it can handle various specific exception types."
"Exception Handling",Getting Exception Information,"In a catch block, use the exception object's methods like 'getMessage()' and 'printStackTrace()' to get more information about what went wrong."
"Exception Handling",Nested Try Blocks,"Create a nested try-catch block structure to handle exceptions at different levels."
"Exception Handling",Rethrowing an Exception,"In a catch block, perform some logging or cleanup, and then rethrow the same exception to be handled by an outer handler."
"Comparable and Comparator",Comparable for Natural Ordering,"Create a 'Student' class that implements 'Comparable<Student>'. Implement the 'compareTo()' method to sort students based on their GPA."
"Comparable and Comparator",Sorting with Comparable,"Create a list of 'Student' objects and use 'Collections.sort()' to sort them. The sorting will use the 'compareTo()' method you defined."
"Comparable and Comparator",Comparator for Custom Ordering,"Create a 'Comparator<Student>' class that sorts students by name instead of GPA."
"Comparable and Comparator",Sorting with Comparator,"Use your custom name 'Comparator' with 'Collections.sort()' to sort the list of students by name."
"Comparable and Comparator",Anonymous Comparator,"Sort a list of strings by their length using an anonymous inner 'Comparator' class."
"Comparable and Comparator",Lambda Expression Comparator,"(Java 8+) Rewrite the previous exercise using a lambda expression for the 'Comparator'."
"Comparable and Comparator",Reverse Order,"Use the 'Comparator.reverseOrder()' method to sort a list of integers in descending order."
"Comparable and Comparator",Chaining Comparators,"(Java 8+) Create a 'Comparator' that first sorts students by GPA, and then by name for students with the same GPA, using 'thenComparing()'."
"Comparable and Comparator",Comparing with Primitives,"Create a 'Car' class and a 'Comparator' to sort cars by their year of manufacture (an 'int')."
"Comparable and Comparator",Nulls First/Last,"(Java 8+) Use 'Comparator.nullsFirst()' or 'Comparator.nullsLast()' to handle sorting a list that might contain null elements."
"Comparable and Comparator",Comparable vs. Comparator,"Write a short explanation of when you would choose to implement 'Comparable' versus when you would write a separate 'Comparator'."
"Comparable and Comparator",Sorting a Map,"Explain that you cannot sort a 'HashMap' directly, but you can sort its keys or values by placing them in a list, or use a 'TreeMap' which keeps its entries sorted."
"Primitives vs References","DeclareBothTypes","Declare an 'int' variable 'primitiveAge' and a 'String' object reference 'referenceName'."
"Primitives vs References","MemoryAllocation","In a comment, explain where 'primitiveAge' and 'referenceName' are typically stored in memory (stack vs. heap)."
"Primitives vs References","DirectValue","Initialize 'primitiveAge' to 25. Explain that the variable itself holds the bits representing 25."
"Primitives vs References","AddressValue","Initialize 'referenceName' to ""Alice"". Explain that the variable holds the memory address of the ""Alice"" object."
"Primitives vs References","PrimitiveAssignment","Declare 'int a = 10;'. Declare 'int b = a;'. Change 'a' to 20. Print both 'a' and 'b' to show 'b' is unaffected."
"Primitives vs References","ReferenceAssignment","Declare 'StringBuilder sb1 = new StringBuilder(""Hi"");'. Declare 'StringBuilder sb2 = sb1;'. Append ""!"". to 'sb1'. Print both 'sb1' and 'sb2' to show they both reflect the change."
"Primitives vs References","TheNullKeyword","Declare a String reference 'favoriteBook' and initialize it to 'null'. Explain what 'null' means for a reference variable."
"Primitives vs References","PrimitiveCannotBeNull","Try to assign 'null' to an 'int' variable and observe the compiler error."
"Primitives vs References","PassPrimitiveToMethod","Create a method that takes an 'int'. Pass 'primitiveAge' to it. Modify the parameter inside the method and show the original variable is unchanged."
"Primitives vs References","PassReferenceToMethod","Create a method that takes a 'StringBuilder'. Pass 'sb1' to it. Modify the object via the parameter and show the original variable's object has changed."
"Primitives vs References","PassByValueExplained","In a comment, explain that Java is always pass-by-value. For primitives, the value is copied. For references, the reference (address) is copied."
"Primitives vs References","ComparePrimitivesWithEquals","Use the '==' operator to compare two 'int' variables with the same value. The result should be 'true'."
"Primitives vs References","CompareReferencesWithEquals","Create two separate 'new String(""text"")' objects. Compare them with '==' and explain why the result is 'false'."
"Primitives vs References","CompareReferencesWithDotEquals","Use the '.equals()' method to compare the two String objects from the previous exercise and explain why the result is 'true'."
"Primitives vs References","StringPoolAndEquals","Create two String literals 'String s1 = ""pool""; String s2 = ""pool"";'. Compare them with '==' and explain the result."
"Primitives vs References","DefaultPrimitiveValue","Declare an integer as an instance variable without initializing it. Print its value to see the default of 0."
"Primitives vs References","DefaultReferenceValue","Declare a String as an instance variable without initializing it. Print its value to see the default of 'null'."
"Primitives vs References","NullPointerException","Call a method (like '.length()') on a 'null' String reference to intentionally trigger a 'NullPointerException'."
"Primitives vs References","WrapperClassIntro","Declare an 'Integer' wrapper object 'wrapperAge' and initialize it with an 'int'."
"Primitives vs References","Autoboxing","Assign an 'int' literal directly to an 'Integer' reference to demonstrate autoboxing."
"Primitives vs References","Unboxing","Assign an 'Integer' object directly to an 'int' primitive to demonstrate unboxing."
"Primitives vs References","WrapperClassCanBeNull","Initialize an 'Integer' reference to 'null'. This is a key difference from its primitive counterpart."
"Primitives vs References","UnboxingNull","Attempt to unbox a 'null' Integer reference into an 'int' primitive to trigger a 'NullPointerException'."
"Primitives vs References","WrapperEquality","Create two 'new Integer(10)' objects. Compare them with '==' and '.equals()' to see behavior similar to Strings."
"Primitives vs References","WrapperCache","Create two 'Integer' objects from the value 100 using autoboxing. Compare with '==' and explain the integer cache."
"Primitives vs References","WrapperCacheOutsideRange","Repeat the previous exercise with the value 200 and explain why the '==' result is different."
"Primitives vs References","ArrayOfPrimitives","Create an array of 'int'. Explain that the array itself is an object, but it holds primitive values directly."
"Primitives vs References","ArrayOfObjects","Create an array of 'String'. Explain that the array holds references (memory addresses) to the String objects."
"Primitives vs References","ModifyPrimitiveInArray","Change the value of an element in an 'int' array."
"Primitives vs References","ModifyObjectInArray","Change an object in a 'StringBuilder' array by appending text. All references to that object will see the change."
"Primitives vs References","ImmutableReferenceString","Create a 'String s = ""Start"";'. Call 's.toUpperCase();'. Print 's' to show the original object is unchanged because String is immutable."
"Primitives vs References","ReassigningImmutableReference","Following the previous exercise, assign the result back: 's = s.toUpperCase();'. Explain that 's' now refers to a new object."
"Primitives vs References","MutableReferenceStringBuilder","Create a 'StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(""Start"");'. Call 'sb.append(""End"");'. Print 'sb' to show the original object was modified."
"Primitives vs References","FinalPrimitive","Declare a 'final int X = 10;'. Explain that the value 10 cannot be changed."
"Primitives vs References","FinalReference","Declare a 'final StringBuilder GREETING = new StringBuilder(""Hello"");'. Show that you cannot reassign 'GREETING' to a new object."
"Primitives vs References","ModifyingFinalReference","Show that you can still call methods like 'GREETING.append("" World"")' on the final reference from the previous exercise. Explain why."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge1","Create a method that swaps two 'Integer' objects. Call it and show that it fails. Explain why in terms of pass-by-value."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge2","Create an array of 'int[]'. This is an array of references to integer arrays. Initialize its elements with different-sized arrays."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge3","Pass an 'int[]' to a method. Inside the method, reassign the parameter to a 'new int[10]'. Show the original array outside the method is unaffected."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge4","Pass an 'int[]' to a method. Inside the method, change the value of its first element. Show the original array outside the method IS affected."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge5","Create an 'ArrayList<Integer>'. Add an 'int' to it. Explain the autoboxing that occurs."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge6","Compare 'new int[0]' with 'new int[0]' using '=='. Explain the result."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge7","What does this print? 'String s = null; System.out.println(s + "" is null"");'. Explain string conversion of null."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge8","Create a 'Person' class with an 'int age'. Create two 'Person' objects. 'p2 = p1; p1.age = 30;'. What is 'p2.age'?"
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge9","Create a 'Person' class with a 'String name'. 'p2 = p1; p1.name = ""New"";'. What is 'p2.name'?"
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge10","Is '""abc"" == new String(""abc"").intern()' true or false? Explain."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge11","Create a 2D array of 'StringBuilder'. Modify an element at '[0][0]'. Does any other element see this change?"
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge12","Given 'Integer a = 10; Integer b = a; b++;'. What are the final values of 'a' and 'b'? Explain."
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge13","Given 'StringBuilder a = new StringBuilder(""A""); StringBuilder b = a; b.append(""B"");'. What are the final values of 'a' and 'b'?"
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge14","Write a method that takes an 'Object' parameter. Pass an 'int' to it. What process makes this possible?"
"Primitives vs References","ComplexChallenge15","Create a 'final ArrayList<String>'. Show that you can still add and remove elements from it."
"Iterator",Iterating a List,"Create an 'ArrayList' of strings. Get an 'Iterator' from the list and use a 'while' loop with 'hasNext()' and 'next()' to print all elements."
"Iterator",Removing Elements with Iterator,"Using an 'Iterator', loop through a list of integers and remove all the even numbers."
"Iterator",ConcurrentModificationException,"Try to remove an element from a list using the list's 'remove()' method while iterating over it with a for-each loop. Observe the 'ConcurrentModificationException'."
"Iterator",Iterating a Set,"Create a 'HashSet' and use an 'Iterator' to traverse its elements (noting that the order is not guaranteed)."
"Iterator",Iterating a Map's Keys,"Get the key set from a 'HashMap' ('keySet()'), and then use an 'Iterator' to loop through all the keys."
"Iterator",Iterating a Map's Values,"Get the collection of values from a 'HashMap' ('values()'), and then use an 'Iterator' to loop through all the values."
"Iterator",Iterating a Map's Entries,"Get the entry set from a 'HashMap' ('entrySet()'), and use an 'Iterator' to loop through the 'Map.Entry' objects, giving you access to both key and value in each iteration."
"Iterator",For-Each Loop as Syntactic Sugar,"Rewrite an iterator-based loop using a for-each loop to show that the for-each loop is just a simpler syntax for using an 'Iterator'."
"Iterator",ListIterator,"Use a 'ListIterator' on an 'ArrayList' to traverse the list both forwards and backwards."
"Iterator",Adding with ListIterator,"Use a 'ListIterator' to add a new element to the list at the iterator's current position."
"Iterator",Custom Iterable Class,"Create your own class that implements the 'Iterable' interface. This requires you to provide an 'iterator()' method that returns an instance of a custom 'Iterator'."
"Iterator",Iterator vs. For Loop,"Discuss a scenario where using an 'Iterator' is necessary (e.g. removing elements during iteration), as opposed to a simple indexed for loop."
"Iterator","GetAnIterator","Create an ArrayList of Strings and get an Iterator from it using the '.iterator()' method."
"Iterator","BasicIteration","Use a 'while' loop with 'hasNext()' and 'next()' to iterate through the ArrayList and print each element."
"Iterator","IteratorVsForEach","Re-write the previous exercise using an enhanced for-each loop. Explain in a comment how the for-each loop uses an Iterator behind the scenes."
"Iterator","IterateOverHashSet","Create a HashSet, add some elements, and use an Iterator to print them. Note the lack of guaranteed order."
"Iterator","SafeRemoval","Create a list of integers. Use an Iterator to loop through the list and safely remove all numbers greater than 10 using 'iterator.remove()'."
"Iterator","ConcurrentModificationException","Try to remove an element from a list using the list's own '.remove()' method inside a for-each loop to trigger a 'ConcurrentModificationException'."
"Iterator","ExplainConcurrentModification","In a comment, explain what a 'ConcurrentModificationException' is and why the code in the previous exercise caused it."
"Iterator","IllegalStateExceptionRemove","Write code that calls 'iterator.remove()' before calling 'iterator.next()' to trigger an 'IllegalStateException'."
"Iterator","IllegalStateExceptionRemoveTwice","Call 'iterator.remove()' twice in a row after a single 'next()' call to trigger an 'IllegalStateException'."
"Iterator","NoSuchElementException","On a small list, use a loop to call 'next()' one more time after 'hasNext()' has returned false to trigger a 'NoSuchElementException'."
"Iterator","IteratorOnEmptyList","Get an Iterator from an empty list. What is the initial value of 'hasNext()'?"
"Iterator","UnsupportedOperation","Create a read-only list using 'List.of()'. Try to call 'iterator.remove()' on its iterator and observe the 'UnsupportedOperationException'."
"Iterator","IterateMapKeys","Create a HashMap and use an Iterator to loop through its key set ('keySet().iterator()')."
"Iterator","IterateMapValues","Use an Iterator to loop through the HashMap's collection of values ('values().iterator()')."
"Iterator","IterateMapEntries","Use an Iterator to loop through the HashMap's entry set ('entrySet().iterator()') and print both the key and value for each entry."
"Iterator","ModifyMapValuesDuringIteration","While iterating over the entry set of a map, use 'entry.setValue()' to modify the map's values in place."
"Iterator","ForEachRemaining","Use the 'forEachRemaining()' method on an iterator to process all subsequent elements with a lambda expression."
"Iterator","IteratorOnQueue","Create a LinkedList (which is also a Queue) and use its iterator to inspect elements without removing them."
"ListIterator","GetListIterator","Get a 'ListIterator' from an ArrayList of characters."
"ListIterator","IterateBackwards","Use the 'hasPrevious()' and 'previous()' methods of a ListIterator to traverse a list from end to start."
"ListIterator","StartFromIndex","Get a ListIterator that starts at a specific index (e.g. the middle) of a list."
"ListIterator","GetNextIndex","While iterating forward, print the results of both 'next()' and 'nextIndex()' in each step."
"ListIterator","GetPreviousIndex","While iterating backward, print the results of both 'previous()' and 'previousIndex()'."
"ListIterator","ModifyWithSet","Use 'listIterator.set()' to replace the last element returned by 'next()' or 'previous()'."
"ListIterator","AddWithListIterator","Use 'listIterator.add()' to insert a new element into the list at the iterator's current position."
"ListIterator","IllegalStateSet","Call 'listIterator.set()' before calling 'next()' or 'previous()' to trigger an 'IllegalStateException'."
"ListIterator","PalindromeCheck","Use a ListIterator to iterate from the start and another to iterate from the end to check if a list is a palindrome."
"ListIterator","ForwardThenBackward","Iterate all the way to the end of a list with a ListIterator, and then immediately iterate all the way back to the beginning."
"Iterable Interface","ImplementIterable","Create a custom 'BookShelf' class that holds an array of 'Book' objects and implements the 'Iterable<Book>' interface."
"Iterable Interface","CustomIterator","Implement the 'iterator()' method in your 'BookShelf' class to return a custom Iterator for the books."
"Iterable Interface","UseForEachOnCustomClass","Demonstrate that your 'BookShelf' class now works with an enhanced for-each loop."
"Complex Challenges","FailFastIterator","Demonstrate the fail-fast nature of an ArrayList's iterator by modifying the list from another thread during iteration."
"Complex Challenges","FailSafeIterator","Use a 'CopyOnWriteArrayList' to demonstrate a fail-safe iterator that does not throw a ConcurrentModificationException."
"Complex Challenges","NestedIteration","Iterate through a list of lists (a 2D list) using nested iterators."
"Complex Challenges","FilteringIterator","Create a method that takes an 'Iterator<String>' and returns a new 'List<String>' containing only the strings that have more than 5 characters."
"Complex Challenges","ReadOnlyIterator","Create a wrapper class for an Iterator that throws an 'UnsupportedOperationException' when 'remove()' is called."
"Complex Challenges","IteratorVsEnumeration","Find a legacy class like 'Vector' and get an 'Enumeration' from it. Compare its methods ('hasMoreElements', 'nextElement') to Iterator."
"Complex Challenges","PeekingIteratorConcept","(Theory) Explain what a 'Peeking Iterator' is. Write a simple wrapper class that adds a 'peek()' method to a standard iterator."
"Complex Challenges","ChainingIterators","Write a class that takes two Iterators and combines them into a single Iterator sequence."
"Complex Challenges","IteratorOnGeneratedData","Create an iterator that doesn't use a backing collection but generates the Fibonacci sequence up to a certain limit."
"Complex Challenges","SpliteratorIntro","Get a 'Spliterator' from an ArrayList and demonstrate the 'tryAdvance()' method."
"Complex Challenges","SpliteratorSplit","Demonstrate the 'trySplit()' method of a Spliterator to process parts of the collection in parallel (conceptually)."
"Interfaces: Basics","DefineAnInterface","Define an interface named 'Playable' with a single abstract method, 'play()'."
"Interfaces: Basics","ImplementAnInterface","Create a 'Guitar' class and a 'Piano' class that both implement the 'Playable' interface."
"Interfaces: Basics","ProvideImplementation","Implement the 'play()' method in both the 'Guitar' and 'Piano' classes to print a specific message."
"Interfaces: Basics","PolymorphismWithInterfaces","Create objects of 'Guitar' and 'Piano' but store them in variables of type 'Playable'."
"Interfaces: Basics","InterfaceInCollections","Create a 'List<Playable>' and add instances of 'Guitar' and 'Piano' to it. Iterate and call the 'play()' method on each."
"Interfaces: Basics","InterfaceAsParameter","Create a method that accepts a 'Playable' object as a parameter and calls its 'play()' method."
"Interfaces: Basics","InterfaceConstants","Add a constant (e.g. 'int MAX_VOLUME = 100;') to your 'Playable' interface. Access it from an implementing class."
"Interfaces: Multiple Interfaces","ImplementMultipleInterfaces","Define a second interface 'Recordable'. Have a 'DigitalPiano' class implement both 'Playable' and 'Recordable'."
"Interfaces: Multiple Interfaces","InterfaceInheritance","Create a 'Tunable' interface that extends the 'Playable' interface, adding a new 'tune()' method."
"Interfaces: Multiple Interfaces","ImplementingSubInterface","Have the 'Guitar' class implement the new 'Tunable' interface."
"Interfaces: Default Methods","DefineDefaultMethod","Add a 'default' method named 'stop()' to the 'Playable' interface that prints a generic ""Stopping..."" message."
"Interfaces: Default Methods","UseDefaultMethod","Call the 'stop()' method on a 'Piano' object without providing an implementation for it in the class."
"Interfaces: Default Methods","OverrideDefaultMethod","Override the 'stop()' default method in the 'Guitar' class to provide a custom message."
"Interfaces: Static Methods","DefineStaticMethod","Add a 'static' method to the 'Playable' interface named 'getLibraryInfo()' that returns a descriptive String."
"Interfaces: Static Methods","CallStaticMethod","Call the 'getLibraryInfo()' method directly on the 'Playable' interface, not on an instance of a class."
"Interfaces: Abstract Classes","AbstractClassVsInterface","In a comment, list three key differences between an abstract class and an interface in Java."
"Interfaces: Abstract Classes","CombineAbstractAndInterface","Create an abstract 'Instrument' class that implements the 'Playable' interface but does not implement the 'play()' method, leaving it for subclasses."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","DefineFunctionalInterface","Define an interface 'Calculator' with a single abstract method 'calculate(int a, int b)'."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","ImplementWithLambda","Use a lambda expression to provide an implementation for your 'Calculator' interface to perform addition."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","The@FunctionalInterfaceAnnotation","Add the '@FunctionalInterface' annotation to your 'Calculator' interface."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","BreakTheAnnotation","Try to add a second abstract method to your 'Calculator' interface and observe the compiler error caused by the annotation."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","BuiltInFunction","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Function' functional interface to convert a String to its length."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","BuiltInPredicate","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Predicate' functional interface to test if a number is even."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","BuiltInConsumer","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Consumer' functional interface with a list's 'forEach' method to print all elements."
"Interfaces: Functional Interfaces","BuiltInSupplier","Use the built-in 'java.util.function.Supplier' functional interface to provide a new 'Date' object."
"Interfaces: Marker Interfaces","SerializableMarker","Explain in a comment what a marker interface is and name 'Serializable' as an example."
"Interfaces: Marker Interfaces","CloneableMarker","Explain the purpose of the 'Cloneable' marker interface."
"Interfaces: Marker Interfaces","CreateCustomMarker","Create your own empty marker interface named 'Loggable'."
"Interfaces: Marker Interfaces","UseCustomMarker","Write a method that checks if an object is 'instanceof Loggable' before performing a logging action."
"Interfaces: Private Methods","DefinePrivateMethod","(Java 9+) Add a 'private' method to an interface. Have a 'default' method call this private method to share code."
"Interfaces: Private Static Methods","DefinePrivateStaticMethod","(Java 9+) Add a 'private static' method to an interface. Have a 'public static' method call it."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","DiamondProblem","Create two interfaces with the same default method signature. Create a class that implements both and resolve the conflict."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","InterfaceAndClassInheritance","Create a class 'A' and an interface 'B' with the same method signature. Create a class 'C' that extends 'A' and implements 'B'. Which method is called?"
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","ComparableInterface","Create a 'Person' class and implement the 'Comparable<Person>' interface to sort people by age."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","ComparatorInterface","Create a 'Comparator<Person>' using a lambda to sort 'Person' objects by name instead of age."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","AnonymousClassImplementation","Create an instance of the 'Playable' interface on the fly using an anonymous inner class."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","InterfaceAsReturnType","Create a method that returns an object of type 'Playable', but the actual object returned is a 'Guitar'."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","GenericInterface","Create a generic interface 'Box<T>' with 'put(T item)' and 'T get()' methods."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","ImplementGenericInterface","Create a 'BookBox' class that implements 'Box<Book>'."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","InterfaceVsTypeParameter","Discuss the difference between using an interface as a raw type ('List') and with a type parameter ('List<String>')."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","SealedInterfaces","(Java 17+) Define a 'sealed' interface 'Shape' that only permits 'Circle' and 'Rectangle' to implement it."
"Interfaces: Complex Challenges","NonSealedImplementer","(Java 17+) In your sealed hierarchy, declare one of the implementing classes as 'non-sealed' to allow further extension."
The Random Class,Generate a Random Integer,"Create a program that generates and prints a single random integer using the Random class."
The Random Class,Generate a Random Double,"Write a program to generate and display a random double value between 0.0 (inclusive) and 1.0 (exclusive)."
The Random Class,Generate a Random Boolean,"Develop a program that produces and prints a random boolean value (true or false)."
The Random Class,Six-Sided Die Roll,"Simulate the rolling of a standard six-sided die. The program should output a random integer between 1 and 6."
The Random Class,Coin Flip Simulation,"Write a program that simulates a coin flip, printing either ""Heads"" or ""Tails"" based on a random boolean."
The Random Class,Number in a Custom Range,"Generate a random integer within a specific range provided by the user (e.g. between 50 and 100)."
The Random Class,Seeded Random Numbers,"Create a program that initializes the Random class with a specific seed. Generate and print 5 numbers to show that the sequence is always the same for the same seed."
The Random Class,Random Array Element,"Create an integer array with at least 10 elements. Write a program to select and print a random element from this array."
The Random Class,Fill Array with Random Numbers,"Write a program to create an integer array of size 20 and fill it with random integers between 1 and 100."
The Random Class,Lottery Number Picker,"Simulate a lottery number drawing. Generate 6 unique random integers between 1 and 49."
The Random Class,Random Password Generator,"Create a program that generates a random 8-character password consisting of random uppercase letters, lowercase letters, and digits."
The Random Class,Guess the Number Game,"Develop a simple ""Guess the Number"" game. The program generates a random number, and the user has to guess it."
The Random Class,Random RGB Color,"Generate a random RGB color. The program should produce three random integer values, each between 0 and 255, for Red, Green, and Blue."
The Random Class,Random Point in a 2D Plane,"Generate a random 2D point (x, y). Both x and y coordinates should be random integers between -100 and 100."
The Random Class,Sum of Two Dice,"Simulate rolling two six-sided dice. The program should calculate and print the sum of the two random outcomes."
The Random Class,Random Character from a String,"Given a string, write a program that selects and prints a random character from that string."
The Random Class,Shuffle a List,"Create an ArrayList of strings. Write a program to shuffle the elements of the list into a random order."
The Random Class,Random Walk Simulation,"Simulate a 1D random walk. Start at position 0. In each step, randomly move one step to the left (-1) or one step to the right (+1). Run the simulation for 100 steps and print the final position."
The Random Class,Random Gaussian (Normal) Distribution,"Use the `nextGaussian()` method to generate 10 random numbers that follow a standard normal distribution. Print each number."
The Random Class,Random Wait Time,"Simulate a process that has a random wait time. Generate a random integer between 1000 and 5000 to represent milliseconds and use it with `Thread.sleep()`."
The Random Class,Card Deck Simulator,"Create a program that randomly draws a card from a standard 52-card deck. The output should be the rank and suit (e.g. ""King of Spades"")."
The Random Class,Random Sentence Generator,"Create three arrays of words (e.g. subjects, verbs, objects). Generate a simple sentence by randomly picking one word from each array."
The Random Class,Monte Carlo Pi Estimation,"Estimate the value of Pi using a Monte Carlo method. Generate random points in a 2x2 square and check how many fall inside a circle of radius 1 centered at the origin."
The Random Class,Random True/False Quiz,"Generate a simple 5-question quiz where the answer to each question is randomly determined to be true or false. Display the questions and their random answers."
The Random Class,Random Byte Array,"Create a byte array of size 16. Use the `nextBytes()` method to fill the array with random bytes and then print the array's contents."
The Random Class,Compare Seeded vs. Unseeded,"Create two Random objects, one with a seed and one without. Generate 5 numbers from each and print them side-by-side to show the difference."
The Random Class,Probability Simulation,"Simulate an event with a 30% chance of success. Run the simulation 1000 times and count how many times the event was successful. The result should be close to 300."
The Random Class,Random Student Selector,"Create a list of student names. Write a program that randomly selects a student from the list to answer a question."
The Random Class,Simple Maze Generator,"Represent a 10x10 grid. Randomly place 'W' (wall) or 'P' (path) in each cell of the grid to generate a simple, random maze pattern."
The Random Class,Rock, Paper, Scissors Game,"Write a program where the user plays Rock, Paper, Scissors against the computer. The computer's choice should be randomly generated."
The Random Class,Random Floating-Point Number in a Range,"Generate a random floating-point number (double) in a custom range, for example, between 10.5 and 20.5."
The Random Class,Random Element from Enum,"Define an enumeration (enum) of at least four constants (e.g. seasons). Write a program to randomly select and print one of the enum constants."
The Math Class,Find Absolute Value,"Write a program that takes a negative integer as input and prints its absolute value using `Math.abs()`."
The Math Class,Calculate Square Root,"Create a program that calculates and prints the square root of a user-provided number using `Math.sqrt()`."
The Math Class,Power of a Number,"Develop a program that computes `x` raised to the power of `y` (x^y), where `x` and `y` are inputs, using `Math.pow()`."
The Math Class,Find the Maximum of Two Numbers,"Write a program that finds and displays the larger of two given integers using `Math.max()`."
The Math Class,Find the Minimum of Two Numbers,"Create a program to determine and print the smaller of two double values using `Math.min()`."
The Math Class,Ceiling of a Number,"Write a program that takes a decimal number and rounds it up to the nearest integer using `Math.ceil()`."
The Math Class,Floor of a Number,"Develop a program that takes a decimal number and rounds it down to the nearest integer using `Math.floor()`."
The Math Class,Round a Number,"Create a program that rounds a floating-point number to the nearest whole number using `Math.round()`."
The Math Class,Area of a Circle,"Write a program to calculate the area of a circle given its radius, using the `Math.PI` constant."
The Math Class,Circumference of a Circle,"Develop a program to calculate the circumference of a circle using the radius and the `Math.PI` constant."
The Math Class,Hypotenuse of a Right Triangle,"Given the lengths of two sides of a right triangle, calculate the hypotenuse using `Math.hypot()`."
The Math Class,Sine of an Angle,"Write a program that calculates the sine of an angle given in radians using `Math.sin()`."
The Math Class,Cosine of an Angle,"Create a program to compute the cosine of an angle given in radians using `Math.cos()`."
The Math Class,Tangent of an Angle,"Develop a program that finds the tangent of an angle given in radians using `Math.tan()`."
The Math Class,Radians to Degrees,"Write a program that converts an angle from radians to degrees using `Math.toDegrees()`."
The Math Class,Degrees to Radians,"Create a program to convert an angle from degrees to radians using `Math.toRadians()`."
The Math Class,Natural Logarithm,"Write a program that calculates the natural logarithm (base e) of a number using `Math.log()`."
The Math Class,Base 10 Logarithm,"Develop a program to compute the base 10 logarithm of a number using `Math.log10()`."
The Math Class,Euler's Number Raised to a Power,"Create a program that calculates e raised to the power of a given number using `Math.exp()`."
The Math Class,Generate a Random Number,"Write a program to generate and print a random double between 0.0 and 1.0 using `Math.random()`."
The Math Class,Distance Formula,"Calculate the distance between two points (x1, y1) and (x2, y2) in a 2D plane using the distance formula."
The Math Class,Cube Root of a Number,"Write a program that finds the cube root of a number using `Math.cbrt()`."
The Math Class,Signum Function,"Create a program that determines the sign of a number (-1, 0, or 1) using `Math.signum()`."
The Math Class,Volume of a Sphere,"Calculate the volume of a sphere given its radius, using `Math.PI` and `Math.pow()`."
The Math Class,Quadratic Formula Solver,"Write a program that finds the roots of a quadratic equation (ax^2 + bx + c = 0) using the quadratic formula."
The Math Class,Factorial Calculation,"Develop a program to calculate the factorial of a number. (Note: This requires a loop, not a direct Math class method, but is a common mathematical exercise)."
The Math Class,Copying a Sign,"Use `Math.copySign()` to create a new number that has the magnitude of a number `x` and the sign of a number `y`."
The Math Class,Next Floating-Point Value,"Given a double, find the next floating-point number in the direction of positive infinity using `Math.nextUp()`."
The Math Class,Integer Part of a Logarithm,"Find the integer part of the base-2 logarithm of a number, which can be used to find the highest power of 2 less than the number."
The Math Class,Law of Cosines,"Implement the Law of Cosines to find the third side of a triangle given two sides and the angle between them."
The Math Class,Simple Harmonic Motion,"Simulate a point's position in simple harmonic motion using `Math.cos()` over a series of time steps."
The Math Class,Rounding to Two Decimal Places,"Write a program that takes a double and rounds it to two decimal places. This requires combining multiplication, `Math.round()`, and division."
Generating Random Integers,Basic Range [0 to n-1],"Using `Random.nextInt(n)`, write a program to generate a random integer between 0 (inclusive) and a user-defined upper bound `n` (exclusive)."
Generating Random Integers,Classic Die Roll [1 to 6],"Simulate rolling a standard six-sided die by generating a random integer in the inclusive range of 1 to 6."
Generating Random Integers,Custom Inclusive Range [min to max],"Write a program that generates a random integer within a specific inclusive range [min, max], where `min` and `max` are provided by the user."
Generating Random Integers,Using Math.random(),"Generate a random integer between 1 and 100 (inclusive) using `Math.random()` and casting."
Generating Random Integers,20-Sided Die,"Simulate the roll of a 20-sided die (D20) by generating a random integer from 1 to 20."
Generating Random Integers,Lottery Number Picker,"Generate a single random lottery ball number, which must be an integer between 1 and 49, inclusive."
Generating Random Integers,Temperature Fluctuation,"Simulate a daily temperature reading in Celsius by generating a random integer between -10 and 35."
Generating Random Integers,Array Index Generator,"Create an array of 10 strings. Generate a random valid index for this array and print the element at that index."
Generating Random Integers,Random Even Number,"Write a program to generate a random even integer between 1 and 100."
Generating Random Integers,Random Odd Number,"Develop a program to generate a random odd integer between 1 and 100."
Generating Random Integers,Range with Negative Numbers,"Generate a random integer in a range that includes negative numbers, for example, from -50 to 50."
Generating Random Integers,Using ThreadLocalRandom,"Use `ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextInt(min, max)` to generate a random integer in a user-defined range. Note this method's upper bound is exclusive."
Generating Random Integers,Fill Array with Ranged Numbers,"Create an integer array of size 50 and fill it with random integers, each between 100 and 200."
Generating Random Integers,Guess the Number [1-100],"Create a number guessing game where the computer picks a random integer between 1 and 100 and the user has to guess it."
Generating Random Integers,Random Grade Generator,"Simulate a student's test score by generating a random integer percentage from 0 to 100."
Generating Random Integers,Two Dice Sum,"Simulate rolling two six-sided dice. Generate two random numbers from 1 to 6 and print their sum."
Generating Random Integers,Random Month,"Generate a random integer from 1 to 12 to represent a random month of the year."
Generating Random Integers,Random Day in a Month,"Generate a random integer from 1 to 31 to represent a random day (ignoring specific month lengths for simplicity)."
Generating Random Integers,Random Uppercase Letter,"Generate a random integer that corresponds to the ASCII value of an uppercase letter ('A' to 'Z') and then cast it to a char."
Generating Random Integers,Random Digit Character,"Generate a random integer that corresponds to the ASCII value of a digit ('0' to '9') and then cast it to a char."
Generating Random Integers,Excluding a Number,"Generate a random integer between 1 and 10, but ensure the number is never 5."
Generating Random Integers,Multiple of 5,"Write a program to generate a random integer between 1 and 100 that is a multiple of 5."
Generating Random Integers,Age Simulator,"Generate a random integer to represent a person's age, from 1 to 99."
Generating Random Integers,Floor Level in a Building,"Simulate an elevator stopping at a random floor in a 40-story building (floors 1-40)."
Generating Random Integers,Range from Zero,"Write a function that takes a single positive integer `max` and returns a random integer between 0 and `max` (inclusive)."
Generating Random Integers,Card Value,"Generate a random integer from 2 to 10 to simulate drawing a numbered card (excluding face cards) from a deck."
Generating Random Integers,Small Negative Range,"Generate a random integer in a small, entirely negative range, such as -20 to -10."
Generating Random Integers,Random Game Level Selector,"A game has 25 levels. Write a program to select a random level for the player to start on, from 1 to 25."
Generating Random Integers,Limited Choices,"Generate a random integer that can only be 1, 2, or 3, representing a choice from three options."
Generating Random Integers,Password PIN Code,"Generate a random 4-digit PIN code by generating a random integer between 1000 and 9999."
Generating Random Integers,Range Defined by Variables,"Write a program where the min and max of the range are stored in variables, emphasizing the dynamic nature of the range."
Generating Random Integers,Java 8 IntStream,"Use `new Random().ints(1, min, max).findFirst().getAsInt()` to generate a single random integer in an inclusive range [min, max-1]."
Inheritance,Simple Base and Derived Class,"Create a base class `Animal` with a method `eat()`. Create a derived class `Dog` that inherits from `Animal` and calls the `eat()` method."
Inheritance,Accessing Parent Class Members,"Create a `Vehicle` class with a `speed` field. Create a `Car` subclass that sets and gets the `speed` field from the `Vehicle` class."
Inheritance,Method Overriding,"Define a class `Shape` with a method `draw()`. Create a subclass `Circle` that overrides the `draw()` method to print ""Drawing a Circle""."
Inheritance,Using the `super` Keyword with Methods,"Create a `Person` class with a `display()` method. A subclass `Employee` should override `display()` but also call the parent's `display()` method using `super`."
Inheritance,Using the `super` Keyword with Constructors,"Create a `Machine` class with a constructor that accepts a name. The `Computer` subclass constructor should call the parent constructor using `super()`."
Inheritance,Hierarchical Inheritance,"Create a base class `Figure`. Create two subclasses, `Rectangle` and `Triangle`, that both inherit from `Figure`."
Inheritance,Multilevel Inheritance,"Create a class `Animal`. Create a subclass `Mammal` that inherits from `Animal`. Create a subclass `Dog` that inherits from `Mammal`."
Inheritance,Protected Members,"Define a class `BankAccount` with a `protected double balance`. Create a subclass `SavingsAccount` that can directly access and modify the `balance`."
Inheritance,Constructor Chaining,"Create a three-level inheritance hierarchy (e.g. A -> B -> C). Place a print statement in each constructor to show the order of execution when a `C` object is created."
Inheritance,Polymorphism in Action,"Create a `Shape` reference variable. Assign a `new Circle()` object to it and call the `draw()` method to demonstrate polymorphism."
Inheritance,Polymorphic Arrays,"Create an array of type `Shape`. Store objects of `Circle`, `Rectangle`, and `Triangle` in it and loop through to call their overridden `draw()` methods."
Inheritance,The `instanceof` Operator,"In your polymorphic array loop, use the `instanceof` operator to check if an object is a `Circle` before calling a Circle-specific method."
Inheritance,Abstract Class,"Create an `abstract` class `Shape` with an `abstract` method `getArea()`. Explain why you cannot create an instance of `Shape`."
Inheritance,Implementing Abstract Methods,"Create `Circle` and `Rectangle` subclasses that extend `Shape`. They must provide a concrete implementation for the `getArea()` method."
Inheritance,Abstract Class with Concrete Methods,"Add a concrete method `getName()` to your abstract `Shape` class that returns the name of the shape. Show that subclasses can use this method."
Inheritance,Final Methods,"Create a method `calculateTaxes()` in a class `Government`. Mark it as `final` and try to override it in a subclass to see the compiler error."
Inheritance,Final Classes,"Create a `final` class `StringUtil`. Attempt to create a subclass that extends `StringUtil` to see the compiler error."
Inheritance,Object Casting,"Create a `Shape` object that is actually a `Circle`. Use `instanceof` to check its type and then downcast it to a `Circle` reference to access Circle-specific methods."
Inheritance,Employee Hierarchy,"Model an employee system with a base class `Employee` and subclasses `Manager` and `Developer`, each with their own salary calculation logic."
Inheritance,Vehicle Hierarchy,"Create a `Vehicle` base class. Create subclasses like `Car`, `Motorcycle`, and `Truck`, each overriding a `getFuelType()` method."
Inheritance,Bank Account System,"Design an `Account` base class. Create `SavingsAccount` and `CheckingAccount` subclasses with different rules for deposits and withdrawals."
Inheritance,Overriding the `toString()` Method,"Create a `Book` class with fields for title and author. Override the `toString()` method from the `Object` class to return a formatted string."
Inheritance,Inheritance and Interfaces,"Create a class `Bird` that extends `Animal` and also implements a `Flyable` interface with a `fly()` method."
Inheritance,Single Responsibility Principle,"Create a `Worker` class with a `work()` method. Create subclasses `HumanWorker` and `RobotWorker` to show how inheritance supports different implementations."
Inheritance,Parent Reference, Child Object,"Create a `Parent` reference pointing to a `Child` object. Try to call a method that exists only in the `Child` class and explain the result."
Inheritance,Zoo Animal Hierarchy,"Design a hierarchy for zoo animals. Start with `Animal`, then `Bird`, `Mammal`, `Reptile`. Add specific animals like `Penguin` and `Lion` with unique properties."
Inheritance,Digital Media Library,"Create a base class `MediaItem` (with title, year). Create subclasses `Book` (with author) and `Movie` (with director)."
Inheritance,`super` vs. `this` in Constructors,"Create a class with multiple constructors. In a subclass constructor, demonstrate calling both a `super()` constructor and a `this()` constructor (and explain the rules)."
Inheritance,Implicit `Object` Superclass,"Create a simple `Person` class. Without extending anything explicitly, create an instance and call methods like `hashCode()` and `getClass()` to show it inherits from `Object`."
Inheritance,IS-A Relationship,"Write a program with `Car` and `Engine` classes. Explain why a Car IS-A Vehicle (inheritance) but a Car HAS-A Engine (composition)."
Inheritance,Covariant Return Types,"Override a method in a subclass where the return type is a subtype of the parent method's return type."
Inheritance,Combining `abstract` and `final`,"Attempt to declare a method as both `abstract` and `final`. Explain the compiler error and why these concepts are mutually exclusive."
My First Java Program,Hello World,"Write a complete Java program that prints the text ""Hello, World!"" to the console."
My First Java Program,Print Your Name,"Create a program that prints your full name to the console."
My First Java Program,Print a Number,"Write a program that prints your favorite number to the console."
My First Java Program,Multiple Print Statements,"Use multiple `System.out.println()` statements to print your name, city, and state on separate lines."
My First Java Program,Using `System.out.print`,"Write a program that uses `System.out.print()` twice to print ""Hello"" and ""Java"" on the same line."
My First Java Program,Single Line Comment,"Write a ""Hello, World!"" program and add a single-line comment explaining what the program does."
My First Java Program,Multi-line Comment,"Create a program that prints a number, and use a multi-line comment to write a short story about that number."
My First Java Program,Simple ASCII Art,"Use several `System.out.println()` statements to print a simple ASCII art smiley face to the console."
My First Java Program,Declare an Integer,"Declare an integer variable named `age`, assign it your age, and print it to the console."
My First Java Program,Declare a String,"Declare a String variable named `favoriteFood`, assign it your favorite food, and print it."
My First Java Program,Declare a Double,"Declare a double variable named `price`, assign it a value like 19.99, and print it."
My First Java Program,Declare a Boolean,"Declare a boolean variable named `isJavaFun`, assign it the value `true`, and print it."
My First Java Program,Simple Addition,"Create two integer variables, add them together, and print the result."
My First Java Program,Simple Subtraction,"Create two integer variables, subtract the second from the first, and print the result."
My First Java Program,Simple Multiplication,"Create two double variables, multiply them, and print the result."
My First Java Program,Simple Division,"Create two double variables, divide the first by the second, and print the result."
My First Java Program,String Concatenation,"Create two String variables (e.g. first name, last name) and combine them into a single string to print."
My First Java Program,Concatenating Strings and Numbers,"Create a String and an integer variable. Print a sentence that combines them, like ""My age is: 25""."
My First Java Program,Fix a Syntax Error (Missing Semicolon),"Copy a simple print statement but forget the semicolon at the end. Observe the compiler error and then fix it."
My First Java Program,Fix a Syntax Error (Mismatched Quotes),"Try to print a string with a missing closing quote. Observe the error and then fix it."
My First Java Program,Fix a Syntax Error (Case Sensitivity),"Try to print using `system.out.println()` (lowercase 's'). Observe the error and fix it to `System.out.println()`."
My First Java Program,The Newline Character,"Use the `\n` escape sequence inside a single `System.out.println()` to print two lines of text."
My First Java Program,The Tab Character,"Use the `\t` escape sequence to print a list of items with a tab space between them."
My First Java Program,Printing Quotes,"Write a program that prints a famous quote, including the double quotation marks, to the console."
My First Java Program,Basic Variable Reassignment,"Declare an integer variable, assign it a value, print it, then assign it a new value and print it again."
My First Java Program,Simple Calculation with Text,"Calculate the sum of two numbers and print the result in a full sentence, like ""The sum of 5 and 10 is 15.""."
My First Java Program,Area of a Rectangle,"Create two integer variables for the length and width of a rectangle. Calculate and print its area."
My First Java Program,Perimeter of a Square,"Create one integer variable for the side of a square. Calculate and print its perimeter."
My First Java Program,Class and Main Method Structure,"Write out the basic structure of a Java program (`public class ... { public static void main(String[] args) { ... } }`) and print ""Ready to code!"" inside."
My First Java Program,Integer Division,"Divide 9 by 4 using integer variables and print the result. Note how the decimal part is truncated."
My First Java Program,Floating-Point Division,"Divide 9.0 by 4.0 using double variables and print the result to see the difference from integer division."
My First Java Program,Printing a Blank Line,"Write a program that prints a line of text, then a blank line, then another line of text."
Java Application and Class Basics,Create an Empty Class,"Write the full code for a Java class named `Car` that has no fields or methods inside it."
Java Application and Class Basics,Create a Basic Application,"Write a complete, runnable Java application with a `main` method that does nothing."
