Java Application and Class Basics,The `void` Keyword in `main`,"What does the `void` keyword in the `main` method signature indicate?"
Java Application and Class Basics,The `String[] args` Parameter,"What is the purpose of the `String[] args` parameter in the `main` method?"
Java Application and Class Basics,A Simple Model,"Create a class to represent a `Song`, with fields for `title` (String) and `durationInSeconds` (int)."
Java Application and Class Basics,An Action Class,"Create a class named `Printer` with a method `printDocument()` that prints ""Printing...""."
Java Application and Class Basics,Combining Fields and Methods,"Create a `BankAccount` class with a `double balance` field and a `showBalance()` method."
Java Application and Class Basics,Spot the Class,"In a full `.java` file, draw a box around the code that represents the class definition."
Java Application and- Class Basics,Spot the Method,"In a class with a `main` method, draw a box around the code that represents the method definition."
Java Application and Class Basics,Spot the Field,"In a class with a variable declaration, draw a box around the code that represents the field."
Java Application and Class Basics,Public vs. Private (Conceptual),"What does the `public` keyword before `class` usually signify about the class's accessibility?"
Java Application and Class Basics,A Class is Not an Object,"In a comment, explain the difference between a class (`Car`) and an object (your specific car)."
Java Application and Class Basics,Multiple Classes in One File,"Can you have two `public` classes in a single `.java` file? Explain your answer."
Java Application and Class Basics,Minimal Runnable Code,"Write the absolute minimum amount of code required to make a runnable Java application."
Java Application and Class Basics,Comment the `main` Method,"Write a `main` method and add a single-line comment above it explaining its purpose."
Keywords,The `class` Keyword,"Write the code to declare a public class named `Computer`. This is the fundamental use of the `class` keyword."
Keywords,The `public` Keyword,"Create a `public` method inside a class. In a comment, explain what `public` means for this method."
