Math.random(),Monte Carlo Pi (Single Point),"Generate one random point (x, y) between 0 and 1 and check if it falls within a circle of radius 1."
Math.random(),Random Wait Time,"Generate a random integer between 500 and 2000 to simulate a random wait time in milliseconds."
Math.random(),Random Test Score,"Generate a random integer between 0 and 100 to simulate a student's test score."
Math.random(),Random Angle in Degrees,"Generate a random integer between 0 and 360 to represent an angle."
Math.random(),Random Angle in Radians,"Generate a random double between 0.0 and 2 * Math.PI to represent an angle in radians."
Math.random(),Random Choice from Three Options,"Simulate a choice between three options (A, B, C) by generating a random number."
Math.random(),Generate a Random Multiple of 10,"Generate a random integer between 1 and 100 that is a multiple of 10 (10, 20, 30...)."
Math.random(),Random Brightness Level,"Generate a random double between 0.0 and 1.0 to represent a brightness or opacity level."
Math.random(),Simulate a Biased Coin (70% Heads),"Generate a random number to simulate a biased coin that lands on ""Heads"" 70% of the time."
Math.random(),Random Day of the Month,"Generate a random integer between 1 and 31 to represent a day of the month."
Math.random(),Random Month of the Year,"Generate a random integer between 1 and 12 to represent a month."
Math.random(),Compare with `java.util.Random`,"Create a `Random` object and call `nextInt()`. In a comment, explain a key difference from using `Math.random()`."
Math.random(),Random 2D Coordinate,"Generate two random integers, `x` and `y`, both between -100 and 100, to represent a 2D coordinate."
Math.random(),Random Character from a String,"Given a string, use `Math.random()` to generate an index and print the character at that position."
Math.random(),Scaling the Output,"Generate a random double, multiply it by 1000, and print the result to demonstrate scaling."
Math.random(),Casting to an Integer,"Generate a random double, multiply it by 10, and cast the result to an `int` to see the truncation."
Java Practice One,Hello World,"Write a complete, runnable Java application that prints ""Hello, Java!"" to the console."
Java Practice One,Command-Line Compile and Run,"Save a simple Java program, compile it using `javac` from the command line, and run it using `java`."
Java Practice One,Declare and Initialize Integer,"Declare an integer variable named `studentCount`, initialize it to 250, and print it."
Java Practice One,Declare and Initialize String,"Declare a String variable named `appName`, initialize it to ""Code Tester"", and print it."
Java Practice One,Simple Arithmetic,"Add two integers (e.g. 135 + 246) and print the result in a descriptive sentence."
Java Practice One,Using `System.out.println`,"Use two separate `System.out.println()` statements to print your first name and last name on two separate lines."
Java Practice One,The `public` and `class` Keywords,"Create an empty class named `MyFirstTest`. Identify the two keywords on that line."
Java Practice One,Floating-Point Division,"Divide 10.0 by 3.0 using `double` variables and print the result."
Java Practice One,Integer Division,"Divide 10 by 3 using `int` variables and print the result. Note the difference from floating-point division."
Java Practice One,The Modulo Operator,"Calculate the remainder of 25 divided by 4 and print the result."
Java Practice One,Square Root,"Use `Math.sqrt()` to calculate the square root of 81 and print it."
Java Practice One,Power of a Number,"Use `Math.pow()` to calculate 2 raised to the power of 8 and print the result."
Java Practice One,Roll a Die,"Use `Math.random()` to generate a random integer between 1 and 6."
Java Practice One,Custom Range,"Generate a random integer between 20 and 40 (inclusive)."
Java Practice One,Simple `if` Statement,"Write an `if` statement that prints ""Access Granted"" if a boolean variable `isLoggedIn` is `true`."
Java Practice One,`if-else` Statement,"Check if a number is even or odd and print the appropriate message using an `if-else` block."
Java Practice One,Relational Operators,"Use the `>` operator to check if 100 is greater than 50 and print the resulting boolean value."
Java Practice One,Equality Operator,"Use the `==` operator to check if two string literals are equal. Explain the potential pitfalls in a comment."
Java Practice One,Comments,"Write a program that calculates an area, and use both single-line and multi-line comments to explain the code."
Java Practice One,The `final` Keyword,"Declare a `final` integer constant for the number of days in a week and try to change its value."
Java Practice One,`for` Loop,"Write a `for` loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10."
Java Practice One,`while` Loop,"Write a `while` loop that prints the numbers from 10 down to 1."
Java Practice One,String Concatenation,"Create two string variables and concatenate them with a space in between to form a full name."
Java Practice One,Create a Simple Class,"Define a class named `Dog` with a single String field called `breed`."
Java Practice One,Create an Object,"In your `main` method, create an instance (object) of the `Dog` class using the `new` keyword."
Java Practice One,Accessing Fields,"Set the `breed` of your `Dog` object to ""Labrador"" and then print it."
Java Practice One,Define a Simple Method,"In the `Dog` class, create a `void` method named `bark()` that prints ""Woof!"". "
Java Practice One,Calling a Method,"From your `main` method, call the `bark()` method on your `Dog` object."
Java Practice One,Method with Parameters,"Create a method `add(int a, int b)` that prints the sum of the two numbers."
Java Practice One,Method with Return Value,"Create a method `multiply(int a, int b)` that uses the `return` keyword to send back the product."
Java Practice One,Simple Inheritance,"Create a class `Animal` and a class `Cat` that `extends` `Animal`."
Java Practice One,Method Overriding,"Give the `Animal` class a method `makeSound()`. Override this method in the `Cat` class to print ""Meow""."
Java Practice One,The `super` Keyword,"In the `Cat` class, create a constructor that calls the `Animal` constructor using `super()`."
Java Practice One,Command-Line Arguments,"Write a program that prints the first command-line argument passed to it (`args[0]`)."
Java Practice One,Get a System Property,"Use `System.getProperty(""java.version"")` to print the current Java version."
Java Practice One,Measure Execution Time,"Use `System.nanoTime()` to measure how long a `for` loop takes to complete."
Java Practice One,Type Casting,"Cast a `double` value (e.g. 9.78) to an `int` and print the result to show truncation."
Java Practice One,`switch` Statement,"Write a `switch` statement that prints the name of a season based on an integer (1=Winter, 2=Spring, etc.)."
Java Practice One,The `static` Keyword,"Create a `static` method in a utility class that does not require an object instance to be called."
Java Practice One,Constructors,"Add a constructor to your `Dog` class that accepts the `breed` as a parameter and initializes the field."
Java Practice One,Increment Operator,"Use the post-increment operator (`x++`) in a print statement to see when the value updates."
Java Practice One,Logical AND,"Write an `if` statement that is true only if two conditions are met using the `&&` operator."
Java Practice One,Logical OR,"Write an `if` statement that is true if at least one of two conditions is met using the `||` operator."
Java Practice One,The `this` Keyword,"Use the `this` keyword in a constructor to differentiate between a field and a parameter of the same name."
Java Practice One,Package Declaration,"Create a directory structure for a package and add the `package` declaration to your Java file."
Java Practice One,Import Statement,"Use the `import` statement to make the `java.util.Scanner` class available in your program."
Java Practice One,Reading User Input,"Use a `Scanner` object to read an integer from the user via the console."
Java Practice One,Declare and Initialize an Array,"Declare and initialize an integer array with the first five prime numbers."
Java Practice One,Accessing Array Elements,"Print the third element (index 2) of the array you created."
Java Practice One,Looping Through an Array,"Use a `for` loop to iterate through your array and print each element."
Java Practice Two,Encapsulation (Getters and Setters),"Create a `Person` class with a private `name` field. Provide public `getName()` and `setName()` methods to access it."
Java Practice Two,The `toString()` Method,"Override the `toString()` method in your `Person` class to return a formatted string like ""Person's name: [name]""."
Java Practice Two,Constructor Overloading,"Create two constructors for the `Person` class: a default one and one that accepts a name to initialize the object."
Java Practice Two,Static vs. Instance Fields,"Add a static integer field `personCounter` to your `Person` class that increments every time a new Person object is created."
Java Practice Two,Static Methods,"Create a static method in the `Person` class that returns the value of `personCounter`."
Java Practice Two,Method Overloading,"Create two methods named `printInfo`: one that takes no arguments and one that takes a String prefix to print before the info."
Java Practice Two,Passing Objects to Methods,"Write a method that takes a `Person` object as a parameter and prints its name to the console."
Java Practice Two,Polymorphism,"Create a `Shape` class and subclasses `Circle` and `Square`. Create an array of `Shape` objects and call an overridden `draw()` method on each."
Java Practice Two,Abstract Class,"Create an `abstract` class `Vehicle` with an `abstract` method `startEngine()`. Show that you cannot create an instance of `Vehicle`."
Java Practice Two,Implementing Abstract Methods,"Create a `Car` class that extends `Vehicle` and provides a concrete implementation for the `startEngine()` method."
Java Practice Two,Interface,"Create an `interface` named `Clickable` with a single method signature: `void onClick()`."
Java Practice Two,Implementing an Interface,"Create a `Button` class that `implements` the `Clickable` interface and provides the `onClick()` method."
Java Practice Two,Nested `for` Loop,"Use a nested `for` loop to print a 5x5 grid of asterisks (`*`)."
Java Practice Two,The `do-while` Loop,"Write a `do-while` loop that asks the user for a number until they enter a positive one."
